Chheng Meng Festival is a reflection of the gratitude of the Chinese people
In fact, the activities and customs of the Cheng Meng Festival in China are not only the tombs, but also the traditional activities and activities in the new era, such as planting trees, flying kites, painting on chicken eggs and Especially after the Cheng Meng Festival, which is designated as a holiday for Chinese people to travel or have fun activities, migrants often return home to reunite with their families.
The fulfillment of gratitude is a tradition and a virtue that all of us should adhere to, regardless of race, color, or caste, especially when "God" is alive, should be obeyed and reciprocated. Clear heart. The previous generation should set an example for the next generation so that the resin blood that adheres to gratitude, which is the virtue and beautiful tradition of mankind, can be passed on to all generations.
Article by: Mr. Tang Sileng, Staff of Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, Police Chief of Post 509, Border Guard Battalion 623, Ratanakkiri Province, was arrested after cutting a young man, causing serious injuries
(Ratanakkiri): Police in O'Yadao district arrested a police officer after stabbing the victim, causing serious injuries, at 5:30 pm on April 2, 2024 in Phum Phi, Sesan commune, O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province.
O'Yadao District Police said that the victims were Sev Saroeun, 21, a Jarai farmer, and the suspect was Thy Sithi, 37, a police chief at Post 509, Phum Phi, under the 623rd Border Guard Battalion. Rattanakiri Provincial Police.
According to local authorities, before the incident, the victim was traveling from the plantation, the motorcycle ran out of gas at the scene, suddenly the police chief arrived drunk and questioned and then took a knife from The victim cut the victim back, causing head injuries.
Seeing the uncomfortable situation, the assailant fled and hid in the forest, leaving a motorcycle, a bag of cashew nuts and a knife at the scene. The perpetrator later called the post officer, who was a descendant of Hak Thearoth, to help take the materials to his place.
The suspect is currently being held at the O'Yav District Police Inspectorate for further investigation and sent to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
The Gaza Ministry of Health said in a statement that the figures included at least 62 deaths in the last 24 hours, as well as the number of casualties in Gaza due to the war. Continued to increase to 75,668 people. While the war has been going on for almost six months, the light of the end has not yet been seen.
Israel has been waging war against Hamas, which controls the Gaza Strip, since October 7, 2023, when a Palestinian militant group launched a large-scale raid on Israel and killed About 1,200 people were taken hostage and about 250 others were taken hostage. Four Poor Families Receive Homes from Climate Change Adaptation Project
(Preah Sihanouk): Four families in Prey Nup district, Preah Sihanouk province, who live in extreme hardship and have old houses that are very dilapidated due to the wind, received a model house per family from the project "Adaptation to Climate Change" by Period of small-scale infrastructure intervention in coastal residential areas of Cambodia.
Citizens who receive model homes include
He added that the project is divided into three main parts, including:
* First, the knowledge and capacity of the community is strengthened to benefit through the project investment * Second: The planning and technical capacity of sub-national officials is strengthened and knowledge is compiled and disseminated for sustainability And enhance the benefits of climate change mitigation of the project. * Third: Increase resilience through investment in small-scale infrastructure.
He emphasized that the project supported the construction of four climate change-resistant houses in Kep and four in Sihanoukville, which have now been completed.
(Siem Reap): On April 4, 2024, Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Vice President of the Mine Authority, gave a lecture on mine action in Cambodia and the journey towards hosting the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on A Mine-Free World of the 2024 Ottawa Convention to Professors, Teachers and Students of Angkor University, Siem Reap Province.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch spoke about the consequences of the war, the challenges, the importance and achievements of the mine action sector in Cambodia under the long-term vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia, in close cooperation with development partners, friendly countries and parties. Involved in ensuring health, safety and security and forming an important foundation for the development of the society.
"These achievements stem from the values of peace under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate and Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King of Cambodia, which has made it possible for Cambodia to address the threat," he said. "Because landmines and unexploded ordnance are effective and there is no fear of participating in providing security and reducing poverty in Cambodia."
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch instructed all teachers and students to continue to learn and remember the true history of Cambodia, the history of war pain and the division of Cambodian society to build a new history and Ensuring that the next generation can live in safety and escape the legacy of those wars.
Ms. O Vandin called on relevant institutions, partner organizations, authorities at all levels to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Health, especially the working group of local health officials in Ratanakkiri.
(Rattanakiri): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on April 3, 2024, chaired a meeting attended by Mrs. Nhean Tith Chenda, Deputy Governor of Rattanakiri Province, Director of Health Department, Deputy Director of Health Department, Director of Health Office of both ODs. Presidents of provincial and district referral hospitals, including presidents of 30 health centers, commune chiefs and 50 commune chiefs, seven partner organizations in Ratanakkiri province.
In addition, Ms. O Vandin advised to adhere to the position of working together with health centers to develop priority action plans and improve the quality of services in health centers for the people by implementing the promotion of primary health care. At the village-commune level, with the inclusion of this health action plan in the 3-year rolling plan of the commune / district / province as well.
Before concluding the meeting, Ms. O Vandin handed over the sample action plan, priority activities and health education documents in a USB storage device for all health centers and referral centers in Ratanakkiri to be used.
After the discussion, the results of this meeting were similar to the meeting in Stung Treng province shared on April 2, 2024.
It should be noted that during the mission from April 1 to 2, 2024, Ms. O Vandin and her team inspected Koun Mom Lumphat Banlung Health Center and Kachan Health Center.
