Mr. Nguon Rattanak said this at the meeting of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command for March 2024 on April 3, 2024.
He added that for the districts adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake, it is strictly forbidden to plow in three areas, and all district governors must report progress to the provincial administration on land development in these three areas. Regularly, he will follow this very closely.
He agreed to allow the military police to train to check for explosive weapons before the New Year, but to avoid traffic jams by targeting the gang, which must be cracked down on. .
For Sankranti New Year, all relevant authorities must be involved in detailed planning, focusing on security, technical, environmental and aesthetic protection, and this work must be prepared in advance to provide special attraction and interest. Along the national road.
The Prime Minister of Japan stated in the full letter:
I would like to congratulate Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on his appointment as President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Cambodia and Japan have built a strong friendship through cooperation for peace, reconstruction and development of Cambodia over the years.
I am pleased that the bilateral cooperation under the comprehensive strategic partnership that Samdech Techo and I have agreed to grow steadily, including not only in the economic field, but also in new areas. Such as digital security and information technology.
The friendship between our two countries is supported through exchanges not only between governments but also between the private sector legislature and between people. I hope that under Samdech Techo's leadership, the exchanges between the two countries' legislatures will be further developed.
I sincerely wish Samdech Techo good health, the development of Cambodia to be more prosperous and wish the Cambodian people happiness.
Samdech Preah Brahma Rattanamony Pin Sem Leads Monks to Organize the 13th Anniversary of the Remembrance of Chuon Nath and the Khmer Trinity Church at Wat Reach Bo, Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): On the afternoon of April 3, 2024, Siem Reap monks held a memorial service for the 13th Khmer Trinity Church at Wat Reach Bo, Siem Reap.
This ceremony was held under the initiative of Samdech Preah Brahma Ratanamony Serey Sovanno Pin Sem, Mahanikaya and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Reachbo, as well as leaders and Buddhists from all walks of life.
The ceremony was held to commemorate the merits of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Choat Gnhano Chuon Nath and the Church of the Trinity and the Khmer Dictionary to show the Buddhists a better understanding of the works of the King and the compilation of the scriptures. Khmer national science is to awaken and raise the consciousness of Khmer children to preserve the legacy of our ancestors for a long time to come.
Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, said that Samdech Preah Sangkareach Choat Gnhano Chuon Nath was an outstanding patriarch who sacrificed everything for the nation, religion, which has historically been recognized as the father of national literature. He devoted his time, energy, and intellect to the bliss and prosperity of the Buddha and the whole realm.
Preah Somongkol Seilachar Chum Kim Leng, Chief of the Provincial Council, is adamant that the cause that led to the Remembrance Day is due to the wisdom of Samdech Brahma Rattanamony, Pin Sem Sereysovano, who always remembered the merits of Samdech Sangkha Reach as an individual. The image is like a rose that grows out of the mud but does not smell of mud, only the fragrance.
(Banteay Meanchey): A military police officer from Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, sent a suspect with evidence to the Provincial Court in connection with a case of drug trafficking, storage and use.
The drug trafficking suspect was led by Poipet City Gendarmerie, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, Municipal Gendarmerie Base Commander in front of Gold World Casino in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. April 2, 2024.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that before cracking down on the case, at the time of the incident, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie received information from the security that there was a case of drug distribution in the back immediately. Arrived at the scene and arrested a suspect, including confiscating exhibits to the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie for processing.
After the police arrested and interrogated the suspect, he confessed that he had actually trafficked, stored and used illegal drugs. He has been jailed several times in the past in connection with cases of theft, violence and drug trafficking. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor Charges Four Vietnamese Nationals and Their Fellows for Drug Trafficking
After receiving and examining the case, the prosecution decided to charge four Vietnamese suspects and their accomplices with the criminal offenses of producing, storing and trafficking drugs and money laundering as criminal offenses. Article 47, Article 48 of the Law on Drug Control and Article 38 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing.
Banteay Meanchey Coalition Authorities Seize More Than 3 Tons of Deteriorated Chicken Products in Search of a Merchant House in O'Chrov District
(Banteay Meanchey): The joint authority of Banteay Meanchey province inspected and inspected the location of a stall selling mixed chicken products in Chok Chey village, O'Bei Choan commune, O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province, and found 4 ice buckets containing chicken products, including: Chicken thighs, chicken wings, chicken bones, offal, chicken wings, 3,100 kg of chicken blood.
The operation was coordinated by Mr. Khlok Nouy, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor's Office, on the morning of April 3, 2024, at the home of a chicken trader. Her name is Chea Danika, female, 29 years old.
According to Chea Dany, the owner of the goods, he told the police that he bought all the chicken wings from a trader who imported them from Thailand and sold them to him in Jochey village. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Market continues.
A total of 3,100 kilograms of mixed chicken products are unlicensed by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production. The content of the law on animal health and animal production that causes loss of original quantity or quality is not allowed to sell in the market because it can allow people to buy and eat unhealthy.
After taking notes, the joint authorities gave Chea Dany, the owner of the crime scene, a thumbprint to stop buying substandard animal production as evidence. As for the 3,100 kilograms of mixed chicken products, the joint authorities also burned them in the evening of the same day. Ministry of Environment and Ministry of Agriculture
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, has ordered the army to take part in the protection of natural forest conservation areas throughout the country with the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. This is according to the order of General Vong Pisen, which was received by Fresh News on April 4, 2024.
The issuance of such an order by General Vong Pisen was made in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, ordering the Ministry of Environment, Ministries, Institutions and relevant authorities to strengthen the management of natural resources throughout the country and strictly enforce the law. The perpetrator of the forest crime.
General Vong Pisen issued the following orders:
First, the Commander of the Army, the Commander of the Navy and the Commander of the National Gendarmerie shall assign a force to cooperate with the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and the local authority. Relevant authorities to participate in the protection and protection of natural forest conservation areas throughout the country.
Second, ready to intervene in time to the request of the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, local authorities and relevant law enforcement forces to take immediate measures to crack down on crime. Who cut down natural forest conservation areas.
Third, assign a task force to search for criminals who come to hide in natural forest conservation areas, who have the means of destroying forests and encroaching on forest land, violating public order, and must immediately take repressive measures.
Fourth, all forces that have the duty to cooperate must adhere to the discipline of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces by not participating in committing illegal crimes.
Fifth, the Director of the Cabinet of the General Command, the Commander of the Army, the Commander of the Navy, the Commander of the National Gendarmerie and relevant institutions shall be assigned to implement this regulation effectively from the date of signing.
Ministry of Environment Continues to Disseminate Measures to Prevent and Reduce Public Air Pollution in Cambodia-Thailand Border Provinces
(Pailin): Campaigns to strengthen measures to prevent and reduce public air pollution continue to be held in the provinces along the Cambodian-Thai border. Dissemination campaign to prevent and reduce public air pollution held in Pailin province
The campaign was presided over by Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, and Mr. Nguon Lina, Deputy Governor of Pailin Province, and was attended by representatives of provincial, municipal, district, provincial and local authorities. On Wednesday, April 3, 2024.
The Ministry of Environment requested to participate in the implementation of Circular 01 of the Royal Government, which must strengthen management:
* Open waste incineration, such as incineration of agricultural waste, firewood, grassland, forest waste, solid waste, plastic waste, etc. * Improve urban environment * Establish air pollution monitoring and forecasting system * Prevent Dust from construction sites * Controls the release of air pollutants from production sites.
It should be noted that in the past, the Ministry of Environment has asked the governors of the 25 provinces to advise people not to burn forests, grasslands, burn plastic, agricultural waste, stumps, garbage, solid waste, plastic and other waste in the open, which causes There is an increase in air pollution.
