(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Investment Promotion Working Group in Sihanoukville, this morning, April 3, 2024, chaired a working group meeting to discuss the preparation of a separate sub-decree. On the issuance of special visas to investors and businessmen in Sihanoukville.
This special sub-decree on the issuance of special visas aims to attract and promote investment in Sihanoukville by 2024 by providing special visas to investors and business people in Sihanoukville for the purchase or lease of long-term real estate that is worth more than the price. Any specific.
He noted that the preparation of the sub-decree on the issuance of special visas is one of the key measures, as stated in the special program to promote investment in Sihanoukville 2024.
This sub-decree will determine the principles, procedures and procedures for issuing special visas and apply to investors, businessmen and foreign tourists who come to invest and do business in Sihanoukville and / or stay in the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with the law and Legal standard letter in force. This sub-decree will pay special attention to streamlining procedures, extending visa validity and length of stay, and collecting visa fees.
After a lively discussion, the meeting agreed in principle on the content of a separate draft sub-decree on the issuance of this special visa.
At the same time, the Lecturer instructed the Secretariat of the Working Group to continue to review, refine and further improve this important draft sub-decree to be more comprehensive and better by meeting, consulting and receiving good input from Relevant ministries and institutions.
