(Phnom Penh): Former Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the President of the Senate on Wednesday, April 3, 2024, a position that provides a wider role not only as a political line on the executive branch, but also Canal to another top legislature.
After leaving the top political seat seven months ago, he returned to the presidency of the Senate when he reached the age of 72, "the same year" after becoming prime minister at a young age. Thirty-two years is a good time to turn from 72 to 27 when he became foreign minister at the age of 27.
The song "Borei Chulong" describes "old lovers know how to care for the heart" embodies a sweet romantic meaning that is attractive in the context of love, but in the political context it may be difficult to find a composer who dares to claim that he will be as sweet as the song This one song.
As president of the ruling party, he can appoint, exchange and have full influence over all political figures, even the prime minister, as long as those figures come from the ruling Cambodian People's Party.
In other words, Samdech Techo already has three aces in his hand: the president of the party, the president of the Senate and the chairman of the King's own Supreme Council, and the last ace is the acting head of state.
According to the above-mentioned positions and roles, Samdech Techo is like a great power in the political empire in Cambodia, because even in all national events, he will be in the highest position after the King. And still taller than his son, the prime minister.
After 38 years in power, Samdech Techo resigned as Prime Minister in August 2023, and this position was succeeded by his eldest son, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet.
As President of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Techo was able to control 120 of the 125 National Assembly seats after the July 2023 general election and 55 of the 58 seats in the Senate, which contested on February 25, 2024. .
Two days before becoming president of the Senate, the influential former prime minister said in the lower house that he had sat in the National Assembly for 43 years (more than half his life), but that he had to resign from the seat. This old one to go and complete a new task.
Five senior political figures have left the camp, including Prak Sokhon, a former foreign minister and four other secretaries of state, two of whom were Cambodia's permanent representatives to the United Nations (Ouch Bo). Rith and Mr. Cham Vidya, Mr. Lay Samkol and Mr. Chhiv Yi Seang).
From the beginning, I tried to anticipate that the presence of the top five senior diplomats who "left the old camp to the new camp" may have been Samdech Techo's sketch, which would use the Senate as a modern diplomatic liaison to work with. Both the East and West blocks, walking in parallel with his son, who is in power.
My outlook may be one-sided after Samdech Techo stated at the Senate on Wednesday that "the role of the Senate is also very important in the development of international relations." "For that reason, and for this legislation, I will make the promotion of parliamentary diplomacy one of the priorities of our institution."
Speaking with conviction, Samdech Techo sent a message to all 62 senators of the new mandate to take care of their health for at least until the end of the six-year term. This is a message that all senators will never forget.
