Samdech Vibol Sena Phekdey Say Chhum sends a message of congratulations and congratulations to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of being elected President of the Senate for the 5th term
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Supreme Personal Adviser to the King, sent a message of congratulations and congratulations to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of his election as President of the Senate for the 5th term in the first session of the Senate. The 5th legislature on April 3, 2024 under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In the message of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, he wrote that my wife and I would like to express our warmest and happiest congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of his election Elected President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the opening ceremony of the first session of the Senate of the 5th legislature on April 3, 2024.
South Korea on Tuesday sanctioned two Russian ships it said were carrying military cargo to North Korea. Seoul has also sanctioned two Russian organizations and Russian citizens linked to Pyongyang's nuclear and missile programs.
Russian Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova told reporters at a weekly news conference: "This is Seoul's unfriendly act and it is very unfortunate. "I would like to emphasize that illegal sanctions will have a negative impact on relations with Russia."
"Russia is developing good relations with friendly North Korea in accordance with the norms of international law without compromising South Korea's national security," she added.
Relations between Moscow and Pyongyang were strengthened last year after North Korean leader Kim Jong Un visited Russia. Russia last week vetoed the annual update of experts monitoring the UN sanctions imposed on North Korea over its nuclear weapons and ballistic missile programs.
The move comes amid US-led allegations that North Korea transferred weapons to Russia for use in the war in Ukraine. Moscow and Pyongyang have denied the allegations, but last year vowed to deepen military ties. Chbar Ampov District Administration Issues Letter of Clarification on Land Issue Behind Wat Champa, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov
