The ceremony will take place on April 7, 2024 at 8:00 am in Prey Romduol village, Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province. Must participate in preserving culture, traditions, and religion
(Kampot): Dr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, requested the authorities, people and young people living in districts bordering with neighboring countries to try to participate in preserving the culture, traditions, religion and high nationalism.
This proposal was made while the Governor of Kampot Province, Mao Thunin, presided over the inauguration ceremony of a school at Wat Yos Sovan Ochum Prey Tonle in Prey Tonle Village, Prey Tonle Commune, Banteay Meas District, Kampot Province on the 3rd. April 2024, with the participation of leaders, civil servants, the armed forces, authorities, citizens and many stakeholders.
At the same time, the provincial governor also said that Cambodia, under the skillful leadership of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set out a strategy for the first phase, focusing on people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology to make Cambodia Become a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
He added that along with the efforts of the leaders of the authorities at all levels must also participate in performing their duties better.
However, the achievements of the pagoda, which was inaugurated today, show the participation of the district authorities, people and philanthropists in promoting the Buddhist sector to develop simultaneously with the sector. Empire.
According to his own view, there are two kinds of life, one is from birth to death, which requires food, shelter, utensils and clothing, and the other is culture, civilization, tradition, religion, which is the soul of the nation. A nation is indispensable.
The provincial governor further stated that in relation to the construction of pagodas, before the construction, it is necessary to look at the style clearly, is it correct according to the Khmer style? Especially on the occasion of the National New Year, the old authorities must lead the youth to participate in folk games and dress in the traditional Khmer way to preserve the heritage of our ancestors to last forever.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Governor Facilitates Kampong Boeung Market Vendors Requesting Postponement of Market Construction from Construction Company at Request of Vendors
(Kampong Chhnang): After a strong request from the vendors at Kampong Boeung Market, asked the Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province to ask the Governor to facilitate the delay in the construction of Kampong Boeung Market above because the people Market vendors have not yet been able to raise money to buy stalls.
As a result, under the coordination of the provincial administration by 1:00 pm, the following unified principles were achieved:
Representatives of investment companies have agreed for a total period of 5 years from before and will start again from April 3, 2024 to the beginning of September 2025 (for a year and a half)
* The company has started construction and requires traders to move their stalls to the site of the disaster building and along the concrete road near Kampong Boeung Market. From September 2025, the investment company will start the construction of the market for 18 months * After the construction of Kampong Boeung Santepheap market, the traders will be allowed to rent stalls in the market for free for another 2 years and required Pay only market fees.
The above compromise made the business representatives happy and expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who assigned the provincial governor and the working group to help. Coordinate all their hardships, they asked for only 3 years, but the company agreed to give them up to 5 years.
On that occasion, the provincial governor also brought the budget of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi to the business people to facilitate transportation and lunch to all of them, which they received with great enthusiasm.
