The following is the message of the Khmer Conservative Party: The Governor of Pursat Province chaired a meeting to review the work of the 10 sub-committees to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes.
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command and Chairman of the Joint Working Group, on April 3, 2024, at the first floor meeting of the Provincial Hall, chaired a meeting to review the work of the subcommittee. The 10 groups of natural resource crime prevention and suppression workers who have been conducting large-scale crackdown operations for the past one month in Phnom Kravanh and Veal Veng districts of Pursat province.
Addressing the meeting, Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command and Chairman of the Joint Working Group praised and highly appreciated the 10 sub-committees for their hard work in preventing and cracking down on crime. Violate natural resources to achieve all goals successfully.
After the 10 sub-committees discussed the results of the past implementation and combined to avoid duplication of data previously implemented in the first step, Mr. Khoy Rida also set out a plan and tasks. Some tasks for the 10 sub-committees for further implementation include:
First, all sub-committees must review the actual location and the installed map in order to minimize bias.
Second: How much data should be subtracted from the first part, how much can be deducted from the second part to be equivalent to the same data?
Third: The team must continue to stand to review the detailed mapping work and reach the destination at all points.
Fourth, the Provincial Unity Command, as well as all 10 sub-committees, must clearly examine which sites will be confiscated as state property for reforestation, which sites will be allowed to reforest, and which villages Communes and districts, as well as communities, used to ask for a cut-off for people to enjoy in the past to ask for a decision from the Ministry of Environment.
Fifth, the chairman of the meeting also donated some money and food to the 10 sub-committees and some light command.
The King sends congratulatory message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on his election as President of the Senate of the 5th Mandate
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on April 3, 2024, sent a message of congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen Has been elected President of the Senate of Cambodia for the fifth term.
Through this message, he warmly commended Samdech Techo as the best, wisest and most talented national leader who properly led the country to peace and built many national achievements in all fields and Strive to eradicate poverty, improve the living standards of the people in the society and enhance the prestige of our nation on the national and international stage.
He believes that Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo, as well as all leaders and members, will continue to lead the Senate in preparing and reviewing the national law properly in accordance with the Constitution of our nation and with good law enforcement. Preserving the traditional culture, customs and morals of the nation, as well as protecting the environment and natural resources, are the key factors in sustaining national and economic stability.
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of April 3, 2024, the Ministry of Rural Development organized a blessing ceremony to bless Preah Serey Mongkul as a farewell to the old year and to welcome the new year, the year of Rong Chhasak, 2567 AD, especially to welcome the new year goddess. Name: Mahot Ratevi, presided over by Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development.
The blessing ceremony was attended by the Permanent Secretary of State, the Under Secretary of State, the Undersecretary of State, as well as leaders and civil servants at all levels under the Ministry of Rural Development.
The event was held in accordance with the Buddhist tradition, with the offering of lanterns, flowers, and other relics to the Preah Ratanatray to pay homage to the Buddha, Dharma, and five monks. Mongkul Chamroeun Serey Soursdey.
(Phnom Penh): Today, leaders of political parties, civil society and many people sent congratulatory messages to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, who was elected President of the Senate of the fifth mandate on the morning of the 3rd. This April 2024.
For His Excellency Dr. Ros Chantraboth, the son of a Cambodian intellectual who has been through three generations and is also an advisor to His Majesty the King Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, sent a meaningful message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen with the following contents:
Today, April 3, 2024, is a great historical day for Cambodia as well as for Cambodians all over the world who have seen and understood that "Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen" continues to maintain peace, protect and Develop this miserable Cambodian territory as "President of the National Senate".
Every Khmer, as well as history, can not forget the great merits of this Samdech.
Please accept, Sir, the assurance of my highest consideration and loyalty to you and my family. ”
I live Ros Chantrabot!
The content of the swearing-in of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President and Vice-President and all 62 Senators is committed to respecting the Constitution and serving the nation
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of April 3, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, as well as the First Vice President, Second Vice President and a total of 62 senators of the fifth mandate, took the oath of office before the King. The faces of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach and Tevta keep the umbrella at the Royal Palace.
With this swearing-in, all leaders and members are committed to respecting the Constitution and always serving both now and in the future for the benefit of the people, the nation and the motherland of Cambodia, and committed not to exploit national interests for personal or family gain; For factions or for their respective parties.
The following is the full text of the swearing-in of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, as well as the two Vice-Presidents and all members:
"We, the President, the Vice President and the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, take the oath of office in the presence of the King, the King and the Deity, as follows:
In carrying out our duties and in fulfilling the mission entrusted to us by the people of Cambodia, we are committed to respecting the Constitution, serving both now and in the future for the benefit of the people. People, nation and motherland of Cambodia. We swear not to exploit the national interest for our own or for our family or for our party or party.
We are determined to sacrifice our lives to protect both now and in the future: * Complete independence of the motherland of Cambodia * Full national sovereignty * Legal territorial integrity in the land and sea borders Cambodia existed from 1963 to 1969 * National unity and did not allow any division or separatism.
- We are committed to maintaining neutrality and non-alignment for Cambodia, both now and in the future, and will not allow anyone who wants to interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia or to take orders. Cannot dictate Cambodia's national and international policies. We do not serve foreign interests and do not harm the interests of the people, the nation and the motherland of Cambodia.
In resolving national and international issues, we will completely eliminate all forms of violence. However, the Kingdom of Cambodia reserves the right to bear arms to fight against foreign aggression in order to defend its homeland.
We are determined to fight against all kinds of corruption, against social injustice, and to fight for national reconciliation, for national unity, for social peace and national peace, for the prosperity of the Cambodian people and for the glorious glory of the motherland of Cambodia. Worship and love of all of us. "
The Ministry of Education strictly prohibits playing with water spray, throwing water bags, and spraying powder during New Year celebrations at public and private schools.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued guidelines on maintaining order and safety during the New Year Sankranti at public and private secondary schools. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News on April 3, 2024.
The Ministry of Education has observed that some students in secondary schools have been playing non-traditional Khmer games, including: spraying water, throwing water bags, spraying paint, etc. on each other without Orderlessness, lack of dignity and insecurity.
In order to prevent and avoid the eventual occurrence and ensure the dignity and safety of students, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports recommends to all the following secondary institutions:
1: Absolutely prohibit and immediately prohibit any games that are not games or Khmer folk dances and some games that face the risk of unsafe and dangerous, such as water spraying, throwing water, throwing water, paint, etc. .
2. The management team, teachers and children's councils, youth councils must organize the division of responsibilities on a day-to-day basis to facilitate students to participate in playing Khmer folk games happily and safely.
3: Take care to maintain health and hygiene to avoid infectious diseases.
4. Cooperate closely with parents or guardians of students, communities, local authorities to provide and receive information related to various negative activities committed by students to provide education, guidance and improvement in a timely manner.
