Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen after receiving the support of 62 out of 62 senators to become the President of the Senate
(Phnom Penh): After the great success of the mission to lead a nation full of difficulties that can not be calculated for more than 40 years as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, now Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues his new role as President of the Senate. As one of the top institutions of the nation.
In the first session of the Senate of the 5th legislature on the morning of Wednesday, April 3, 2024, one day before the 54th anniversary of the turning of life as a fighter for power to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received support. From the senator 62 out of 62 votes to be the chairman of the Senate.
The following is the main content of Samdech Techo Hun Sen after receiving the support of 62 out of 62 senators to become the President of the Senate in the first session of the Senate for the 5th term:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to express his deep gratitude and heartfelt thanks to the members of the National Assembly, Commune / Sangkat Councilors in the constituencies in the eight constituencies, most of whom voted for the CPP on the 25th. February passed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this overwhelming support once again reflects the confidence and trust in the CPP as a party that guarantees peace, stability and development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of the previous term, as well as His Excellency Dr. Simka, former First Vice President and His Excellency Dr. Tep Ngon, former Second Vice President. The dedication and leadership of both Samdech and His Excellency has helped strengthen our institution over the years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalls the history of the establishment of the Senate to resolve the political stalemate in Cambodia 25 years ago
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Reminds of the Establishment of the Senate, the Great Grace of His Majesty the King in Resolving the Cambodian Political Crisis
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges all senators to take care of their health while they are old
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that about the attempted assassination of Samdech on September 24, 1998 in Siem Reap, if at that time Samdech died, Siem Reap would become a killing field and a pool of blood
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the establishment of the Senate was the end of the political stalemate at that time, which was like an arrow shooting many birds
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the division of power at that time after the establishment of the Senate was Samdech Chea Sim as the President of the Senate, Samdech Krom Preah as the President of the National Assembly and Samdech himself as the Prime Minister and no longer had the First and Second Prime Ministers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without political coordination to resolve the stalemate by His Majesty the King, there would be a long period of bloodshed
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the co-founder for the political negotiations to form the Senate at that time was only one Samdech left now
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the commitment of both Samdech and His Excellency in respecting the Constitution, defending the monarchy and the development of the nation and the well-being of our people deserves the deepest gratitude and encouragement. Let us all continue this noble legacy in our daily work.
* At the same time, the Senate also plays an important political role in the country by coordinating the work between the National Assembly and the Royal Government to resolve any possible political crisis.
* As co-founder of the Senate, Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to take this rare opportunity to recall the political importance of the establishment of the Senate in resolving the political crisis that has posed a major threat to unity and National stability after the second parliamentary election.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the will of Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim under the agreement of 13 November 1998 to accept the leadership of this supreme institution in 1999 opened the way for a political solution and cooperation between Elected political parties.
* As President of the Senate, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirms his commitment to lead this institution in fulfilling its roles and responsibilities and in joining the National Assembly and the Royal Government to fulfill their respective mandates. In serving the nation and the people of Cambodia. We will firmly defend the Constitution, monarchy and liberal democracy, pluralism and the rule of law.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that 54 years ago, he was preparing to enter the jungle, now he is leading the Senate, 32 years old is the Prime Minister, 72 years old is the President of the Senate
