The following is the full text of Russey Keo district administration: People in 4 villages in Sangkat Krabei Riel received land titles from Siem Reap provincial authorities
(Siem Reap): Residents of Roka village, Kork Dong village, Proma village and Khnar village, Sangkat Krabei Riel, Siem Reap city, on April 3, 2024, received a certificate of real estate (land title) from Siem Reap Provincial Authority. 3,426 plots The ceremony took place at Prey Pdao pagoda in Krasaing village, Sangkat Krabei Riel, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Samkol Sochetra, Deputy Governor and Mr. Bou Chum Sambath, Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, as well as representatives of various departments around the province and many people.
Mr. Bou Chum Sambath said that during the issuance of the title to the people, the professional officers worked very carefully and with the highest responsibility to issue the title deed in a systematic way for each village until the completion. Has provided a certificate of ownership of real estate to citizens to use legally and have permanent rights.
Mr. Bou Chum Sambath said that the plots that are being handed over at this time are only those plots that do not have any disputes related to archeological sites or protected areas managed by the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology. In connection with various disputes, the Administrative Commission will continue to review and resolve the procedures to reach the issuance of land titles to the landowners.
Mr. Samkol Sochetra also urged the local authorities to help the people to get the certificate of ownership of this property to everyone.
He also reminded people who have not yet paid the property tax and the land tax on unused land, please hurry to pay the tax at the tax office of the Siem Reap Provincial Tax Branch for 2024, which will expire on the 30th. September 2024 as well. Samdech President Hun Manet sends congratulatory message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the first session of the Senate elected as the President of the Senate for the fifth term
(Phnom Penh): His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on April 3, 2024, sent a congratulatory message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of his election by the first session of the Senate for the fifth term. Appointed President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The message of the Prime Minister is as follows: "On behalf of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and on my own behalf, I am very pleased and sincerely extend my heartfelt congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen on the occasion that Samdech Techo was unanimously elected by the Senate of the 5th legislature to be the President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
I firmly believe that the new Senate, chaired by Samdech Techo, will continue to play a more active role in strengthening liberal democracy, pluralism and the rule of law in Cambodia, as well as promoting national prestige in the regional and global framework. The catalyst is indispensable in pushing Cambodia to achieve its vision of a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
