But in the incident, caused a controversy on social media, with public opinion accusing the authorities of colluding with the car to change drivers. The public claimed that the driver was a woman, but when the police arrested him turned into a man.
Regarding this accusation, the spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Colonel Sam Vicheka, came out and explained that it was not true, that is, the driver was a man while the passenger was his wife.
Colonel Sam Vichheka explained that the husband was the driver of the car when the accident happened. Both the driver (husband) and his wife (passenger) came down. From the car on the victim, when the victim was seen lying on the road and other passengers stopped to look, causing traffic jams.
At that time, the husband told his wife to get in the car to get to the corner so that there would be no congestion. Suddenly, while driving, the reporter arrived at the scene and took pictures of his wife. Hold the steering wheel. When the police took the driver for questioning, there was a misunderstanding that the driver was stolen.
A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police confirmed that "the driver of the car was a man who, prior to the incident, was questioned by a professional officer who admitted that the man was her husband. Get out of the car to see all the victims, and when there is a traffic jam, his wife (the driver's wife) got in the car to avoid congestion, then the reporter arrived.
However, in this incident, the car side shared the sad death with the family of the motorcyclist who encountered this horrific incident.
