Minister of Information Invites Monks to Hold a Blessing Ceremony for the Blessing of the New Year and Happy New Year
On the afternoon of April 2, 2024, Mr. Neth Pheaktra and Ms. Tuy Serey Rattanak, together with the leaders of civil servants of the Ministry of Information, invited the arts group of the National Cultural Movement Association to perform a traditional dance to dispel bad luck in the old year and celebrate the New Year. Khmer national tradition 2024.
Trod dance is a dance that represents the passing of the old year, the change of the new year and the elimination of bad luck, and to give blessings to the locals on the occasion of the new year.
According to the book "Khmer Folk Dance" of the Khmer Traditional Church, the Trudi dance is a kind of folk dance that is still found only in Siem Reap today and sometimes in some Battambang provinces in the adjacent provinces. Siem Reap itself. Trud dance is only played during the Khmer New Year to bless the locals on the occasion of the New Year.
Tomorrow morning, the Senate will hold its first session for the fifth term under the presidency of the King.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, April 10, 2024, the Senate will hold its first session for the fifth term under the highest presidency of God. His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Senate is the supreme body of the nation as enshrined in the Constitution. The Senate is the legislative body that contributes to ensuring legal security through the review and passage of laws, especially the Senate is the steering wheel and compass of local democracy.
The Senate of each legislature is elected. The number of senators is equal to half of the members of the National Assembly. Of these, two senators are appointed by the King and two are elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote.
The Senate for the fifth term was elected on February 25, 2024. There are four political parties competing in the 5th Senate election: the Cambodian People's Party, the Khmer Will Party, the National Forces Party and the FUNCINPEC Party.
The two senators appointed by the King are: Princess Norodom Arunrasmey and Prince Sisowath Thomico. By two senators nominated by the National Assembly: Mr. Sok Isan and Mr. Heng Halim.
+ Organization and functioning of the Senate
The organization and functioning of the Senate shall be determined in the Rules of Procedure of the Senate. The Senate shall convene the first session of each legislature 60 days after the election convened by the King.
The King or His Majesty the King confers or honors the opening of the first session of each legislature.
After the King or his / her representative has opened the legislature, if the Senate has more than half of the total number of members present, the Senate may proceed under the chairmanship of one of the Provisional Presidents, elected or appointed senator. Most present and no complaints, as well as five elected or appointed senators, the youngest present as a secretary to assist the chairman in the work.
Under the leadership of the caretaker President, the Senate shall commence the following activities: a: Declare the validity of the mandate of each member.
Nothing can be discussed under the chairmanship of the interim chairman. All senators must be sworn in before taking office.
Prior to the commencement of the work under the chairmanship of its President, the Senate shall elect members of the commissions separately by secret ballot and approve the Rules of Procedure of the Senate, which shall determine the organization and functioning of the Senate by an absolute majority of the number of senators. As a whole.
Each committee has at least 5 members.
After receiving the support of the Senate, before commencing its work, each Commission shall meet within the Commission to secretly vote to elect the Chairman, Vice-Chairman and Secretary of each Commission.
Each Commission shall determine its roles, duties and powers in accordance with the Constitution, the Rules of Procedure of the Senate and the laws in force, and submit them to the Standing Committee for review and decision.
+ History of the Cambodian Senate
The establishment of the Senate is an important political event in history, shining a new light for Cambodia through the strengthening of the spirit of national unity, national reconciliation, political stability and the commitment to building a liberal, pluralistic democracy and the rule of law.
Pursuant to the Constitutional Law on the Amendment to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which came into force on March 8, 1999, the Senate was established and convened its first session of the first legislature on March 25, 1999.
Out of the 61 senators in the first term, there are 10 members. The organization and functioning of the Senate shall be in accordance with the internal rules and regulations of the Senate and the relevant laws as well as the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Senate has a standing committee to lead, manage and review all matters within the conditions set by the rules of procedure. The President of the Senate is the Chairman of the Standing Committee, the two Vice-Chairmen and the Chairmen of the various committees of the Senate are members.
The Senate of the first legislature has nine committees as members in the performance of its functions, which are divided into the following jurisdictions:
1: Human Rights Protection Commission and receive complaints.
2: Finance and Banking Commission.
3: Committee on Economy, Investment Plan, Agriculture, Rural Development and Environment.
4: Interior Committee, National Defense, Investigation and Clearance.
5: Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information.
6: Legislative Committee.
7: Committee on Education, Cult, Culture and Tourism.
8: Committee on Health, Social Affairs, Labor and Women's Affairs.
9. Commission on Public Works, Transport, Telecommunication, Post, Industry, Energy and Commerce.
The first term of the Senate was extended twice (once a year) by Royal Decree:
Pursuant to the Law on the Election of Senators from the second and subsequent terms, the Senate shall be elected by universal suffrage, elected and appointed for a period of six years.
The second legislative election for the Senate took place on January 22, 2006.
The second legislature has 61 members, of which 57 are unanimously elected, two are nominated by the King and two are elected by the National Assembly by a simple majority.
The second legislature of the Senate convened on March 20, 2006 under the high presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Of the 57 elected senators, the following are:
Of the 61 senators, nine are members.
The election of senators for the third term took place on Sunday, January 29, 2012. As a result, out of 57 elected members, the following are:
Out of the 61 senators in the third term, there are 10 members.
The third legislature of the Senate held its first session on March 20, 2012 under the high presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
From the first session onwards until the middle of the third legislature, there are nine committees of the Senate, and the composition of the commissions elected by the Senate is in accordance with the rules of procedure of the Senate from the CPP. All Cambodians, including the chairman, vice chairman, secretary and members of the commission.
Pursuant to the Agreement on Political Settlement dated 22 July 2014 between the CPP and the CNRP, the working group of the CPP and the working group of the Sam Rainsy Party agreed to sign an agreement on the reorganization of The locomotive leads the Senate on August 11, 2014.
Through the above agreement, the Senate amended Article 15 of the Rules of Procedure of the Senate. Article 15 of the new rules of procedure of the Senate, the committees of the Senate are as follows:
1: The Human Rights Commission receives complaints and investigations.
2: Committee on Economy, Finance, Banking and Auditing.
3: Agriculture Investment Planning Committee, Water Resources, Meteorology, Rural Development and Environment.
4: Committee on Interior, National Defense, Relations. National Assembly, Senate, Inspection and Public Function.
6: Commission on Legislation and Justice.
7. Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religion, Culture, Fine Arts and Tourism.
8. Committee on Health, Social Affairs, Veterans, Youth Rehabilitation, Vocational Training and Women's Affairs.
9. Commission on Public Transport, Civil Aviation, Post, Telecommunication, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
10. Commission of Inquiry, Clearance and Anti-Corruption.
At the same time, the composition of the 10 commissions has been revised, re-elected and re-elected. The 11 SRP senators have been included in all the committees, including the seats of the two commission chairpersons, the first and tenth commissions, the two deputy chairmen, the third and seventh commission secretaries. Two committees, the first and tenth commissions, and five other members, were added to the first, third, seventh, eighth and tenth commissions.
Note: The Senate of the third legislature has Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim as its chairman, Mr. Say Chhum as its first vice president and Mr. Tep Ngorn as its second vice president.
On June 8, 2015, Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim, President of the Senate, passed away. In the Extraordinary Session of the Senate on June 9, 2015, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum was elected President of the Senate and Mr. Ney Pena was the First Vice President of the Senate for the third term.
The election of senators for the fourth term will take place on February 25, 2018. As a result, the CPP won a total of 58 seats in eight regions of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
For the fourth term, a total of 62 senators, an increase of one seat in the 7th constituency (58 elected by 2 elected by the King, 2 elected by the National Assembly by a simple majority). National Assembly increases 2 seats in Sihanoukville constituency (6th legislature has a total of 125 members).
The 4th Senate opened its first session on April 23, 2018 under the high presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Of the 62 senators of the fourth term, 10 were.
Note: The composition of the Senate leadership consists of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum as Chairman, Mr. Ney Pena as the First Vice President and HE Tep Ngorn as the Second Vice President.
On September 29, 2018, Mr. Ney Pena, First Vice President of the Senate passed away. During an extraordinary session of the Senate on October 11, 2018, Mr. Sim Ka was elected by the Senate as the First Vice President of the Senate. King Dismisses Ouch Borith as Senior Minister for Special Missions
