This exhibition features paintings on the walls of pagodas throughout Cambodia from 1890 to 1970. Through photos of these paintings, visitors can learn about the artistic content of important historical sites that emphasize the importance of preserving these cultural treasures.
The murals on display in this exhibition are a mix of tradition and religion linked to contemporary aspects to showcase the talents of local anonymous artists, leaving a strong legacy through Their work. These paintings also provide an in-depth understanding of the daily lives of the Cambodian people and the effects of technological, cultural, political and social changes at the time.
