In the first session of the Senate of the 5th legislature on the morning of Wednesday, April 3, 2024, one day before the 54th anniversary of the turning of life as a fighter for power to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received support from The senator, 62 out of 62 votes, shall be the chairman of the Senate.
At the age of 32, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 40 years ago, became the Prime Minister without any objections from the members of the National Assembly, and now he is the President of the Senate without any objections, even though there are three senators. From the opposition party.
The vote of confidence in Samdech Techo to lead this supreme institution is a clear demonstration of the noble role of Samdech Techo, which is deeply respected by the Cambodian people and has always had a strong belief in wisdom and integrity. Samdech Techo's ingenuity in leading the country as the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the son of a farmer living along the Mekong River in Peam Koh Sna village, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province. Samdech Techo was born on Tuesday, August 15, 1952. Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the third child of five siblings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that the greatest goal of Samdech when he was young was only to be a teacher, but the turn and the problems of the country pushed Samdech Techo to become a leader who received the top destiny of the nation.
After sacrificing and struggling in many national causes, the result of his deep loyalty and patriotic conscience to the nation and the people of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was trusted by the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Cambodia to be elected President. Council of Ministers or Prime Minister on January 14, 1985, replacing Mr. Chan Si, who died of leukemia.
This word is committed to the well-being of the people, mainly used by Samdech Techo throughout his life as Prime Minister.
After taking office, not only did he face food shortages, but he also faced many other challenges. The four priority priorities set by the 33-year-old prime minister as his political line are rehabilitation, infrastructure, water, railways and human resource training. The genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Seeing that being in a state of peace and war could not enable Cambodia to develop and bring happiness to its people, and was a threat to its regime. Comrade Hun Sen also wanted to find peace by uniting all parties to the conflict.
The intention to unite the nation urged Samdech Techo to launch a policy of negotiations with His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk until the implementation of the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991 in 1987 and to implement a policy of win-win, end the flames of war and national division. Complete Cambodia on December 29, 1998. Unification and unification break the historical record of post-Angkorian national disintegration that lasted no less than 500 years.
After the complete success of national unification in line with the political crisis was also eased after 1998, that is, from 2000 is a new time that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is fully focused on building. National development and national integration into the international community as well.
Since the end of 1998, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has become one of the best guides in the new era, transforming Cambodia into the fastest growing and developing nation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen is seen as a leader with great flexibility and skill in leadership and has attracted the attention of both national and international circles.
In the period of about 20 years from 1998 to 2018, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Cambodian nation has changed dramatically, making Cambodia known only as the smoke of war, turning it into a beautiful land, small and large buildings emerge. Infrastructure, bridges, roads show a mixed presence from the city to the countryside, Cambodians used to be flooded with tears turned into a beautiful smile.
The leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen also received great admiration and admiration from His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk when he was alive, as well as the King of Cambodia, the Queen and the Cambodian people of all walks of life.
Cambodia since the fall of the Angkorian Empire in the 12th century has known only the breakup, war, despair, and decline, and its fame has been buried on the international stage. It can be said that only in the last 20 years, Cambodia has known the reunification of the nation and the rebuilding of its prestige in the international arena, full of national honor and pride for all Cambodians.
As Prime Minister, he also created historical events related to sports. After missing out and waiting for more than 60 years due to the war and economic crisis, in 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to organize the SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games with the greatest pride for the nation of Cambodia.
As for international politics, as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has made Cambodia play an important role and contribute to solving global problems through ASEAN mechanisms and as a member of international organizations. Through those roles, Cambodia's reputation is not tarnished like in the past.
(Kandal): The spokesperson of Kandal Provincial Police on April 3, 2024 came out to clarify and reject the accusation that the authorities of the Provincial Police arrested a Vietnamese man and started imprisoning him for transporting A rotten teal tree extracted from the bottom of a river.
