(According to the provincial announcement attached) Ministry of Environment strengthens measures to prevent and reduce air pollution in the northwestern provinces
It should be noted that Dr. Eang Sophalleth launched the Clean Sky Campaign, in which the Blue Sky Campaign started on November 15, 2023.
The Ministry has taken a series of measures to control the quality of air in factories and other sources that can cause air pollution, with the results confirming that the air quality in Cambodia is not yet polluted and does not cause pollution to neighboring countries.
In the past, the Ministry of Environment has asked the 25 provincial governors to advise people not to burn forests, grasslands, burn plastic, agricultural waste, stumps, garbage, solid waste, plastic and other incineration in the open, which has caused an increase. Up pollution.
The Ministry of Environment has recommended strengthening the prevention of forest fires, burning of grass, burning of tree stumps, burning of agricultural waste, dumping and burning of plastic waste and landfill fires, and taking measures to prevent dust at construction sites. And transportation of construction materials.
At the same time, the Ministry also recommended dusting and cleaning the streets and public places regularly.
