(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of April 2, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, Abhisit Bandit Sar Sokha, announced the promulgation of the recently promulgated Rule 873 of the Cambodian National Police. This of the Cambodian National Police Force.
General Professor Seng Phally, Director General of the General Department of Human Resources, presented the joint contents of the Prakas on the Discipline of the National Police of Cambodia in honor of Dr. Aphisandi Dr. Sar Sokha and disseminated to the whole ceremony.
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha added that the Ministry of Interior had issued the Prakas to replace National Police Rule 006, which had been in place for more than 28 years.
In addition, this important proclamation is a testament to the further reform of the National Police Force of the Ministry of Interior, which sets out new regulations and rules in response to the progress of society in accordance with the program. The policy and pentagon strategy of the Royal Government under the wise leadership and progressive vision of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Dr. Sar Sokha advised and instructed the following relevant units:
* First, each unit must organize a meeting to disseminate this Prakas to the police officers under their supervision and promote the effective implementation of this Prakas.
* Second: The Police Academy of Cambodia must include this prakas in the curriculum for all levels of training.
* Third: The General Department of Human Resources shall hold regular meetings to monitor the implementation of the Prakas on the Discipline of the National Police of Cambodia with the relevant units under the Ministry of Interior and the Capital and Provincial Police Commission on a regular basis.
* Fourth, the General Department of Human Resources must cooperate with relevant units to produce promotional videos on the strengthening of discipline, uniforms and respect of the National Police Force.
Please be informed that the Prakas on the discipline of the National Police of Cambodia was signed and implemented by Mr. Abhisandiband Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, which has 7 chapters and 35 articles.
