One child killed, two injured in school shooting in Finland, 12-year-old suspect arrested
A child has been killed and two others seriously injured in a shooting at a school on the outskirts of the Finnish capital on Tuesday, Finland police say. Authorities have arrested the suspect in connection with the attack. This is according to the release by Reuters on April 2, 2024.
There are no other suspects at this time, police said. However, they did not provide details on the identities of the suspects or victims, saying that they were all Finnish and that the suspects were 12 years old and a schoolboy.
The Helsinki Regional Hospital said in a statement without giving details that the two survivors were being treated for serious injuries.
