General Phuong Siphan, Secretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense, said: "We all remember that in the mission of the United Nations Engineering Force on Cambodian territory from April 1992 to September. In 1998, two Chinese People's Liberation Army soldiers sacrificed their lives in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Skun area, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Phuong Siphan on that occasion also mentioned the new historical achievements from the cooperation between Cambodia and China, especially through the visit of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia to the country. Recently, China, especially the cooperation between the Cambodian and Chinese armies, has been strengthened and expanded for continuous development.
Mr. Phuong Siphan also took this opportunity to express his deep gratitude to the Party, Government, Army and the people of the People's Republic of China, who have always provided full and material support to the Armed Forces and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Forever until now.
Wang Wentian also said that the celebration is to continue the ideal of promoting China-Cambodia friendship and spread the sacrifices of the heroes who strive to strengthen China-Cambodia friendship, uphold global peace and continue to achieve the Chinese dream. Restore the glory of the nation.
Hundreds of students, police, local authorities and students attended a memorial service for Chinese peacekeepers in Skun village on Tuesday morning. In addition to speeches by representatives of both sides, wreaths were laid at the Chinese military memorial there to forever remember the Chinese peacekeepers who sacrificed their lives in Cambodia.
