Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet Issues Sub-Decree on "Establishment of Committee for Promoting Private Sector Solutions"
(Phnom Penh): The Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, on April 2, 2024, issued a sub-decree on "Establishment of the Committee for the Promotion of Private Sector Solutions" under the Prime Minister's Office.
This confirmation was made by Samdech President at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the afternoon of April 2, 2024.
On that occasion, the President said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has established a National Commission to organize a new generation school program and will implement the first 50 schools, focusing on primary schools.
"Human education can not wait until the school is ready or until there is a new generation of school programs or until there is enough money, it requires innovation or innovation in the program," he said.
He added that we will test 50 more schools that will be implemented in the near future so that we can find the key link between normal schools, which is three and a half hours, extending two hours a day.
Samdech stated that in the future, when there is enough resources, enough funds, we will expand this new generation school program to reach all schools across the country.
PM Hun Sen Presents 10 Recommendations to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for the Basis and Inputs for Better Education Development in Cambodia (Phnom Penh) This 2024 provides 10 recommendations to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports as a basis and input for the development of education in Cambodia to better in line with the development of society.
This recommendation was made at the closing ceremony of the meeting of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the afternoon of April 2, 2024.
Samdech emphasized that in order to encourage and pay attention to this important work, Samdech would like to recommend 10 important recommendations for further implementation as follows:
First, continue to strengthen school governance and develop a stronger, proactive, modernized and responsive education system that responds to rapidly changing national and international facilities through the implementation of standard school standards and guarantees. Provide effective and quality education services with an equitable environment and enhance lifelong learning opportunities for all.
Second, continue to review, adjust and organize curriculum and extracurricular activities in accordance with the need to strengthen the knowledge, discipline, ethics and behavior of students, such as starting to practice throughout the day, and improve the textbook to be consistent with Developed countries.
Third, introduce new teaching methods, learning methods and assessment methods that can allow students to develop critical thinking skills, solve problems related to daily life, and apply scientific knowledge in daily life.
Fourth, continue to reform teacher training institutions and strengthen the qualifications of new teachers and improve teachers, improve teacher training to meet the "teacher professional standards" and provide regular professional development.
Fifth, continue to develop digital education by continuing to integrate digital technology into curricula at all levels, equip digital laboratories, connect to electricity and the Internet in educational institutions, improve the qualifications and digital capabilities of teachers, integrate the use of Technology into teaching and learning, improving digital content and establishing digital education centers and disseminating digital platforms more broadly and comprehensively.
6) Continue to improve health and hygiene in educational institutions, prepare measures to respond and participate in immediate prevention and increase education on safety, health, food safety, food safety, improve health infrastructure such as standard health rooms, green school environment, schools Clean, no litter, and promoting clean water and sanitation.
8) Continue to develop children and youth to have a sense of responsibility, believe in their abilities and adhere to positive actions in society, morality and living in good citizenship by inspiring the movement "good children, good students, good friends "Good Citizens", a youth volunteer program, and encouraging young people to help the community, as well as continuing to train young people in technical and soft skills to respond to job opportunities and the strength of social cells.
Ms. O Vandin: Less salt, less fat, less sugar, helps improve health, not prone to disease
(Stung Treng): Seeing the current social context where people are vulnerable to diabetes, nephropathy and high blood pressure, Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Public Health Officer, warned. Remind people to reduce their intake of salty, fatty and sugary foods and not to smoke.
Dr. O Vandin's remarks were made on the afternoon of April 1, 2024, during a meeting with civil servants and staff of Stung Treng Provincial Health Department to introduce and set out some work directions to strengthen the health system at the local level. High quality and trust from the people.
"Low salt, low fat, low sugar, which means that people want to reduce their diet, such as sugar, salt and fat from more to less and ban smoking," she said.
The senior official of the Ministry of Health also reminded the heads of the 20 centers that are operating to provide services to local people throughout Stung Treng province to manage the identity of patients in each locality and to disseminate as a group. To easily manage people with local diseases so that they can receive the most effective and reliable treatment services.
Ms. O Vandin urged the presidents of the 20 districts to continue to pay more attention to the provision of services to the people, setting up various locations to meet the needs in the centers that benefit the people, the preparation of uniforms according to Professionalism, as well as maintaining a clean environment and planting trees or flowers as an environmental attraction.
Speaking on the occasion of closing the meeting of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the afternoon of April 2, 2024, Samdech Hun Sen also wants teachers to be creative to provide more education to students. Samdech Thipadei advised not to impose obligations on parents to participate in the education promotion program.
On that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen announced 50 primary schools to strengthen education by extending the study time by 2 more hours. According to the statement of Samdech Hun Sen, every parent wants their children to get a good education.
Samdech Education President Hun Manet said, "Education is not a day or 12 years or 16 years, we need a lifetime of education, a lifetime of training, teachers must learn. Even I, the Prime Minister, study every day. "Learn about the problems that arise, learn to solve new problems, but what is fundamental to ensuring the quality of human resources is education, and especially at the grassroots level."
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia stressed that the most important factor to ensure human resources is to strengthen the foundation, and not just to kindergarten, primary and grade 12, that is, to continue to develop in higher education. Aims to contribute to ensuring competition. He added that Cambodia needs high-level, modern and modern human resources to compete with other countries.
In order to ensure the building of a foundation for the training of human resources to be of higher quality, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet has set a goal by announcing 50 primary schools to strengthen education by adding two more hours of study time. The prince emphasized that all parents want their children to get a good education.
He added that the school is a public service unit that is close to the people, the school must play a responsible role in teaching and learning and provide medical skills, fitness and behavior to all students. That requires schools to strengthen proactive governance and mobilize the participation of all stakeholders, especially the community and parents in the development of schools in all aspects in accordance with the standard school standards.
At the same time, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet supported the evaluation of the three levels of schools that the Ministry has selected and recognized as the 120 model schools in this initial phase in terms of recognizing the achievements of the schools and the academic results of the students. The joint efforts of the school management, teachers, students and families in the development of the school as a school ranked good public service unit, clean school, good director.
