Confucius Institute at National University of Battambang Celebrates International Chinese Language Day and Cambodia-China Cultural Exchange
(Battambang): The Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang on April 2, 2024 organized a celebration of the International Day of Chinese Language and Cambodian-Chinese Cultural Exchange under the chairmanship of Mr. Sok Khorn, Rector of the National University of Battambang and Mrs. Pak Somovityani era.
The event was also presided over by Mr. LU Qizhi, Chief of Consular Section of the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Siem Reap, Mr. Pheng Sethy, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, Major General So Kimpak, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division, Mr. Chhorn Chheang Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Battambang Province, as well as about 500 national and international guests.
Prof. I Yong Jung, Co-Director of the Confucius Institute on the Chinese side, made a report on the celebration of the International Chinese Language Day of the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang and the Confucius Institute Progress Ceremony.
"China and Cambodia all have a very long civilization and history, as well as great culture and art," he said. Cultural people-to-people exchanges are an important pillar of the Sino-Cambodian "Hexagonal Diamond" cooperation on the occasion of the China-Cambodia Cultural Exchange Program 2024.
The Institute has taken this opportunity to promote Chinese language and culture as a bridge through organizing more cultural exchange activities to strengthen international Chinese language education, promote cultural exchange and deepen international understanding, and establish The relationship between Chinese and Cambodian youth to strengthen the relationship between the Chinese and Cambodian people and increase civilization exchange and mutual learning.
He added that we all contribute to building Sino-Cambodian cooperation to share the future together in this new era.
We hope that more Cambodian friends can experience more about traditional Chinese culture and find out through this International Chinese Language Day event. We are willing to continue to work closely with all circles in Cambodia to write a new chapter on building a China-Cambodia community with a common destiny in the new era.
