BERLIN: Germany will support Ukraine by providing 180,000 artillery pieces to contribute to a Czech-led plan to buy ammunition to help Ukraine, the German Defense Ministry has announced. Worth 576 million euros ($ 618 million). This was released by the news agency Reutes on Tuesday, April 2, 2024.
The most urgent need for Ukraine in the more than two-year war with Russia is the growing number of artillery and shells, while both sides use these weapons to defend their respective positions. Most of the bodies are not very flexible along the front lines, which are about 1,000 kilometers long.
More and more countries are registering for the Czech Republic's initiative to buy hundreds of thousands of ammunition from outside Europe to help Ukraine. According to the German Defense Ministry, Berlin's share will be responsible for about 40 percent of the overall Czech plan.
