(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN-Cambodia Business Advisory Council, outlined the vision for the Cambodia-ASEAN Business Summit 2024: for regional cooperation and connectivity. To make Cambodia the heart of ASEAN's economic engine.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Duke Kith Meng attending the Cambodia-ASEAN Business Summit 2024 under the chairmanship of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of April 2, 2024, with the participation of senior officials. Royal Government of Cambodia, diplomats, development partners and about 450 national and international business leaders.
On that occasion, Duke Kith Meng stated that the efforts of all partners have made this business summit a success and promote stronger business relations across ASEAN countries.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng stated that the summit was organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce based on the success of the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit to be held in Phnom Penh in 2012 and 2022.
Duke Kith Meng stated that three main agendas will be discussed at this Cambodia-ASEAN Business Summit: 1: Promoting effective connectivity, 2: Supporting innovation and digitalization through Technology and 3: Ensure environmental growth that does not leave anyone.
"Cambodia is the center of ASEAN and is ready to become a strategic link for trade and cooperation in the ASEAN region," said Kith Meng.
The duke also pointed out that Cambodia has become an attractive regional gateway because: Open door methods and progress, 2. Rich resources, 3. Stable political environment, 4. Future-looking investment law, 5. Comprehensive tax incentives and 6. Extensive network of free trade agreements.
Duke Kith Meng also pointed out that "for businesses looking for production centers or business offices to serve the 2.5 billion people across ASEAN, Cambodia is the perfect place to do business."
In addition, Duke Kith Meng stated that Cambodia is firmly committed to conducting open trade and investment based on regulations and adhering to the principles of multilateralism and international agreements.
Duke Kith Meng affirmed that this commitment turns into a stable, predictable business environment and is backed by a government that adheres to transparency, governance and efficiency.
At the same time, Duke Kith Meng said that the Royal Government's open and digital dynamic policy creates a favorable environment for industrial innovation that promotes investment and trade.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng stated that under the visionary leadership of Samdech Thiptey Hun Manet, Cambodia has embarked on an ambitious journey in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy.
Duke Kith Meng said that this strategy serves as a roadmap for our overall success, with five key areas: growth, employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability.
Duke Kith Meng believes that this policy will continue to ensure economic growth, job creation, poverty reduction, strengthening governance and ensuring sustainable socio-economic development.
Therefore, we have laid the foundation for a bright future and made Cambodia a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050. This is an additional confirmation of Duke Kith Meng.
