(Phnom Penh): View photos of the Senate preparing for the opening ceremony of the first session of the 5th legislature under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia on April 3. 2024 at 8:00 in the morning.
According to the Constitution, the Senate is an organization that has legislative power and fulfills its duties as defined in the Constitution and the laws in force. The Senate has a maximum of half the total number of members of the National Assembly.
Two senators are appointed by the King. Two senators are elected by the National Assembly by a simple majority. The other senators are elected by universal suffrage (elected by the Commune / Sangkat Councilors and the National Assembly in office).
In the 5th Senate election, four political parties competed for 58 seats, of which the CPP won 55 seats and the Khmer Will won three. Separately, FUNCINPEC and the National Forces Party, which also contested, did not win seats.
The two senators appointed by the King are Princess Norodom Arunrasmey and Prince Sisowath Thomico. Meanwhile, the two senators who were elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote were Mr. Sok Isan and Mr. Heng Hak Lim.
