More than 800 cross-border swindlers arrested in joint Myanmar-China operation
The Chinese Embassy in Yangon announced on Monday that more than 800 suspected cross-border swindlers had been arrested in a joint operation between Myanmar and Chinese police. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, April 1, 2024.
Fraudulent operating sites are booming in Myanmar as people from China and most other countries are forced to work there to defraud their compatriots in an industry that analysts claim to have. Worth up to billions of dollars. Beijing has repeatedly called on Myanmar's military government to crack down on the scam.
In 2023, the UN Office for the Coordination of Human Rights claimed that at least 120,000 people were being held in custody at fraudulent locations in Myanmar. More than 40,000 people suspected of involvement in cyber-fraud in Myanmar were deported to China last year, according to Chinese state media.
