Samdech President Hun Manet calls on people to support the purchase of Cambodian products to use more to promote national prestige and national spirit
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, called on the people to support the purchase of Cambodian products to use as much as possible to promote national prestige and national spirit.
In addition, Samdech instructed the relevant ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels, as well as development partners, to promote the One Village, One Product movement to help develop Cambodian products.
His Excellency Hun Manet's appeal was made through a message celebrating the 7th National Day for the Promotion of the Use of Khmer Products on April 9, 2024 under the theme "Sustainable Production and Supply Market, One Village, One Product Movement".
"I would like to call on all citizens to actively support and encourage the purchase of Cambodian products to use as much as possible in order to promote national prestige and national spirit," said Hun Sen. "
"Let the relevant ministries and institutions, both national and sub-national, as well as development partners of national and international NGOs, the private sector continue to cooperate with the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product Movement to help develop Cambodian products. One village, one product to be more diverse and have trade potential in both national and international markets.
Hun Manet stated that the One Village, One Product movement, which is characterized by local mixed economic development, has helped to promote the production of raw materials, cultivation and animal husbandry, good processing, special environment, good quality and reasonable price. And have a sufficient amount to meet the needs of both domestic and foreign markets, achieve a scale economy, aiming to make the economic growth of every family lively and sustainable.
This movement still plays an important role and is more appropriate in the agenda of the policy of socio-economic development of Cambodia, because this concept originated in Cambodia a long time ago, the people of Cambodia as a nation has a tradition of knowledge and skills in the profession. Agriculture, animal husbandry and processing of these products in large numbers in different places.
It is noteworthy that in recent years, the promotion of one village, one product movement has achieved excellent results, leading to positive changes in Cambodian products, such as quality, hygiene standards. Packaging, especially the labeling of products as "Village 1 Product 1", which has 559 by 2023 across 25 provinces.
