Minister of Women's Affairs encourages women entrepreneurs to continue their efforts to develop their business and contribute to national economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ung Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, encouraged all women entrepreneurs to continue their efforts and be proud of themselves for the development of their business and to participate in economic recovery and to promote national economic growth.
This encouragement was made on the occasion of Dr. Ung Kantha Phavi's participation in the closing ceremony of the 2023 Annual Meeting and the direction for the year 2024 and the election of the Board of Directors of the 5th Mandate 2024-2027. Cambodian women at the Sokha Residence Hotel on March 31, 2024.
Dr. Ing Kantha Phavi stated that the Ministry of Women's Affairs is implementing a strategy to expand the functions of Women's Development Centers (WDCs) in the provinces in partnership with the private sector and relevant partners to support women start-ups, especially with micro and small businesses. Informal by community.
Dr. Ing Kantha Phavi added that the Women Entrepreneurship Development Center (WEDC) is starting to expand its partnership and coordinate with the private sector and relevant institutions to support women in small and medium enterprises.
In addition, Dr. Ing Kantha Phavi said that the Ministry also continues to support the Association of Women Entrepreneurs and other women entrepreneurs by participating in the mainstreaming of gender and the needs of women entrepreneurs, as well as your suggestions into the framework. Policies, policies and programs of ministries, institutions and relevant partners.
On that occasion, Ms. Dr. Ing Kantha Phavi highlighted some of the views and opinions as follows:
First, I would like to ask all women entrepreneurs to continue their hard work and be proud of themselves, which in the past and present, not only strives for the development of their business, but also a valuable part in participating in economic recovery and progress. To promote national economic growth.
Second, continue to develop skills and knowledge on the development of their business and individuals in charge, proactive, innovative and innovative to meet the needs and rapid development of society, especially the connection with technology and business solutions and solutions. Digital.
Third, let's all entrepreneurs strengthen and connect the network, which is an important force in supporting each other and expanding the scope of voice, and join the local business force to be a force to compete with External market as well. As the saying goes, "If you want to go fast, go alone, if you want to go far together."
Fourth, I would like to ask CWEA to continue to implement strategies to strengthen and expand its branches in the provinces in order to become a broader and more powerful force of women entrepreneurs.
Kampong Cham Provincial Administration announces the management of Phtea reservoir land in Khchao and Reay Pai communes, Kang Meas district.
(Kampong Cham): Recently, there has been a conflict among some people in Khchao and Reay Pai communes, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province, on the case of encroachment on land and water in the main river basin caused by the encroachment. Land use in the Mekong River Basin since after 1979 and continues to spread, there will be more cases of buying and selling.
In September 2023, the Kang Meas District Administration issued a directive stating that the Mekong River Basin is a public property of the state and would not allow or recognize the encroachment on land at the bottom of the Twin Basin. .
In response to this case, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration would like to reiterate that the Mekong River Basin is a state property that must be preserved for the public benefit of the people living in the surrounding area. In this regard, the provincial administration would like to introduce the following urgent measures aimed at managing the Mekong Basin:
* Second, it is strictly forbidden for new encroachment to occupy or enjoy the land of the reservoir further, and it is not allowed to dig or modify the land at the bottom of the reservoir without permission. The area at the bottom of the basin that the people have encroached upon and enjoyed in the past and are not allowed to buy, sell or transfer ownership will be returned to the state unconditionally when it no longer needs to continue to enjoy or When the state needs to develop.
