* Second: Report on the work of the National Assembly between the first and second sessions of the National Assembly from January 1 to March 11, 2024.
The National Assembly convenes normally twice a year and each session lasts at least three months. Between each session of the National Assembly, the National Assembly actively fulfills its functions, including legislative functions, "drafting and passing laws", monitoring the implementation of laws and policies, and the function of representing the nation and its people in accordance with the Constitution and Internal Rules of the National Assembly.
