(Phnom Penh): A former opposition leader who had been involved in politics with Sam Rainsy saw the "Khmer Movement for Democracy" formed by Sam Rainsy and Mu Sochua as a mere event. But it did not move forward, that is, it exploded and calmed down like the previous movement.
Opposition groups in exile abroad, escaping the Cambodian legal trap led by Sam Rainsy, who are considered traitors, are forming a new political movement, the Khmer Movement for Democracy. The movement, led by Mu Sochua, has announced its intention to mobilize Democrats against the Royal Government of Cambodia.
San Sang, a Khmer Kampuchea Krom-born politician who has been in politics with Sam Rainsy since 1998, saw that the "Khmer Movement for Democracy" was not moving forward.
Mr. San Sang highlighted that since 2017, after the CNRP emerged, Mr. Rainsy and opposition politicians have formed several movements that are considered political resistance movements. But all those movements formed one, cooked, faded and calmed down, to no avail.
San Sang, a former opposition leader based in the United States, also attended a rally of former opposition leaders attended by Sam Rainsy in Long Beach on March 24, 2024. .
Meanwhile, some observers of the opposition see the formation of the "Khmer Movement for Democracy" in addition to creating an event to attract attention and that could also be a way to make money from supporters.
In fact, on the day of the rally, Mu Sochua, the movement's president, announced that her supporters would contribute $ 1 or more to the fund. Minister of Labor and Governor of Por Senchey District organized a solidarity meal with factory administration and staff delegates from nearly 100 factories in Por Senchey District
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Mr. Sak Chankanharith, Governor of Por Senchey District, on the night of March 30, 2024, yesterday organized a solidarity meal with the factory administration and a delegation of nearly 1,000 employees from 87 factories in Po Sen Chey district.
