Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Dr. Yong Pov: The President's announcement that Cambodia will register "Sankranti in Cambodia" next year is the end of the misconception that Cambodia can not use the word "Sankranti"
(Phnom Penh): The announcement by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen, that Cambodia is preparing to register the document "Sankranti in Cambodia" as a UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity next year is the end of the misunderstanding that Cambodia can no longer use the word Sankranti. This is according to Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of March 31, 2024.
Along with the announcement, on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the stupa and achievements at Wat Mony Ratanaream in Sangkat Roleap, Pursat City, Pursat Province, Samdech Hun Sen also claimed that Cambodia is ready to list intangible cultural heritage in the list of Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Seven more UNESCO in a row.
According to Dr. Yong Pov, Sankranti is a Khmer cultural heritage for thousands of years and no one can take it because it is ours for a long time. It infects each other, even on New Year's Day. The Khmer have Sankranti of the Khmer way.
Dr. Yong Pov stated, "The word Sankranti is inscribed on the wall of K17, please verify. The announcement of the Prime Minister this morning is the end of the confusion that is often distorted on social media. Please be careful with well-known commentators before interpreting.
At the same time, Dr. believes that the competent authorities such as the Ministry of Education, the Ministry of Culture and the Ministry of Information should further explain to the people to understand, especially should make information and videos not only Sankranti but other cultural assets. He said that in the past he saw the explanation, but if he did not reach out to the people, he would still be confused.
At the same time, Dr. Yong Pov urges the land monitoring authorities to organize Sankranti well in our Khmer way, in our cultural way. "This is why he recently reacted to playing water polo in the Thai culture."
So far, 10 Cambodian cultural properties have been inscribed on the World Heritage List, of which 4 are tangible and 6 are intangible. Intangible heritage sites include Angkor Archaeological Park, Preah Vihear Temple, Sambor Prei Kuk and Koh Ker. Intangible heritage includes royal dances, large-scale shadow puppetry, tug-of-war, long chapei, long puppet, Wat Svay Andet, and bokator.
According to the group leader, the spokesperson for the Intangible Heritage List, which is already registered and ready to be registered in Cambodia, includes:
* Documents to be prepared for future registration:
1: The krama that we have already submitted the technical documents can be checked and registered in 2024.
2: Khmer weddings (including traditional wedding dresses) The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts is preparing the registration documents, which we hope to send to UNESCO by the end of March 2024, if there are no technical problems. One will be completed by the end of 2025.3: Sankranta in Cambodia, if necessary, we can prepare the application for registration by March 2025 and the registration will be by the end of 2026.
Please be informed that the statement made by Samdech Hun Sen was made after a case was mentioned on social media that Thailand had registered the word "Sankranti in Thailand", making it impossible for Cambodia to use this word anymore. In addition, some provinces, such as Svay Rieng, have decided not to hold Sankranti but to hold concerts.
