Police crack down on drug offenses, arrest 4 Vietnamese nationals, seize more than 3 kg of drugs and nearly 10 kg of chemical compounds
(Phnom Penh): Anti-Drug Department cracked down on drug processing, storage and trafficking in Phnom Penh, arrested 4 Vietnamese suspects, confiscated more than 3 kg of drugs and nearly 10 kg of chemicals .
The crackdown was carried out on the orders of General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner General, and under the command of Lt. Gen. Bun Pa Marilux, Lt. Gen. Prum Santhor, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, and under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Kheung Sarath, Director of the Anti-Drug Department. .
A senior police officer of the Anti-Drug Department confirmed on March 31, 2024 that on March 29, 2024 at 22:30, the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department cooperated with the force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. Phnom Penh, led by Mr. Kim Hong San, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, cracked down on points along Street 432, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 2, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh.
As a result, the specialized force arrested 4 perpetrators: Nguyen Cao Yuy, male, Vietnamese, born in 1996, Nguyen Mai Song Hien, male, Vietnamese, born in 2002, Nguyen Huy Yi, male, Vietnamese, born in 1990, And Nguyen Yi Tam, male, Vietnamese, born in 1995.
Currently, the four perpetrators and exhibits have been sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action and continue to search for the mastermind and other relevant people to be punished according to the law.
Notably, the Anti-Drug Department has recently cracked down on a number of major offenses involving criminals transporting consignment goods in large quantities in large quantities, arresting and sending offenders. To be sentenced in court.
Banking Association of Cambodia: Cambodia becomes one of the countries with the highest digital payments in the world
(Phnom Penh): In its press release on March 31, 2024, the Banking Association of Cambodia stated that Cambodia has become one of the countries in the world with the highest digital payments. Compared to gross domestic product (GDP).
The rise of the Banking Association of Cambodia after some media outlets recently reported that the digital payment behavior of the Cambodian people has decreased significantly and cash payments have increased by Excerpted from a study of consumer payment behavior conducted by CLEAR M&C Saatchi from October to November 2023.
The Banking Association of Cambodia states that the news articles and reports do not reflect the current use of digital technology and digital trends in Cambodia.
In fact, there has been significant progress in the capture and use of digital systems by consumers in Cambodia in recent years, and this growth has been further accelerated during and after the outbreak of Kovid. 19 With investments in digital payment platforms and other digital infrastructure by the National Bank of Cambodia, relevant ministries and other stakeholders, including banking and financial institutions.
The Banking Association of Cambodia strongly believes that digital payments and technology will remain a core priority of the banking sector, so banking and financial institutions will continue to invest in mobile banking and payment platforms and digital services to serve the market. Make digital banking easier, more affordable, and more secure.
The Association and its members will continue to support the National Bank of Cambodia and the Royal Government of Cambodia in facilitating and developing further digital ecosystems and innovations both in the banking sector and beyond the banking sector, as set out in the Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework 2021. 2035 of Cambodia.
The Banking Association of Cambodia elects the new Chairman of the Board, Mr. Rath Sophoan!
(Phnom Penh): The Banking Association of Cambodia on March 31, 2024 issued a press release on the Annual General Meeting and the election of the new Board of Directors of the Association for the mandate 2024-2025.
In addition to the election of the new Banking Council, the Banking Association of Cambodia also presented its members with the 2023 Annual Report and Financial Report, as well as the 2024 Budget Plan.
Mr. Raymond Sia, former President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, thanked all the members of the Council and the Secretariat Working Group and appreciated the contribution and dedication in supporting the members and the banking sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Rath Sophoan, newly elected President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, thanked the former Chairman and all the members of the Board for their energetic and strong leadership over the past 2 years and congratulated the team. A new advisor to the Banking Association of Cambodia.
Mr. Rath Sophoan added that he is honored to serve the banking sector and its members. With the new councilors, he and the new councilors will lead the association to the next level, outlining his vision and four pillars.
First, determine the structure of good governance and function and functioning of the Banking Association in Cambodia.
Second, to advise on the management and operation of the bank responsibly and based on values to increase public trust, promote the financial environment, and enhance the strength and growth of the banking sector to support economic growth. .
Third, to promote a culture of continuing education for bankers and to enhance the ability of bankers in technical skills, professional excellence and ethical leadership.
Fourth, to establish more cooperation in the banking ecosystem to increase the potential of the banking sector to further increase the potential of the banking sector to contribute to national economic growth and national prosperity. Schools and education come to the local level, please send all your children to school.
