Canada sends troops to help train Caribbean forces for Haiti mission
In 2023, Kenya announced that it would lead a coalition force set up to help Haitian police fight powerful gangs as violence escalated. Ignite the humanitarian crisis there. However, the initiative has stalled in Kenyan courts since then, making it impossible for the mission to begin yet.
The Canadian Defense Ministry said in a statement that the Canadian troops from Quebec, a predominantly French-speaking province, would provide training in core peacekeeping and life-saving skills. French is one of the two official languages of Haiti.
The Canadian army will stay in Jamaica for one month as a first step and will help train about 330 troops from Jamaica, Belize and the Bahamas. In February, Canada announced it would provide C $ 80.5 million to support the launch of a Kenyan-led Haitian mission.
