JAKARTA: A major fire broke out at an ammunition depot near Jakarta, but it was successfully extinguished as the military inspected the surrounding area to collect items, an Indonesian military official said. Others may have been blown away by the explosion during the fire. This was released by Reuters on Sunday, March 31, 2024.
The blaze broke out on Saturday at a military ammunition depot in Bogor, on the outskirts of Jakarta, at around 6:30 p.m. It also triggered a series of explosions, with the military claiming no one was killed or injured.
