The 15th Anniversary Celebration was held to celebrate the efforts of the Association for the past 15 years, with the Association making significant contributions to the development of the ecosystem, entrepreneurship, business policy, investment and promoting the growth of entrepreneurs and micro-enterprises. And medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), which are the backbone of the Cambodian economy.
For more than a decade, the Association has played an important role in partnering with development partners, the Royal Government, civil society and the private sector directly in the development of business and most actively contributing to the promotion of Cambodian business to be more capable and competitive. In the field of regional and international business.
The association was established in September 2009 by a group of young entrepreneurs from various business sectors with the mission of working in partnership with relevant institutions to empower young entrepreneurs, empower entrepreneurs and youth through the establishment of Forum to network entrepreneurs, share business learning and create business opportunities to increase productivity, job creation, economic development and capacity building for the next generation for Cambodia.
Mr. Oknha Pech Bolen stated that currently the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association has more than 600 members, representing about 1,800 companies in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kratie and Sihanoukville. The Kampot-Kep branch is preparing to open in the near future, and the association is organizing branches in Koh Kong, Kampong Speu and Pursat provinces in 2024.
The Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association aims to open branches in all capitals and provinces by the end of 2026 to mobilize young entrepreneurs across the country to participate as economic operators, develop entrepreneurship and promote the national economy.
In addition, the association also cooperates with the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, the Association of Cambodian Banks, the Association of Cambodian Microfinance, investment partners and various financial institutions to promote and train entrepreneurs on knowledge and financial management, joint ventures, access to capital. From the bank, knowledge of the stock market and preparation for development in the stock market.
