Gaza: A famine is not just a risk, but it is likely to occur in some parts of the northern Gaza Strip, a senior State Department official said Friday, adding that the shortage of trucks is a major threat. An obstacle to providing more aid to densely populated areas besieged by Israeli troops. This is according to the release by Reuters on March 29, 2024.
"While we can confidently say that famine is a serious concern in southern and central Gaza, it has not yet happened," the official told Reuters on condition of anonymity. "North Gaza is a risk and is likely to occur in some areas as well."
Earlier this month, the UN-backed World Food Security Agency warned of possible famine in northern Gaza in May and spread across the region in July.
The Food Security Stage Report (IPC) says malnutrition and food insecurity in northern Gaza could exceed famine and starvation-related deaths are likely soon.
