Cambodian diplomat urges officials to monitor, analyze and assess regional and global situation
(Phnom Penh): As the world situation becomes more complex, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, urges Foreign Ministry officials to work hard to analyze and evaluate the regional and global situation, as well as strengthen institutional capacity for change. Turn challenges into opportunities and maximize core interests for the nation.
The launch took place at the opening ceremony of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on March 28, 2024.
Currently, the regional and international situation is difficult to predict, including the crisis in Myanmar, the South China Sea issue, the situation on the Korean Peninsula, the war in Ukraine, the Middle East issue, the tension of geopolitical competition, as well as other traditional and non-traditional security issues. Climate change, natural disasters, food security and energy.
The Deputy Prime Minister considered that these issues are still urgent issues that need to be addressed together, while the global economic and financial situation remains fragile despite the gradual recovery.
"In the context of the above and in order to continue to successfully implement foreign policy and independent diplomatic work based on the law, His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister urges all government officials to work hard to monitor, analyze and evaluate the regional and global situation, as well as strengthen "Institutional capacity aims to turn challenges into opportunities and maximize core interests for the nation." This was confirmed by the head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps.
With this situation, the Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that the work that the Ministry will continue to do is to continue to build professional capacity and train human resources, especially in foreign affairs and international relations, so that diplomats will be more loyal to the nation. Professional and acquire enough new skills, have high skills, ability, agility, flexibility and become a leading fighter to protect the interests of the nation and the people.
"This reform work is in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy, which continues to prioritize" people "as one of the five key priorities for" promoting economic growth, creating jobs, ensuring equity, increasing efficiency and sustainability, "he said. "Sustainability."
