Ministry of Economy: Fuel prices seem to be improving, not yet alarmingly high
The Ministry of Economy stated that "the increase in domestic fuel prices in February 2024 is a consequence of the increase in crude oil prices in the international market, however, the current increase in fuel prices seems to be good and has not yet risen." High to alarming levels. "As a result, in the first two months of 2024, the average daily gasoline and diesel prices decreased by 2.1% and 6.6%, respectively, compared to the same period in 2023."
In 2024, international crude oil prices are likely to rise for two consecutive months, which may be due to problems with global crude oil supply, including:
1: Reducing OPEC crude oil supply. 2. Continuing attacks in the Red Sea. 3. Tensions in the Middle East. 4. Explosion at an oil refinery in Russia's Brainsk province. Attack from Ukraine.
