According to a press release from the National Bank of Cambodia, "The National Bank of Cambodia would like to clarify the progress of payments in Cambodia that in recent years, digital payment transactions in Cambodia have increased rapidly, through the use of "Credit cards, debit cards, remittances and, in particular, scratch code payments for payments ranging from small to large stores, covering almost everywhere across the country."
This development is due to the continuous deployment of modern payment systems, allowing cross-institutional payments, the development of apps for Q-code payments, the development of Q-code standards, etc., which facilitates secure and fast digital payments, especially in While the use of smartphones has increased to more than 19 million units, more than the total population of Cambodia more than 16 million.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia has been actively promoting digital payments through various initiatives and collaborations with financial institutions, stakeholders and countries in the region and the world.
With the implementation of these policies, overseas digital payments have also increased, such as in Thailand, Vietnam and Laos, where Cambodians can pay at stores in these countries from their riel accounts.
At the same time, international customers are also using more digital payments through QRC due to efforts to connect the payment system with more and more countries in the region.
