Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leads a Delegation to Return to Cambodia Safely (Video inside) (China, Hainan): At more than 11 am on Friday, March 29, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council The King led a delegation to return to Cambodia safely after completing a mission in Hainan Province, China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to leave Cambodia on March 26, 2024 to attend the annual conference of the Boao Forum for Asia at the invitation of Secretary-General of the Boao Forum for Asia.
The conference focused on issues facing Asia and promoting international cooperation. At the opening ceremony of the conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave a keynote address.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that with the presence of more than 20 years ago, the Boao Forum for Asia has been recognized as an influential forum for setting regional and global agendas, bringing voice and wisdom. Asia in tackling difficult challenges in its efforts to build a world that is peaceful and better for all.
In front of thousands of participants, Samdech Techo Hun Sen raised issues that are happening in the world, causing serious consequences for innocent civilians as well as the economy and international trade. The issues he highlighted include the fact that the war in Ukraine has entered its third year and, unfortunately, has not yet seen the light of peace. The war between Israel and Hamas continues to cause many deaths and injuries.
Samdech Techo expressed satisfaction and pleasure at China's active cross-border mediation efforts to find a ceasefire in Ukraine. Samdech Techo expressed confidence that such actions would be a good example for other responsible actors of the international community in speeding up negotiations and achieving a ceasefire in Ukraine, as well as In other parts of the world that have been devastated by war and conflict.
Samdech Techo also noted that Asia also has many triggers that could erupt into conflict if Asian leaders do not consult and communicate with each other to resolve differences in a meaningful and responsible manner. Yes.
With these issues in mind, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the common responsibility of countries in Asia is to maintain peace and security in the region to ensure that the results of poverty reduction do not return. Post-assurance promotes better future development for common prosperity.
He stressed that it must be recognized that China's model of growth and development has allowed other countries to prosper together, not abandon other countries for their own growth.
In addition to attending the conference during his three-day working visit to China, Hun Sen also visited the Institute of Tropical Agriculture and the International Space City in Wenchang, Hainan Province, China.
