Announcing the composition of the Royal Government working group to visit 8 communes of Tang Kork district, the Royal Government representatives introduced 6 main working directions to serve the people well
(Kampong Thom): In the ceremony of announcing the composition of the Royal Government Working Group to visit 8 communes of Taing Kork District and the Secretariat of the Royal Government Working Group to visit Taing Kork District, representatives of the Royal Government introduced 6 main working directions to become Government Officers in Serving the people well.
The ceremony was held on the morning of March 29, 2024 at Tang Kork District Hall, Kampong Thom Province, presided over by Mr. Chheang Vannarith, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Tang Kork District, with the participation of the Chairman, Deputy Chairman. About 365 members of the Royal Government's working group visited the eight communes of Tang Kork district, civil servants and members of the Armed Forces.
Mr. Chheang Vannarith stated that with the attention of the Head of the Royal Government led by Samdech Moha Bovathipati Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the high level of trust from Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Head of the Royal Government Working Group to Kampong Thom Province. Assign local government working groups in Tang Kork district and 8 communes of Tang Kork district to help solve the challenges and concerns of local people.
Mr. Chheang Vannarith outlined the main work directions as follows:
1: The Royal Government working group visited all villages, communes of Taing Kork district to cooperate and work together with high will, responsibility and ownership
2. Encourage relevant ministries and institutions at the sub-national level to participate in solving challenges, especially land issues with transparency, accountability and ownership.
3. Urge district, commune and competent administrations at all levels to provide more efficient, quality and environmentally friendly public services.
4. Urge the district, commune and competent administrations to continue to promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats in order to continue to solve inactivity such as theft, gambling, drugs, gangs, land disputes, and fraud through information technology.
5: Promote the development of necessary physical infrastructure to serve the economic activities and livelihoods of local people
6. Promote fundraising and technical assistance from relevant ministries and institutions, development partners, NGOs, civil society and philanthropists.
At the same time, the Secretary of State also introduced the working mechanism of the Royal Government working group to visit all 8 districts and communes of Taing Kork district in accordance with the instruction No. 04 Sann dated 30 November 2023 of the Royal Government.
He also instructed all participants to work together as a force in the development of Tang Kork district from the time of declaring this composition to be accurate and fair to the people in the commune.
It should be noted that the composition of the Royal Government Working Group visited 8 communes of Tang Kork District and the Secretariat of the Royal Government Working Group visited Tang Kork District, a total of 350 people.
