Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 caused the deepest crisis in Russia's relations with the West since the 1962 Cuban Missile Crisis.
Putin told Russian air force pilots that the US-led military alliance had extended eastward toward Russia since the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, but Moscow had no plans to attack NATO member states. No.
The Kremlin, which has accused the United States of fighting Russia through its support for Ukraine, both militarily and militarily, has said relations with Washington may not be worse.
In response to questions about F-16 fighter jets that the West has promised to send to Ukraine, Putin said the planes would not change the situation in Ukraine.
"F-16s can also carry nuclear weapons," he said. "And of course, if they are used from airports in third countries, they become a legal destination for us, regardless of where they are located."
Countries such as Belgium, Denmark, Norway and the Netherlands have pledged to donate F-16s to Ukraine. Other allied countries have also pledged to help train Ukrainian pilots in the use of the aircraft.
Dr. Ly Thuch Chairs the Third Meeting of the Coordinating Committee for the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use of Anti-Personnel Mines
The four commissions are: (1) the Commission for the Implementation of Article 5: Anti-Personnel Mine Action, (2) the Compliance Committee, (3) the Victim Support Commission, and (4) the Commission for Cooperation and Assistance and Preparation. Strategies to promote the globalization of the Convention, as well as review the financial situation to support the Ottawa Convention Support Unit (ISU).
At the same time, the meeting discussed important issues, including the submission of the report of the States Parties concerned and the implementation of Article 7 (Transparency Measures) and Article 9 (National Implementation Measures), the implementation of Article 5 (Mine Clearance), Victim Relief. Disasters and the promotion of cooperation and assistance.
The outcome of the meeting will be considered and used as an "essential entry point for the June 2024 Transitional Meeting of the Convention and in preparation for the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on a Mine-Free World in November 2024 of the Ottawa Convention to achieve Cambodia's priority goals.
The Meeting reminded the Commission to monitor and resolve any State Party that fails to submit the Article 7 Report (Transparency of the Convention), and shall do its utmost to promote the reporting of Article 7 this year. The meeting will continue to work with these States Parties to suggest steps that States Parties can take to ensure that the Convention remains strong and effective.
