The following is the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration: As of February 2024, loans used in tourism are more than 2.68 billion USD.
(Phnom Penh): As of February 2024, $ 2.68 billion in loans have been used in tourism across the country to support local tourism businesses. This is according to Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Chief Executive Officer of KREDIT Bourro Cambodia, who held a knowledge sharing workshop on credit information sharing system for the growth of small and medium enterprises in the tourism sector in Siem Reap.
Mr. Oeur Sothearoth said that of the $ 2.68 million loan, 12.68% of the tourism loan was given to people in Siem Reap who applied for the loan.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association, said that the tourism sector plays an important role in restoring the economic growth of Siem Reap, as well as throughout Cambodia.
"We need to boost our cooperation with the financial sector, business associations, associations and the government to create a strong package that can achieve growth in tourism in line with government policy," he added.
Financing plays an important role in helping businesses in the tourism sector to accelerate growth and recovery after the recession after the Kovita 19 pandemic. In the context of announcing a $ 50 million loan package from the Cambodian government to small and medium-sized tourism enterprises in Siem Reap, this workshop aims to focus on factors that enable businesses to better prepare for a loan.
