Thirteen Air Force pilots receive training on international flight procedures
(Phnom Penh): Thirteen pilots of the Air Force Command received training on international flight procedures at the National Institute of Civil Aviation, an initiative of General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander of the Air Force.
The opening ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Ly Sovannarith, Secretary of State, on behalf of Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, on March 28, 2024 at the National Institute of Civil Aviation.
Mr. Ly Sovannarith praised and appreciated the members of the Committee for Trainings and Mr. Lim Kao, Director of the National Institute of Civil Aviation, who held a research meeting to be able to organize this training to help strengthen the capacity of the pilots of Air Force Command.
Mr. Ly Sovannarith stated that this course is designed and designed to provide the pilots of the Air Force Command with the necessary information and capabilities for searching and flying to or through other countries safely and securely. .
In addition, he emphasized that this course is not used to meet the conditions of flight within the civil framework, unless there is a request to complete all the requirements and in accordance with the procedures of civil traffic law. National and international.
