(Battambang): Six gunmen opened fire on a villager's house in the center of Battambang city, Battambang province. The incident happened at midnight on March 28, 2024, but the owner was not aware of this, causing a surprise in the morning and the authorities intervened to investigate.
Keo Dang, a 41-year-old homeowner who sells mobile phones and electronics, said he was unaware when gunmen opened fire on his home, saying he and his family were asleep. In the room. In the morning, he came down to open the door of the house to sell as usual, suddenly found 6 leaks in the door, while that night he did not hear the sound of gunfire.
After seeing such bullet holes, he also reported to the local authorities to intervene and investigate.
At the scene, police found six bullet holes and three bullet holes, but no shell casings. Presumably, the gunman was likely armed with a shotgun, leaving no ammunition.
Authorities claimed that the shooting was suspected to be out of resentment, and that this was a warning shot to the victims, however, the force is still investigating and investigating.
