Mr. Khim Finang added that the team is now trying to connect the market to the community, with two companies waiting to sign a contract to buy cashew nuts directly from the community at a price higher than the market. According to the average yield for this year, the community can harvest about 200 tons, a number that both companies can guarantee to buy at once.
According to Khim Finang, this group of farmers is an old member of the existing community out of a total of 189 families with nearly 600 hectares of cultivated land.
He hopes that with the start-up in the form of a modern agricultural community, combined with other benefits such as foreclosure, low-interest unsecured loans and technical support for farmers in Sala Visay commune. Will consider joining the community in the future as well.
In the past, Mr. Khim Finang encouraged smallholder cashew growers to form a "modern farming community", which is understood to be a "modern farming community" that will balance the small-scale cashew farming business of farmers. By standard and profitable.
Mr. Khim Finang explained that some cashew growers with small plots of land and family plantations could face losses because most of them were technically weak, costly, low yielding and had high yields. Lack of capital forced them to accept loans to buy high-interest inputs.
