(Phnom Penh): Dr. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that the problem of drug use and e-cigarette flow is still a serious challenge and an obstacle to affect the development of children's fitness. Young people and the problem that affects the family economy and the national economy as a whole.
Dr. Soeur Socheata said, "In terms of technical work, each school has really worked hard and achieved satisfactory results. Along with the results, we also see many problems that we think. "The acute challenge and obstacle to the development of children's fitness, the fitness of our young people is the flow and use of drugs, e-cigarettes."
