Ms. Soeur Socheata asserted that without the participation of all of us, our society would be able to face many challenges related to social order, safety and security, in addition to the economic problems of the family. And the national economy as a whole, in fact, the Royal Government has spent a lot of money on social protection to maintain the politeness of the people, which has hindered the development in many other areas as well.
The Australian Ambassador believes that under the leadership of Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, the Ministry of Interior will continue to achieve even greater achievements.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 27, 2024, Mr. Justin Whyatt, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, congratulated Mr. Abhisit Bandith, who has been appointed by the Royal Government as the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, and believes that the Ministry of Interior will continue to achieve even greater achievements.
During the meeting, Dr. Sar Sokha thanked and warmly welcomed the Australian Ambassador Justin Whyatt and his colleagues, considering the meeting as a demonstration of their efforts to further their work. Cooperation between the Government of Australia and the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia now and in the future.
The head of the Cambodian Ministry of Interior also congratulated the Australian Government on hosting the ASEAN-Australia Special Summit, as well as the celebration of the 50th anniversary of ASEAN-Australia relations in Melbourne in early March 2024, as well as the Narrow and other bilateral, with the successful participation of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Before concluding, Abhisit expressed hope that through this mission, cooperation between the two countries would be continuously strengthened, both now and in the future, and that he was confident that Australia would continue to provide joint assistance. Provide technical assistance, materials and training to law enforcement officers on the fight against transnational crime and on public administration reform, decentralization and deconcentration reform.
Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and Ministry of Labor Sign MoU to Promote Vocational and Technical Training for Youth
(Phnom Penh): The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia was presided over by Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training. Colleagues at Mani Center, The Kampus Building, on the afternoon of March 26, 2024.
On that occasion, Mr. HUN Many thanked the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training for choosing the CPPCC. To promote the dissemination of vocational and technical training to young people and to register for job search and career guidance.
At the same time, Mr. Heng Sour stated that this cooperation with the CPPCC was due to the scope of the CPPCC structure. Which is comprehensive and widespread throughout the country, which can provide high results in promoting the promotion of vocational and technical training programs to the members of the CPPCC. And young people in general to have more potential.
The Minister considered that this Memorandum will facilitate the members of the CPPCC. Young people in general register for a job after receiving information about job opportunities of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
Please be informed that the CPPCC Aims to contribute to the development of professional employment and digital economy for a sustainable future, especially to support vocational training and provide employment services and labor market information more widely to ensure that young people across the capital, provinces at all skill levels can Receive information related to the field of employment and have the opportunity to attend various training courses.
Please be informed that the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia was made for the purpose of:
* This cooperation will co-organize the establishment of a career and employment office at the CPPCC headquarters. All provincial capitals with the permission of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to place the mark at the appropriate location
* Disseminate vocational and technical training programs to CPC members and young people in general, especially young people from poor and vulnerable families, and facilitate digital enrollment of young people. Members of the CPPCC General Youth and Youth
* Facilitate job search registration and career guidance, especially after receiving professional training from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training
Disseminate information on the job opportunities needed to the target youth and prepare monthly, quarterly, semi-annual and annual job summary reports at the CPPCC headquarters. Relevant and sent to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Israel continues to bomb Gaza and fight Hamas around hospitals despite UN Security Council call for ceasefire
(Gaza) - The Israeli military on Wednesday (March 27) continued to drop bombs on the besieged Gaza Strip and fight Hamas around several hospitals, despite a UN Security Council call for a ceasefire. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on March 27, 2024.
Negotiations in Qatar to reach a ceasefire and a hostage release agreement involving US and Egyptian mediators have so far yielded no results as Israel and the Palestinian movement have blamed it. Each other.
Israel on Wednesday again struck Gaza and Rafah with flames of up to 1.5 million people, most of them refugees from the war.
Hamas-controlled Gaza Health Ministry said 66 people had been killed in shelling and fighting overnight. Israeli forces also clashed with gunmen in and around three hospitals in Gaza City, raising fears among patients, medical staff and refugees inside.
Earlier this week, the UN Security Council called for an immediate ceasefire between Israel and the Palestinian militant group Hamas and for the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages after the United States. Abstain.
Samdech Manet strives to persuade South Korean investors to seize investment opportunities in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Attracting foreign investors to invest in Cambodia is the great intention of Samdech Hun Sen Manet as a person responsible for the fate of the nation and the people. Everywhere, anytime, Samdech Hun Sen is not afraid to ask foreign investors to invest in Cambodia.
For Samdech President Hun Manet, meeting with South Korean giant investors now is a golden opportunity for Samdech to persuade them to invest in Cambodia or expand their investment in Cambodia. He made efforts to highlight the potential as well as the many reasons why South Korean investors should invest or expand their investment in Cambodia.
He also stressed that by ensuring and maintaining political peace and stability, Cambodia can achieve strong and resilient economic growth of around 7% per annum for more than two decades. So far. After the effects of Kovid-19, the Cambodian economy has been resilient and is confident that the economy will grow at around 6.6 percent in 2024.
The Prime Minister briefed the delegation on policies to attract as well as encourage investors in Cambodia through the implementation of the Law on Investment in Cambodia, as well as the introduction of concrete policies to support the investment climate and sustainability. Cambodia's competition in the region and globally.
He reiterated that the Royal Government of Cambodia remains open to investment from all countries based on flexibility and realism and policy in response to and addressing the challenges of existing investors. Business in Cambodia to maintain the investment climate as well as remain competitive in order to retain existing investors and attract more new investors to Cambodia.
The South Korean delegation thanked Prime Minister Hun Manet for allowing the Korean delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss work. The delegation praised and appreciated Cambodia's rapid progress, especially in terms of infrastructure and Cambodia's successful fulfillment of its role in the international arena, such as its chairmanship of ASEAN and related summits in 2022.
The Chairman and members of the delegation highly appreciated and appreciated Cambodia's economic growth and also expressed their intention to strengthen and expand cooperation on promoting investment, trade and economy in accordance with the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement. (CKFTA) entered into force. Through this free trade agreement, the trade volume between the two countries has increased significantly.
The delegation also pledged to continue to strengthen and expand cooperation as well as further investment in a number of areas, including education, tourism, vocational training, agriculture, energy, electronics, automobiles and components, food services and journalism in Cambodia. Also.
Please note that South Korea is a big market of Cambodia. In 2023, Cambodia exported products to the Korean market under the Free Trade Agreement in the amount of 26.21 million US dollars, an increase of 2048 percent compared to 2022, which amounted to 1.22 million US dollars.
According to a report by the Council for the Development of Cambodia, from 1994 to early 2024, there were 228 South Korean investment projects in Cambodia with an investment of more than 5 billion US dollars. Cambodian Red Cross Receives SIPCO
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, received Mr. Hang Andong, President of SIPCO and a delegation from the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development to pay a courtesy call on SIPCO. Vietnam with the Cambodian Red Cross. This meeting was held at the headquarters of the Cambodian Red Cross on March 27, 2024.
On that occasion, Mr. Hang Andong confirmed the intention of the company that wants to cooperate with the Cambodian Red Cross by providing water filters and water treatment stations in schools or pump wells to people in Regional areas face water shortages.
The First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross expressed her happiness and emphasized that the Cambodian Red Cross provided clean water wells, hand washing facilities and toilets to students and residents. In a series of remote areas already.
In response to the above request of SIPCO, the Cambodian Red Cross will request the permission from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, together with the study with the 25 branches in the capital and provinces to examine the possibility of any branch to implement the above project. .
At the same time, she informed the delegation about the work activities of the Cambodian Red Cross in the past, especially related to the theme of the celebration of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024, which the Cambodian Red Cross. Committed to working with the Royal Government and all stakeholders to make the community healthy and resilient to the weather.
