Regarding the drug action, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated that if the civil servants of the Armed Forces are the servants of the people, if they do not clean themselves, what do the people expect?
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet said that after the formation of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate in just a few months, professional officers launched a large-scale operation to crack down on drug offenses by confiscating drugs and chemicals. Tons as well as detaining many people.
Samdech Manet said that the drug problem exists in every country, even in countries where there are strict laws where traffickers are severely punished until they are executed, there is also a drug problem. The superpowers, which spend millions of dollars a year, still face this problem.
Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet added that in the past, the armed forces have been applied, including the police and the army, and from now on, civil servants as well. This practice is to strengthen the moral discipline and responsibility for each civil servant to set an example for the people.
