After years of distrust, many South Korean giant investors venture to seek investment in Cambodia again (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): After distrust for investment in Cambodia for many years At the moment, more than 30 South Korean giant investors are visiting Cambodia to seek investment opportunities.
For information on investing in Cambodia, South Korean investors will meet with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and other relevant Cambodian officials.
On Tuesday morning, March 26, 2024, South Korean investors who are looking for investment opportunities in Cambodia also met with Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia to receive relevant information. Cambodia's Investment Policy.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol expressed his pleasure and considered the current visit to explore the investment of South Korean investors in Cambodia as a development and a new step for the investment situation in Cambodia in your view. South Korean investment.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol also highlighted the construction of infrastructure to facilitate the transportation system, including the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the Sihanoukville Deep Sea Port Expansion Project, the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway project, Phnom Penh-Siem Reap. Siem Reap-Poipet, as well as the project to improve the railway. In particular, the Funan-Techo canal project is an important waterway transport project connecting the river network to the sea of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister, who is Hun Manet's chief of staff for investment affairs, expressed confidence that after the visit, South Korean investors, all of whom are large companies, will decide to invest in Cambodia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by President Hun Manet, has been working hard to attract more new investors to Cambodia. In particular, want to turn the industry into a high-level industry, technology industry, etc. to raise the wages of the people.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol expressed his desire to see big South Korean investors invest in electronics and vehicles to get higher return on investment, helping Cambodia achieve its economic plan as a middle-income country. High level by 2030 and high income country by 2050.
According to a report by the Council for the Development of Cambodia, from 1994 to early 2024, there were 228 South Korean investment projects in Cambodia with an investment of more than 5 billion US dollars.
