34 Cambodian students who received scholarships from the Japanese government in 2024 will go to study at Japanese universities soon
(Phnom Penh): The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia on March 26, 2024 organized a ceremony to send 34 Cambodian students who received scholarships from the Government of Japan in 2024 after a tough competition from the Government of Japan before leaving. Leaving Cambodia to go to Japan to study there soon.
The farewell ceremony for the 34 Cambodian students was held at the residence of the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, with the participation of Mr. Ou Ino Atsushi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, and Dr. Oum Romney, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. , Mr. Vokora, President of the Khmer Alumni Association from Japan.
On that occasion, the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia stated that there are three levels of Japanese Government Scholarship Students in 2024, including: Postgraduate Level, Technical Secondary Level and Vocational Training Level, he also congratulated The 34 students who received scholarships after going through a series of tough competitions.
The Japanese government has been providing scholarships for Cambodian students to study in Japan since 1992. So far, more than 1,400 young Cambodians have received scholarships to study in Japan. Many Cambodian alumni studying in Japan are playing an active role in various fields.
He said last year was the year of the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia. The friendship between Japan and Cambodia has been further strengthened with the support of Cambodian alumni from Japan in various activities.
According to Dr. Oum Romney, the Japanese government's scholarship program for Cambodian students is very important, as Cambodia has sent human resources to study in Japan through fierce competition to achieve good results. And accepted from each Japanese university. While those universities are strong, respectively.
A senior official of the Ministry of Education said that many Cambodian alumni who returned to Cambodia have contributed to the development of Cambodia with the Royal Government by bringing knowledge, skills and experience studied in Japan to sow. Because in the private sector and civil servants. In addition, some Cambodian alumni studying in Japan have also become guides for many Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia.
On behalf of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Dr. Oum Romney expects that the Royal Government of Japan will expand the number of scholarships for Cambodian students even more.
