Inter-ministerial committee inspects and evaluates the work of restoring gravel roads in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): An inter-ministerial commission consisting of the Ministry of Rural Development and the Ministry of Economy and Finance on March 25, 2024, chaired by Mr. Try Meng, Secretary of State, Representative Mr. Chhay Rithisen, Minister of Rural Development, inspected and evaluated Rehabilitation of a paved gravel road after the completion of flood damage.
On that occasion, Mr. Try Meng said that this road has a length of 7,000 meters, a width of 7 meters, built one double gutters and three gutters and two name plates in Chambok Kphos and Rong villages. Thmey, Lveang Russey commune, Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province, implemented by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense, using the budget of the Royal Government through the Ministry of Rural Development.
He said that the newly restored 7-kilometer gravel road is very important for local people to transport all kinds of agricultural products of rural people, especially students' travel to school.
Mr. Try Meng also called on local authorities and people to take care of this road for the long term. Also, it is forbidden to transport heavy goods in excess of the limit, which makes the road vulnerable. After the restoration and official opening, the people expressed their enthusiasm and happiness because this road is a lifeline for people to travel because in the past it was difficult to travel because the road was damaged by Floods, too.
At the same time, the people in Lveang Russey Ba commune thanked the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Rural Development, for rehabilitating this road for easy travel, which showed that the Royal Government cares about People everywhere, whether urban or rural.
