(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of March 26, 2024, led a working group of officials of relevant units to inspect the progress of construction of more than 27 kilometers of roads in Reay Pai and Prek Koy communes, Kang Meas district and construction site. The construction of the Prek Chik Bridge, a historical site for birds guarding the city and checking the condition of the bank in Prek Koy commune, has solved some challenges for the people.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the construction of concrete roads and paved roads with a length of more than 27 kilometers in Reay Pai and Prek Koy communes and the construction of the Prek Chik bridge, the historical site of the birds in Kang Meas district, is now 90 percent completed.
