It should be noted that the official visit to Laos for a day and a half of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, ended at 12 noon on Tuesday, March 26, 2024, with good results. Happy place. Congratulations, Kratie is the 15th province to be declared a demining province in Cambodia! Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An thanks the warriors and young women who sacrificed their lives to liberate the nation and maintain peace in Cambodia.
Mr. Vathorn, Governor of Kratie Province, said that for more than 40 years, the people of Kratie Province have lived and suffered from hidden killers (landmines) and caused people to become orphans, widows, but now Kratie Mines are also an important contributor to the development of the province.
Dr. Ly Thuch pointed out that for more than 30 years from 1992 to 2023, Cambodia has liberated 3,024 square kilometers of land from the threat of landmines and explosive remnants of war for use and cultivation. As a result, the agricultural sector 76%, infrastructure 5% and others 19%, including:
Construction of houses, villagers, schools, health centers, etc., with more than 11 million people benefiting, of which 15 provinces were declared demining, including Kratie today.
In particular, 2023 is the year of the history of the clearance of landmines and munitions, which the government has cleared the most in more than 30 years in an area of 444 square kilometers, finding and destroying 23,946 anti-personnel mines. 204 tanks and 66,374 unexploded ordnance.
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An expressed his gratitude to the warriors and young women who sacrificed their lives to liberate the nation and maintain peace in Cambodia. Samdech Men Sam An stated that the Humanitarian Mine Action Program in Cambodia was started in 1992 in response to the urgent repatriation of refugees.
As a peace-loving country in 1997, Cambodia signed and became a party to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, Storage, Production and Transfer of Anti-Personnel Mines (also known as the Ottawa Convention) in 2000. There are now 164 member countries.
Cambodia has demonstrated to the international community its full capacity to address demining issues by sending demining forces to countries through UN missions. Currently, Cambodia has an area of approximately 1,854 kilograms. Square meters, of which 533 square kilometers are mined, Cambodia has ambitions to complete the cleanup by 2025.
Since 2022, Cambodia has declared 14 provincial capitals as mines, including Stung Treng, Kep, Prey Veng, Phnom Penh, Preah Sihanouk, Kandal, Svay Rieng, Takeo, Kampot, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Speu and Mondulkiri provinces. . In 2024, Cambodia plans to declare four more provinces, including Kratie, which was announced today, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap and Ratanakkiri as demining provinces.
