The Prime Minister paid his first official visit to Laos on March 25-26, 2024. During the visit, Samdech paid a courtesy call on Lao President Thongloun Sisoulith and held bilateral talks with his Lao counterpart Dr. Sorn Saisiphandon.
1. Energy Sector The two sides signed an agreement on cooperation in the energy sector, the second phase, accompanied by four memoranda of understanding, the goal is to continue to guarantee the supply of energy resources to Cambodia.
2. Economy and Trade: The two sides discussed the importance of holding the 15th meeting of the Joint Commission for JCBC Cooperation, the re-launch of the Joint Trade Commission with the organization of the Business and Investment Forum and Expanding economic integration through trade exchanges in services such as financial services, freight, land and tourism.
3. Connections between the two countries: The Prime Ministers of the two countries welcomed the launch of the direct flight of Lao Airlines Vientiane-Phnom Penh, which will further contribute to the growth of tourism, trade and other important sectors between the two countries. . The two sides also discussed detailed projects and other initiatives to connect people and people.
4. Defense and Security Cooperation: Both sides are committed to strengthening cooperation along the border, especially the communication between the leaders of both the Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Interior. In particular, cooperating on existing military cooperation and strengthening the prevention and suppression of transnational crime, especially human trafficking and drugs.
