(Laos, Vientiane): The official visit to Laos by Prime Minister Hun Manet for a day and a half ended at 12 noon on Tuesday, March 26, 2024 with good results. It should be a pleasure. Samdech President Hun Manet has led a delegation to return to Cambodia.
At the invitation of Mr. Sorn Sai Siphandon, Prime Minister of Laos, on March 25, the Prime Minister of Cambodia led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia, accompanied by investors from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce. Pay an official visit to Laos to further enhance relations and cooperation between the two countries.
For the first official visit as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen received a warm welcome, pleasure and honor from the Prime Minister of Laos, Mr. Sorn Sai Siphandon.
During the bilateral meeting between Samdech Hun Sen and Mr. Sorn Siphan Don, expressed satisfaction and pleasure in the relationship and cooperation between the two countries in the past. In addition to expressing satisfaction over the relationship and cooperation between the two countries, the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Laos also discussed focusing on enhancing relations and cooperation between the two countries.
In a joint conference after the bilateral meeting, President Hun Manet said that during the meeting with the Lao Prime Minister, the two sides discussed six major issues, including border issues, security, economic issues, trade, tourism and people-to-people contacts. People from both countries as well. The six issues raised include:
1: Energy Sector: In relation to the energy sector, Cambodia thanked Laos for its continuous energy supply. In addition, the two sides signed a second phase of cooperation agreement on energy cooperation, accompanied by four memoranda of understanding. The goal is to continue to ensure the supply of energy to Cambodia.
2. Economy and Trade: The two sides discussed the importance of organizing the 15th meeting of the Joint Commission for JCBC Cooperation, the re-launch of the Joint Trade Commission with the organization of the Business and Investment Forum and Expanding economic integration through trade exchanges in services such as financial services, freight, land and tourism.
The sixth task is for the two sides to discuss measures to promote cooperation in tourism, education, sports and agriculture.
Please be reminded that after the bilateral talks, the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Laos also co-chaired the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the two countries to expand cooperation on Boundaries and energy.
During his current visit to Laos, in addition to meeting bilaterally with the Prime Minister of Laos, Samdech Hun Sen also paid a courtesy call on Mr. Thongloun Sisoulith, President of Laos.
The President of Laos expressed his satisfaction with the outcome of the talks between the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Laos. The President of Laos considered this result as a meaningful result for the two countries' relations in the spirit of implementing the points agreed upon and the continuation of friendly cooperation, solidarity and brotherhood.
The Laotian President expressed his commitment to finding a solution to the remaining issues, especially in the fields of energy, border affairs and other important cooperation to improve relations and cooperation between the two countries. .
In front of the President, the President of Laos emphasized that Laos is fortunate to be a border country with Cambodia and expressed the hope that the two countries will continue to maintain this traditional and historical relationship and work together to resolve it. Challenge together to make this relationship even better for the benefit of the people of both countries.
He also stressed that the potential of Cambodia and Laos is still high and encouraged the friendly association between the two countries to do more to facilitate greater connectivity between the two countries.
