But amid rising global pressure for a ceasefire in the war, which has killed more than 32,000 Palestinians, the United States abstained in Monday's election to allow the Security Council to demand a ceasefire. Immediately during the Muslim holy month of Ramadan, which closes in two weeks.
It also calls for the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages. Israel says Hamas took 253 hostages in the October 7 attack.
The Security Council resolution also "emphasizes the urgent need to expand humanitarian assistance throughout the Gaza Strip and strengthen civil protection, and reiterates its call for the removal of all barriers to large-scale humanitarian assistance." Also.
Israeli military radio reported shortly before the start of the Security Council meeting that Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu would cancel a planned delegation to Washington if the United States did not veto the resolution.
The United States has vetoed three Security Council resolutions on the Gaza war and has twice abstained, allowing the Security Council to adopt a resolution aimed at increasing aid to Gaza and calling for an extension. When the ceasefire.
Russia and China also vetoed a resolution proposed by the United States in October and Friday.
