(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for March 26, 2024.
The Ministry states that low pressure will continue to cover the Kingdom of Cambodia, Thailand, the Gulf of Thailand, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea. This situation will make: From March 26 to 28, 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 26 ° C and maximum temperature 36 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest have an average speed of 2 m / s. In the lowland areas of Battambang, Pursat, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang and Svay Rieng, about 30% of the area is likely to receive rain.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 37 ° C. Winds from the east and southeast have an average speed of 2 m / s. In the highlands, Pailin, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Stung Treng and Mondulkiri provinces will receive about 20% of rainfall.
