Analysis: China's economy continues to recover steadily
Second, employment conditions were stable, and the overall unemployment rate in registered urban and rural areas remained stable. The unemployment rate in urban and rural areas registered in January was 5.2 percent and in February it was 5.3 percent, down 0.3 percent from the same period in 2023. Third, the consumer price index turned from a 0.8 percent decline last month to a 0.7 percent increase over the same period in 2023.
Fourth, new dynamics and new excellence are constantly being accumulated and new business forms remain active. From January to February this year, online retail sales rose 14.4 percent year-on-year in 2023 and 6 percent year-on-year in 2023.
Today, although the environment facing economic development is still complex and tense, the fundamentals of the Chinese economy have steadily improved and the positive factors driving the economic recovery have improved. On the other hand, macroeconomic policies continue to have an impact and are effective enough to support the achievement of the expected growth target of 5%.
Driven by demand for services, the service industry has recovered for two consecutive months. The rapid growth of new consumption will further expand the growth space, which is conducive to further economic recovery.
Li Qiang pointed out that the international environment is currently undergoing profound changes and global economic development is facing serious challenges. China will take effective action to promote high-quality development and inject more certainty and positive energy into the recovery and sustainable development of the world economy.
It should be noted that the 2024th annual meeting of the China High-Level Development Forum will be held for two days under the theme "Sustainable Development in China". Officials from major international organizations, the world's top 500 companies and world-renowned international scholars will discuss and exchange views on issues related to China's sustainable development.
