(Svay Rieng): Thirty drivers of reversing vehicles on National Road No. 1, along with 29 motorcycles, were arrested by the traffic planning force of Bavet City Police Inspectorate in cooperation with Bavet City Military Police and People's Defense Force. Made an education contract on March 24, 2024.
According to the traffic police of Bavet City Police Inspectorate, in the past, some drivers who drove on National Road No. 1 in Bavet City did not obey the traffic law, driving in the opposite direction, causing traffic accidents. Often, almost daily.
Most reversing drivers say they are too lazy to cross the road, as Bavet City has developed parks, installed traffic lights at night and parted roads to avoid traffic jams, but drivers who do not obey traffic rules still drive in reverse. Only then did the authorities lead the coalition forces to enforce the traffic law, stop the offending drivers and educate them, and if they do not resign, they will be fined according to the law.
Police said that in the case of arresting 30 motorcycle owners and 29 motorbikes, they took them to the Bavet City Police Inspectorate to make a contract and educate them, "The next day, do not drive in reverse" and let them shout, "I stopped "Driving a motorcycle in the opposite direction, and if the next time driving in reverse, let the authorities follow the law."
