Riel loans accounted for 25% of total loans in the Cambodian microfinance sector, while riel deposits accounted for 16%.
Cambodia's microfinance sector has become an important driving force in the national economy, helping to drive an impressive growth in the use of the riel in 2023.
According to the report, the balance of loans in riel has reached 5.56 trillion riel, while deposits in riel at the four deposit-taking microfinance institutions (MDIs) have reached 1.52 trillion. Million Riels. This data shows a significant shift in public savings habits towards local currency savings.
Ms. Dith Nita, President of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said, “The effective approach that the members have implemented in 2023 is designed to enhance the role of the riel in financial transactions and to strengthen the relationship between the community and the national currency. "In depth, this effort is critical to building an ecological and resilient financial sector ecosystem."
She added that microfinance loans have had a significant impact on the Cambodian economy through sectors such as households, business, agriculture and other sectors, and that the intervention of targeted loans has not only boosted economic activity, Emphasized the important role of the microfinance sector in supporting the development of Cambodia.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, this morning, March 25, 2024, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the Chan School and achievements in Wat Tep Nimit (Wat Thmey). ) Located in Village 3, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City.
The ceremony was attended by His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Excellency Dr. Bour Kri, His Highness the Archbishop of the Judiciary of Cambodia, Mrs. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, as well as senior officials, government officials, Buddhists and monks. 150 people as well.
Ms. Mithona Phuthong said that on behalf of the Buddhists and the people of Koh Kong province, they were very happy and thankful for the peace after the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council. Found peace, development for the people and the nation for progress in all fields, including Buddhism.
According to the provincial governor, the inaugural Buddhist achievements include a 51-meter-long and 29-meter-wide Chan school complex with achievements in Wat Tep Nimit, Khemarak Phoumin, with 99 monks. There are 7 abbots, 20 grandmothers and 22 students (pagoda children).
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha continued that, sadly, during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the pagoda was forgotten, the educated monks were destroyed by the secular Tamils and the monks were decapitated. Dharma-rules, rules and regulations related to Buddhism were almost completely destroyed for later Buddhism.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha confirmed that now that Cambodia has achieved complete peace, pagodas have flourished everywhere. In fact, the field of Buddhism, pagodas all over the country are flourishing, not only are pagodas a place for Buddhists to receive Buddhist teachings, but also a place for poor students to stay and study.
