(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, said that the Ministry of Industry has been preparing a number of policy measures to help small and medium enterprises and promote the transformation of informal businesses into formal businesses. In Cambodia's economy of more than 770,000 enterprises, only about 2% are officially registered enterprises.
He added that if the work to promote informal business transformation to formal business success will boost economic growth even more.
Mr. Hem Vandy said this at a press conference this morning, Sunday, March 24, 2024, on the second National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation.
According to the Minister, among the more than 770,000 economic entities, about 2% are officially registered SMEs and about 0.2% are large companies, of which more than 97% are micro-enterprises and most of them are micro-enterprises. In the informal economy.
He explained that there are many factors that keep many enterprises out of the system, such as market experience, entrepreneurship, ability to meet compliance, as well as some tax conditions and the management of their own business is still limited.
He stressed that both the previous mandate as well as in this mandate, the government wants to strengthen and help those small businesses to grow.
He stressed that the promotion of informal business to formal business is extremely important to attract foreign investment (FDI), which is looking to Cambodia to relocate investment to Cambodia.
He encourages business owners to participate in implementing and fulfilling the policies and measures of the Royal Government that will be prepared. And within the framework of the Chairman of the Informal Economic Development Coordinating Committee, the Ministry of Industry will start promoting more outreach campaigns to business owners to know and understand more.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, on March 24, 2024, called on business owners and development partners, as well as all stakeholders, to seize the opportunity to learn, learn and cooperate to create new innovations. .
This call was made on the occasion of Mr. Hem Vandy's participation in the press conference of the opening ceremony of the 2nd National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation 2024 under the theme "Small and Medium Enterprises Towards Science, Technology and Innovation" on the 21st This March 2024.
Mr. Hem Vandy stated, "I would like to call on all business owners, teachers, researchers, students and development partners and all stakeholders, as well as companies that have participated in the exhibition and strive to seize the opportunity for "Learn, understand, learn, collaborate, create more new innovations."
Mr. Hem Vandy said that the National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation is a rare opportunity for business owners, teachers, researchers, students and the private sector, Cambodia's development partners to share and practice together for the development of the country.
At the same time, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation hopes that through this day, ideas and experiences can be exchanged, as well as plans for cooperation with partners such as countries that Cambodia has actually cooperated with.
Mr. Hem Vandy also asked the participants to help each other think about what technology can be applied to strengthen and expand to improve productivity and business together to join the Royal Government as well as society, development The economy develops entrepreneurship successfully and reaches 2030 and 2050 with pride.
According to Hem Vandy, this year's National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry has chosen the theme "Small and Medium Enterprises Towards Science, Technology and Innovation" in order to boost the productivity of private enterprises through the inclusion of technology in Production line to increase efficiency and added value.
The Minister also said that the three-day National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation has four main objectives, including:
The Technology and Manufacturing Equipment Exhibition will feature exhibitions of equipment and / or technologies that serve the development of production, especially for small and medium-sized enterprises, including: machinery, machinery, supporting equipment, related enterprises, production or supply of goods. Raw materials: engineering consulting, maintenance, repair and training, small and medium enterprise regulatory consulting, and digital and financial solutions.
This program lasts for 3 days from March 24 to 26, 2024, open to the public, especially traders who are representatives from small and medium enterprises. There are 228 booths and 15 food and beverage booths. Exhibitors include: public institutions, the private sector, which is mostly small and medium enterprises, educational and higher education institutions, new businesses and development partners.
