Cambodia strongly condemns terrorist attack on Moscow theater
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on March 24, 2024, issued a statement strongly condemning the terrorist attack on the theater in Moscow, Russia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia is shocked by the deaths and injuries of dozens of people in the terrorist attack on the Moscow Theater on March 22, 2024. The Royal Government of Cambodia strongly condemns this heinous attack.
The Royal Government of Cambodia would like to express our deepest condolences and deepest sympathies to the families of the victims and the Government of the Russian Federation, and wish all the injured a speedy recovery.
Cambodia reaffirms that any act of terrorism is a crime that cannot be justified, regardless of the purpose or the individual. We would like to express our solidarity with the Russian government and people during this sad time.
(Phnom Penh): Investigating Judge Li Sokha of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has ordered the detention of a woman who owns the Facebook page of Sdech Champeam KH, who posted the sale of processed weapons using metal bullets on charges of "trafficking in weapons for various attacks." "Sell all-metal firearms" which has been carried out on Facebook from 2022 to the present under Article 20 of the Law on the Control of Weapons, Explosives and Ammunition.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, with the coordination of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and in cooperation with the competent forces of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
The above suspect confessed that he did commit the crime after the interrogation of the competent authorities, the case was prepared and the suspect was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for processing and was ordered by the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Detained for trafficking weapons for various purposes (selling weapons, processing metal bullets).
