Key Remarks by Samdech Hun Sen Manet on the Opening Ceremony of the 2nd "National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Sunday, March 24, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, inaugurated the second "National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation". .
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani President Hun Manet's opportunity to open the second "National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation":
* Samdech Hun Manet praised and commended the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation for celebrating the 2nd National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation, as well as organizing major accompanying events, including: Technology and Equipment Exhibitions, Exhibitions Science, Technology Forum, Outstanding Cambodian Scientist Award.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet said that the capture of science, technology and innovation is the key to the development of the digital socio-economy by incorporating the leading technologies in the production chain and other public services to increase productivity in line with international standards, which is a valid factor. Indispensable.
* Samdech Hun Manet said that the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Council for Science, Technology and Innovation have been assigned by the Royal Government to achieve the construction of a high-middle-income country by 2030 and towards Achieved Cambodia's vision for 2050 by adding technology as the fifth priority in the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1.
* Samdech Hun Manet said that today's event is a testament to the potential of science, technology and innovation with the Royal Government's attention to encourage and encourage small and medium enterprises to focus on and embrace science and technology. And innovation as a pillar and engine in building and developing enterprises to achieve an innovative national ecosystem.
* President Hun Manet said to continue to push for more diversified technology nurseries to support stakeholders, especially the private sector, in finding markets, capturing regional and global supply chains.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet urges educational institutions, research and the private sector, especially small and medium enterprises, to cooperate with the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to establish a strong foundation in science, technology and innovation in all fields.
* Samdech Hun Manet requested the relevant ministries and institutions to continue to cooperate, support, lead and coordinate by the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation so that this priority sector can become a key element of Cambodia's socio-economic development.
* Samdech Hun Manet concludes his speech at 8:36 AM on March 24, 2024, Thank you for watching the live broadcast on Fresh News. The Ministry of Water Resources announces the weather conditions at Cambodia for March 24, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for March 24, 2024.
The Ministry states that low pressure will continue to cover the Kingdom of Cambodia, Thailand, the Gulf of Thailand, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea. This situation will make: From March 24 to 26, 2024:
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 37 ° C. Winds from the east and southeast have an average speed of 2 m / s. In the northwestern highlands, Pailin, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear provinces are likely to receive about 10% of rainfall.
"National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation" was initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia, with March 26 as the day to celebrate this day. The first "National Day of Science, Technology and Innovation" was held in 2023 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, said that this year's National Science, Technology and Innovation Day, the Ministry has chosen the theme "Small and Medium Enterprises Towards Science, Technology and Innovation" in order to boost the productivity of private enterprises through Incorporating technology into the production line to increase efficiency and added value.
