Achievements at Wat Hong Lam in Kratie City, which cost more than 1.5 million USD, were officially inaugurated.
(Kratie): Achievements in Pursatharam pagoda called Hong Lam pagoda in Orussey 2 village, Sangkat Or Russey, Kratie city, Kratie province, which cost US $ 1,566,994.5, was inaugurated this morning. March 23, 2024.
The inauguration ceremony of the temple was presided over by Mr. Vathorn, Governor of Kratie Province, and was attended by monks, government officials and many Buddhists.
The provincial governor said that the temple is also considered an important part of continuing to implement policies for the elderly, children and the poor. The temple has become a safe haven for grandparents, a place for begging, begging, children and some young people who can not afford to use the temple, some venerated to continue their studies and some even stay to Continue studying.
He added that after the day of liberation, January 7, 1979, which was a historic day, a day of resurrection of the people, all religions were re-practiced in harmony, without discrimination, and under the shadow of peace, stability and peace. Development, which is the aspiration of the Cambodian people and the achievement of the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party over the past 40 years.
At the same time, Mr. Vathorn also expressed his pride in the many achievements that have been made in this temple and would like to join in congratulating the inauguration program and the achievements.
The provincial governor also paid tribute to Nhean Sarveti Lim Bunthon, the Royal Ballon of Honor of Preah Balat, the Provincial Council and the Chief Bishop of Wat Pursatharam (also known as Wat Hong La) for leading many achievements since 2013. To date, the temple, the temple, the pagoda, the gates, the fences and the infrastructure in the temple have been built at a total cost of US $ 1,566,994.5.
In addition to the above achievements, Preah Nhean Savey Lim Bunthon also donated money, personal resources, contributed to the construction of many achievements that have contributed to the development of Kratie province and called on all people and Buddhists to continue to support Build more achievements, especially to participate in maintaining the achievements in this temple to be stable and sustainable for the practice and preservation for future generations.
