Officials from the Office of the Council of Ministers distributed donations to more than 1,000 students and teachers in Siem Reap and renovated school buildings in Kampong Thom
(Kampong Thom): On the afternoon of March 23, 2024, Mr. Ke Granit, Member of Information and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers, visited and distributed study materials to students and teachers in Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province and Chey Primary School. Located in Sankor Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province.
On that occasion, he stated that these are great contributions to the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting education as well as human resources, and he also advised all students to study hard both at school and at school. Home to be a good student, a good child and a good friend to everyone and a pillar of the future of the nation.
With this, he also brought 32 sheets of zinc, 3 wooden doors, 12 wooden windows to repair a school building in Chey village, Sankor commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, which is very dilapidated and allows students to study well. Re-security.
He also thanked the philanthropists near and far who supported both materials and funds through his own to distribute to students, teachers, as well as renovate the school building now.
He also announced the scholarships that the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and universities in Phnom Penh have offered through him to students who want to continue their studies at the university in the upcoming 2024-2025 academic year, please contact him directly. To continue the study according to the situation and the actual number.
It should be noted that the study materials to be distributed are at Hun Sen Model Buffalo Primary School and Chey Primary School, which includes 1,500 story books, coloring books, some sports materials such as 10 footballs, 10 volleyballs, 4 basketballs, 4 slogans, 200 posters. 3,000 pictures and 50 wall clocks. Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many: The election results clearly show that the people give confidence and warmth to the Cambodian People's Party.
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Hun Many, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) visited Kampong Speu province during the inauguration ceremony of achievements in Ang Lum Tong pagoda, Snom Krapeu commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province on the morning of March 24, 2024. He said that the results of the election on July 23, 2023 clearly show that the people trust and are warm with the CPP.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many thanked Grandma Oum Puming for believing in the CPP by going to the polls on July 23, 2023 until the CPP won. The results should be satisfactory.
"The results of the July 23, 2023 election clearly show that the people trust and are warm with the CPP," Hun Many said.
In connection with the above, he also emphasized that voting for the CPP is a vote of confidence and protection of peace, and voting for the CPP is also a protection of what is in the interests of The people are all born from the policy of the Cambodian People's Party to ensure and improve the daily life of the people. Therefore, voting for the Cambodian People's Party is tantamount to voting to protect the interests of the people.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many thanked all the people who continue to give confidence to vote for the Cambodian People's Party, which allows us to make real achievements, just like what we inaugurated today.
Srey Sour Srey Keo denies allegations made by Brigadier General Ou Sophal, Deputy Director of the Criminal Department, on charges of incitement, defamation and destruction of property
(Phnom Penh): Srey Sour Srey Keo has issued a letter dismissing the allegations made by Brigadier General Ou Sophal, Deputy Director of the Criminal Department, in connection with cases of incitement, slander, and destruction of property.
It should be noted that the dismissal of these allegations came after Brigadier General Ou Sophal recently filed a complaint with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, accusing the chief of Trapeang Prey village, Ksem Ksan commune, Udong city. May Chey, Kampong Speu province, and three other people, including a woman named Sour Srey Keo.
The lawsuit was filed after Trapeang Prey village chief filed a complaint with the Minister of Interior, accusing Ou Sophal of violence and death threats in a land dispute, but later wrote a letter. I apologize to Brigadier General Ou Sophal.
In the complaint, Brigadier General Ou Sophal considered that the complaint filed by Trapeang Prey village chief Yoy Nuon was made by Sour Srey Keo. Due to such accusations and allegations, Srey Keo issued a dismissal letter saying that she was not behind the village chief's complaint.
In his letter of clarification on March 22, 2024, Sour Srey Keo confirmed that in the case of all kinds of media coverage, Mr. Yoy Nuon Chea, the chief of Trapeang Prey village, was the interviewer with the media himself, she was not there. In fact, the interview.
Regarding the slander, she also confirmed that it was the story of the village chief and Ou Sophal, because she did not know about the dispute between the two, unless there is a description of Yoy Nuon herself, then the media will know the facts. And time.
She also said that in the complaint of Brigadier General Ou Sophal, Deputy Director of the Criminal Department did not write and there is no evidence of damage to other people's property and she did not know.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al: Wastewater treatment plant needs to be built to support economic growth and create jobs for people in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Assistance Team, said that waste and sewage management is important for the whole country. In particular, for Sihanoukville, it is necessary to speed up the management and implementation, otherwise it will lose the opportunity to build and build Sihanoukville into a potential tourism province.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al said this on the occasion of the inauguration of the third wastewater treatment plant, which has the capacity to purify water from wastewater to 20,000 cubic meters per day before discharge. To the sea on March 22, 2024 in Ochheuteal 2 beach, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville on March 24, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Say Samal also added that as the population grows, the development, the growth of tourists increases, it requires us to set up a sub-wastewater treatment plant, although today we have a new wastewater treatment plant, but we Together, keep thinking about the future, all dirty water must be filtered before being dumped into the sea.
With the care of His Excellency Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, we will continue to firmly safeguard peace, political stability, security, and social order, and ensure the process of promoting economic growth through the promotion of reforms. Responsible and to achieve new achievements in maintaining peace and developing the motherland.
Meanwhile, the second pentagon, the first corner, focuses on accelerating the development of Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose special economic zone, which is an important economic pole for tourism, financial services centers, industrial zones, etc. by defining mechanisms. Clearly implement all aspects and master planning development of Cambodia's coastal provinces as a multi-purpose economic corridor and cell interface.
