Mr. Peng Po Na introduced 6 points to strengthen the capacity of CPP officials as party members of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport
(Phnom Penh): To contribute to help the Cambodian People's Party and to help party officials who are party members of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to be stronger, more capable and have potential and to contribute to building the party Mr. Peng Por Nea, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the CPP Cambodia and the Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has issued six guidelines to all members to implement effectively.
The one-day training course consisted of 3 meaningful lectures, including: History, achievements and historical lessons of the party by Mr. Nuon Pharath. Building the good attitude of party officials by Mr. Lay Sopanha, Deputy Chairman of the YKC Training Research Group. The mode of work and the line of organization of the youth of the middle party by Mr. Kim Sothea, Deputy Chairman of the research team for the YCK training.
At the opening ceremony, Ms. Mon Manvi, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Vice Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry, gave a welcome speech and instructed all participants to strive to acquire knowledge in order to strengthen their capacity. As the successor of the party.
Speaking at the Closing Ceremony of the Training Course, Mr. Pheng Sovicheano, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Education and Propaganda Committee of the Ministry Party Committee, gave a brief report on the training course to the Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry and the event, which reflected the efforts The efforts of the trainers and the program team.
On that occasion, Mr. YOS Phanida, as the head of the training section of YCC, who co-led the training program, noted the attention to listen to the presentation on the above topics and participation. Participants are encouraged to ask questions and participate in their comments.
In order for the Ministry Party to be strong, to have potential party officials and to contribute to the building of the party, Mr. Peng Porna has made six proposals to all members, including the following:
1: On behalf of the party members, no matter what level they are in, they must understand their duties, in which they must strive to properly implement the party's political program and statutes, must maintain internal unity, keep secrets and always help each other. Reciprocate and build good relationships with people for growth.
2: As a successor, please take part in maintaining the positive achievements that the older youth have built and left behind and expand more positive achievements for the better, and together build a strong foundation to transfer The next generation of youth.
3. Each of us must have good qualities that refer to the ability, morality, popularity and good health, be willing to support the implementation of all tasks and decisions of the party and the movement of relatives, friends and relatives to support the right cause of the party.
4: To continue to educate political party members on a regular basis and to learn from each other's good experiences in order to carry out their work effectively and to strive to learn and enhance their abilities and virtues in order to fulfill their duties for the motherland.
5. Strive to build and strengthen the party in the financial sector by supporting and participating in mobilizing financial means from various legal sources to serve the party's political activities.
6. Participate in basic work as assigned to the back of the people's houses to implement the party's political program, connect with the people and actively contribute to the implementation of the political program for building and defending the motherland 2023-2028.
On that occasion, Mr. Peng Porna, Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry, was honored to hand out certificates to attend the training on strengthening the capacity of party officials for the sustainability of the party leadership to the participants.
Speaking on the occasion, Samdech Hun Sen stated that in order to promote the participation in the implementation of science, technology and innovation with the strengthening of the National Council for Science, Technology and Innovation, Samdech would like to recommend to the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the Ministry. Relevant institutions for further implementation include:
Second, continue to promote technological revolution to industry, small and medium enterprises in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.0 in order to quickly capture the latest technologies to increase enterprise productivity and promote local traditional enterprises. Keep up-to-date and complete the progress of science, technology and innovation.
Fourth, to implement the mechanism to strictly monitor and evaluate the implementation of the relevant ministries and institutions according to the indicators set out in the Roadmap for Science, Technology and Innovation 2030. He requested all relevant ministries and institutions to cooperate with a high sense of responsibility in deciding to transmit all information and indicators set out in the roadmap in a transparent and effective manner.
Fifth, educational institutions, training and research, and the private sector, especially small and medium enterprises, must cooperate with the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to establish a strong foundation in science, technology and innovation in all fields. This goal can be achieved depending on the change of mindset, management style, employment and business management with the investment of both capital and human resource training.
The presence of the Prime Minister at the opening of this forum clearly shows the Royal Government's attention and high value to the field of science, technology and innovation, which is a strategic tool to achieve the vision of Cambodia to become a country with income. High average in 2030 and high income in 2050.
