Cambodia will soon have a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation with Azerbaijan
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the Republic of Azerbaijan have agreed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation and to speed up the connection between the two countries.
The agreement was reached during a meeting between Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. Shovgi Mehdizada, Ambassador of the Republic of Azerbaijan to Hanoi, Vietnam on March 22, 2024, to discuss the promotion of tourism cooperation between the two countries. Both countries.
The Azerbaijani Minister and Ambassador also agreed to push for the signing of a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation and to speed up the connection between the two countries.
As 2024 marks the 30th anniversary of Cambodia-Azerbaijan diplomatic relations, the Ambassador requested the Minister to explore the possibility of co-organizing various events to celebrate the 30th anniversary of diplomatic relations and promote tourism between the two countries.
The Ambassador appreciated the development of Cambodia's tourism sector and asked the Minister to share his experience through the Cambodia Tourism Marketing and Promotion Board, National Institute of Tourism and Tourism Vocational School.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on March 23, 2024 released a video on dengue fever and dengue prevention strategies while this disease is still a public health problem in Cambodia.
According to the Ministry of Health, as of the beginning of 2024, there were more than 3,000 cases of dengue fever. In the first nine weeks of 2024, more than 1,000 cases of dengue fever were being treated at Kantha Bopha Hospital.
On this occasion, the Ministry of Health called on all citizens and local authorities to join the movement to reduce and prevent the occurrence of tiger mosquitoes, which are a source of dengue transmission.
