Honorary Prince Dr. Men Sam An: Win-Win Politics Brings Progress to Women in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Speech at the Celebration of the 113th Anniversary of the International Women's Day, March 8, 2024 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution" at the Ministry of Women's Affairs on March 22, 2024 The King's personal adviser stated that win-win politics has brought prosperity to women in Cambodia.
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An said that due to the cold shadow of peace, the country has created favorable conditions for the development and progress of the country, which allows the Royal Government to continuously expand its investment in social development and implement political programs. Respond to gender and protect human rights more broadly.
According to Dr. Men Sam An, Cambodia celebrates International Women's Day on March 8 every year to commemorate the struggle for equal rights and freedoms and to reflect on progress, achievements, challenges, commitments and positive measures. Promote gender equality and empower every woman and girl.
This year 2024 is to commemorate the 113rd anniversary of the International Women's Day, March 8, 2024. The Ministry of Women's Affairs has selected the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution" in order to highlight the potential and necessity of promoting the participation and representation of women and girls in the digital sector.
Responding to the context of social development in the digital age and in line with the vision outlined in the Royal Government of Cambodia's first phase of the Pentagon Strategy and the policy framework to promote gender equality and empower women and children. Female. This is an additional emphasis of Samdech Kittisangha Dr. Men Sam An.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, said that the Royal Government has continued to prioritize the promotion of gender equality and the empowerment of women and girls in all areas as a priority in the first phase of the Pentagon policy agenda and strategy. By strengthening citizenship in a highly civilized society with morality, equity and environment in which "women are the core".
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi added that the Royal Government has recently launched the National Strategy for Informal Economy Development (2023-2028) to develop the informal economy to grow and have access to the system and become It is an important driving force in improving people's lives and can contribute to the maximum in achieving sustainable development, environment, resilience and crisis resilience.
In addition, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi stated that the Royal Government has established the Informal Economic Development Coordinating Committee and is preparing an action plan and data collection mechanism prior to the future development of the registration system to determine A clear goal for receiving practical assistance from the Royal Government.
(Kratie): A vehicle inspection team stopped four overweight trucks on National Road 73, Chroy Thmor Krom village, Chhlong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province on March 22, 2024.
