Preah Vihear is the province with the potential for organic farming and the largest supplier of organic agricultural products in Cambodia.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Ouk Kimsan, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, said that Preah Vihear Province is the province with the potential for organic farming and the largest supplier of organic agricultural products in Cambodia, such as organic rice, organic cassava, organic peanuts and organic sesame. Original.
On behalf of the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, Mr. Ouk Kimsan warmly welcomed the presence of the ladies and gentlemen from the relevant units who participated in the important agro-ecological exhibition, which was organized for the first time for Preah Vihear Province.
He thanked the project for the development of ecosystems and food security in Southeast Asia, known as the "ASIT Project" and the donors of the French Agency for Development and the European Union, especially the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Department of Agricultural Land Management, Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union. Sirat Center, Swiss Consult and other project partners.
Mr. Ouk Kimsan stated that this important agro-ecological exhibition was organized for three main purposes:
* First: To mobilize and provide opportunities for stakeholders, especially farmers' organizations and private companies to share knowledge, experience and present products and processed products of good agricultural practices, organic farming as part of agro-ecology, as well as the impact of consumption. Chemical inputs to the public, especially farmers and consumers, including women and youth.
* Second: To create opportunities for stakeholders, especially agricultural communities, to learn and exchange experiences with each other regarding challenges and effective solutions of agriculture, especially to reduce costs and maintain or increase yields. And mortgages based on agro-ecology and sustainable agriculture.
* Third: To present to the stakeholders, especially the farming community, new technical knowledge gained from research for the development of the Acid project, as well as other projects and programs to ensure the sustainability, productivity and profitability of organic farming, especially crops. Rice.
