(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said that the research team of the Fisheries Administration and WWF found a newborn dolphin at 13:45 on March 22, 2024. Anlong Kaing Koun Sat, Koh Preah village, Koh Preah commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province. The baby dolphin is in a herd of six other dolphins.
On the same day in Kratie province, the team received sad news and found the body of a dolphin that died at Prek Prosop, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, about 10 km in the morning of March 22. 2024. The dead dolphin is 1.06 meters long and weighs 11 kilograms, which is likely to be born within a day or two.
According to preliminary conclusions, the death of the dolphin in Anlong Kampi, Kratie province may be caused by the abuse of large dolphins, but the research team will continue to analyze to find the exact cause.
Please note that as of March 23, 2024, Cambodia has received 5 newborn dolphins and 2 dead dolphins.
