General Commissioner of National Police handed over electric car with siren to 5 Capital-Provincial Police Commissioners
(Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, this morning, March 22, 2024, presided over the handing over ceremony of electric vehicles with sirens to five Capital-Provincial Police Commissions.
On that occasion, General Sar Thet thanked the philanthropists who have spent their personal resources to support the National Police Force to contribute to the security, safety and daily duties of the unit. This car is an electric car that can be used within 300 to 400 km to recharge, and this car can be used daily, such as: leading the procession and other work in its capital-province.
The General Commissioner instructed the Capital-Provincial Police Commissioners who received the car to be responsible for maintaining it as their property to ensure long-term use. Particularly for the provinces that have not yet received the car, it may be later because the provinces that received the car are the provinces that need to receive these cars.
The General hopes that the philanthropists will continue to provide vehicles or materials to the General Commission of the National Police to contribute to the protection and security of the people.
Please note that 10 vehicles to be handed over to the Capital-Provincial Police Commissioners at this time, including 2 units of Phnom Penh Municipal Police, 2 units of Battambang Provincial Police, 2 units of Prey Veng Provincial Police, 2 units of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police and 2 units of Pursat Provincial Police.
