Moldova is a former Soviet territory between Ukraine and Romania and has been considering EU membership since the start of the Ukraine war. Prime Minister Maia Sandu, who has always said that Russia is a major threat to Moldovan security, has set EU membership as the cornerstone of her government.
Following a debate at the EU summit in Brussels, the Moldovan parliament approved the resolution by a 54-vote majority and no opposition. "Only joining Europe can secure the future of Moldova as a fully sovereign and neutral democracy," the statement said.
