Researchers find species of amphibians and mammals suspected to be new species or a new record for Cambodia and the world in Battambang
(Battambang): Researchers from the Ministry of Environment have found and collected a number of species of animals and animals that are interesting for science in the limestone mountains in Banan district, Battambang province.
Some species are suspected by experts to be new species or a new record for the world and Cambodia as well. Confirmation will be further confirmed through the analysis of the genetic resources of the biodiversity samples after the field studies and data collection are completed.
The new biodiversity data from the current study is important information to support future biodiversity conservation and planning for the management and conservation of those limestone mountains in the future.
