Crude oil prices fall slightly after US energy stocks fall sharply
LONDON (Reuters) - Crude prices fell slightly in trading on Thursday after a sharp drop in US crude inventories as the Fed strengthened its outlook. Interest rates this year. According to Reuters.
The U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA) on Wednesday reported a two-week straight drop in crude inventories in the United States, the world's largest consumer of oil, Reuters reported.
Oil inventories fell unexpectedly by 2 million barrels to 445 million barrels in the week ending March 15 as exports rose and refiners continued to increase their business activities. Analysts surveyed by Reuters expected oil inventories to rise by 13,000 barrels.
