Trade will be on the agenda during Xi Jinping's visit to Paris in May
BEIJING (Reuters) - Trade will be on the agenda when Chinese President Xi Jinping meets with his French counterpart Emmanuel Macron in Paris in May, according to several diplomatic sources. His first visit to Europe in more than five years comes amid tensions between the EU and China. This is according to a release by Reuters.
Makrong in 2023 was warmly welcomed during a visit to Beijing, which Western analysts see as part of China's strategy to draw attention from major European countries in the bloc to counter US influence. . But since then, trade relations between Beijing and Paris have been strained after France backed a European Commission investigation into the import of electric cars from China.
In addition to trade, the Ukraine war is also expected to be a topic of discussion between Xi Jinping and Makrong. Last year, French officials tried to persuade Beijing to put pressure on Russia over the war in Ukraine and reduce its support for Putin.
