Samdech Hun Manet Presides Over 6 Recommendations to Continue to Pay Attention and Promote Education and Training to Khmer Muslims (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): This provides six recommendations to stakeholders to continue to pay attention and promote education and training to Cambodian Muslims in Cambodia.
These recommendations were made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the Ramadan meal attended by about 6,000 Cambodian Muslims at the Chroy Changvar International Convention and Exhibition Center on the afternoon of March 21, 2024. .
On this occasion, Samdech Thipdey emphasized that the education sector in the field of Khmer Islam is currently developing and the Royal Government has provided a framework for teachers to the Khmer Muslim community, which has increased the number of Khmer Muslim graduates.
At the same time, Samdech Dhipady calls for continued attention to the training of professional skills and various technologies so that Cambodian Muslims can get appropriate jobs and improve their family life and society through the following recommendations. :
First. All Muslim leaders and Muslims continue to work together in solidarity and good relations with other religious communities, both nationally and internationally, based on the principles of national harmony.
Second. Must continue to organize religious affairs in the Khmer Muslim community through close cooperation with the Ministry of Cults and Religions and the competent authorities at all levels.
Third. The competent authority shall facilitate the construction of the Surah Mosque for the Cambodian Muslims by strictly enforcing the notification on the construction of religious places of worship in the villages where the Khmer Muslims live in accordance with the law. Islam is defined and practiced technically by the competent institutions.
Fourth. Increase social activities through humanitarian work, education, development and religious activities based on the principles of Islam and in accordance with the Constitution.
Fifth. Please have confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government, which has guaranteed the right to freedom of religion in Cambodia through solidarity with all religions for religious harmony.
Sixth. Continue to cooperate nationally and internationally to raise funds and techniques to support the development activities of the Khmer Muslim community, avoiding the use of religion for business, creating problems in the community.
At the same time, Samdech thanked the Cambodian Muslims who believed in the government and voted for the Cambodian People's Party. National Social Protection Fund plans to launch village registration campaign for national social assistance beneficiaries in the family package
