Siem Reap Provincial Health Department Holds a Meeting to Summarize 2023 Work Results and 2024 Work Directions
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Health Department has organized a meeting to review the work results for 2023 and work directions for 2024 for 2 days from March 21-22, 2024 at the meeting hall of Jayavarman 7 Hospital, Siem Reap Province. .
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Koy Sang, Provincial Councilor, Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor and Dr. Kros Sarath, Director of the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, as well as the leaders and health officials of the relevant units of the mayor / district governor. Communes, commune chiefs and many relevant partner organizations also participated.
Dr. Krous Sarath said that the work of providing all kinds of vaccines, nutrition work for infants, children and women of childbearing age has achieved good results compared to last year, and the Department of Health will continue to implement this work in the coming years. Even better.
At the same time, Mr. Pin Prak said that the leaders and civil servants of the Provincial Health Department have united, cooperated and actively made efforts to guide the management and development of health facilities until there is progress, including: Public, local development, providing quality, efficient and virtuous health care to the people of Siem Reap.
Mr. Pin Prak also expressed his appreciation to all the leaders of all provincial health departments who performed their roles well in their respective skills with high responsibility. And many activities and achievements, such as: education activities, health promotion and prevention of communicable and non-communicable diseases in the community, and work to strengthen the health system, the provincial health department has implemented the work plan well. .
He said that the provincial health department has deployed staff and midwives with the right skills in health centers to reduce maternal and infant mortality. In addition, people are well aware of the living conditions of eating in order to reduce the risk of infectious and non-communicable diseases, especially the referral system is ready.
Japan provides nearly $ 80,000 grant for roof construction at wheelchair basketball court in Battambang province
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Cambodia, has signed a grant of US $ 76,333 to a recipient under the Grants for Small-Scale Cultural Project (Kusanoni).
The grant agreement was signed on March 21, 2024 by Mr. Ou Nou Atsusi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and Ms. Sisowath Kanthiret, President of the Cambodian Wheelchair Basketball Federation (CWBF). Roof construction at the wheelchair basketball court. Recipient: Cambodian Wheelchair Basketball Federation (CWBF).
The grant will be used to build a roof for a wheelchair basketball court located at the Battambang Provincial Rehabilitation Center. Because the venue has no roof, wheelchair basketball players have less time to practice in the morning or evening when the sun is not too hot, or may not exercise at all when it is raining.
Through this project, we expect athletes to be able to train at any time of the day or night, regardless of the weather, and to lead the wheelchair basketball team to better results in future international competitions. . In addition, we strongly expect that more people will be interested in sports and through sports they will live in a healthier society in the future.
Japan's "Kusanoni" small-scale cultural project directly contributes to the promotion of culture, sports and higher education activities, as well as the preservation of cultural heritage by non-profit organizations active at the grassroots level in developing countries.
On that occasion, the Japanese Ambassador stated that the grant for this small-scale cultural project supports local authorities and NGOs in implementing projects that directly contribute to the promotion of cultural activities, sports and higher education. Such as the preservation of cultural heritage in developing countries. He hopes that more Cambodians will be interested in sports and will live in a healthy society through sports.
Ms. Sisowath Kanthyret said that this support will enable us to carry out training activities with a good field and provide opportunities for athletes to compete at both national and international levels. This commitment is an important part of strengthening cooperation and solidarity through sports activities, and we are honored to have the Embassy of Japan as a partner in this mission. Third party
