This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet presided over the Ramadan Vegan Dinner
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, the 12th day of the month of Phalkun, the year of Panchasak, BE 2567, corresponding to March 21, 2024, corresponding to the 10th day of Ramadan, 1444 Presiding over the Khmer Muslim vegetarian meal. The event was held at the Chroy Changvar International Convention and Exhibition Center, with about 6,000 Khmer Muslims in attendance.
From March 12, 2024 in Cambodia, and in some countries starting from March 11, corresponding to the first month of Ramadan, 1445 Muhammad, the era of Muslims in Cambodia, as well as Muslims around the world are fasting. Drinks, etc. From dawn to dusk for more than 14 hours, with changes in some areas for a month a year, which is the fourth of the five obligations of Muslims.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Founder of Peace and National Unification of Cambodia, is a leader with a broad-minded leadership philosophy and deep feelings for all people, regardless of race, color or religion. This non-discriminatory leadership views the Cambodian people to live together in harmony, regardless of their religious beliefs.
Samdech Techo, although the national leader is a Buddhist, but Samdech has organized and invited to have a vegetarian meal with Khmer Muslims starting in 2014. As of 2024, the event has been held eight times, while in 2020, 2021 and 2022, it was missed due to Kovid 19 disease. The National Vespers in Cambodia is also considered to be one of the largest government-sponsored Vespers in the world.
Although the Royal Government of Cambodia was born out of the Cambodian People's Party and was replaced by the Prime Minister, the policy of religious unification was still a necessary policy for the new government led by Samdech Manet. Samdech Thepdey continued to follow the guidance of Samdech Techo and continued to participate in the Khmer Muslim vegetarian meal.
The presence of Samdech President Hun Manet at the vegetarian dinner is a clear demonstration of Samdech's concern for the Khmer Muslim community, and there is no policy of prejudice or discrimination against any religious practice in Cambodia.
Ramadan is the ninth month in the Islamic lunar calendar and is considered the lord of the other months. Because the lunar calendar year is 11 days shorter than the solar calendar, Ramadan revolves around each season.
In addition, this fasting is fasting during the forbidden time from dawn to dusk. During the day, one should not eat, drink or have sexual intercourse, while menstruation of women also violates this fast. However, unintentional or forgetful eating is not considered a break or a break in fasting.
* Fasting is not a punishment
On the other hand, this endurance is not only a reduction in the fulfillment of bodily needs from eating and drinking more or less, but it is a commitment between the body and cleansing the spirit from material needs, patience. Have control over lust or hunger, and especially the practice of dharma discipline as an apostle who adheres to the right doctrine.
* Other practices during Ramadan
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, the 12th day of the month of Phalkun, the year of Panchasak, BE 2567, corresponding to March 21, 2024, the 10th day of Ramadan, 1444 Presiding over the Khmer Muslim vegetarian meal. The event was held at the Chroy Changvar International Convention and Exhibition Center, with about 6,000 Khmer Muslims in attendance.
