His Excellency Hun Manet Presents Some Recommendations to Contribute to the Promotion of Persons with Disabilities in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): 2024 Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has made a number of recommendations to contribute to the promotion and care of people with disabilities in Cambodia.
He said the new government will continue to pursue policies and policies to continue to support people with disabilities without disregarding those with disabilities. Strengthening the disability sector now is a joint effort to increase hope for all people with disabilities, courage and to promote the rights, freedoms, dignity of people with disabilities, as well as to change positive thinking with virtue. For people with disabilities.
In order to contribute to the promotion of people with disabilities in the community in the process of socio-economic development as much as possible, Samdech provided the following recommendations:
First. I would like to recommend to the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and relevant ministries and institutions to participate and prepare all legal standards to ensure that the National Center for the Disabled Techo Sen is a property for our disabled people to use continuously and continuously. Present and future.
Second. All development activities, including social, economic, political and cultural activities, must encourage and promote the maximum participation of people with disabilities at the community level in order to achieve inclusive development in both aspects and roles of Development.
Third. I would like to encourage further cooperation in organizing specialized skills training and using appropriate techniques for the education of people with disabilities to improve the ability and access to high-paying jobs to improve the daily lives of people with disabilities. And better families, as well as enable people with disabilities to participate more fully and equitably in the labor market in the private and public sectors.
Fourth. For the effectiveness of the work, the National Center for the Disabled Techo Sen and the National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia need to have funds to support the development of sports for the disabled, especially to host the 6th Asian Para Games 2029 . At the same time, I would like to agree with the proposal of the National Center for the Disabled Techo Sen and the National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia to establish the "Techo Sen Disabled Sports Fund".
At the same time, Samdech emphasized that at the request of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Yi Veasna and his brothers with disabilities, Samdech agreed to be the Honorary President of the National Center for the Disabled Techo Sen and the National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia.
