ASEAN Foundation Unveils Digital Literacy Research Findings Focusing on Digital Literacy Gap across Regions
Under the heading "One gap or multiple gaps? Meaningful Digital Literacy of the ASEAN Community in Deficit and Response to False Information ”This study demonstrates the digital engagement of the ASEAN Community in need.
This study focuses on their knowledge, skills, experiences and responses to false information in order to establish a basic understanding of the role of digital literacy in recognizing and responding to false information in these communities.
Indigenous peoples, in particular, face problems because their digital skills and limited sources of reliable information make the digital divide even more divisive. Although 62.2 percent of the population demonstrates a high level of critical thinking ability, education plays an important role in determining the ability of Cambodian individuals to access information accurately.
These findings underscore the need for on-demand digital literacy initiatives to address the diverse needs of the Cambodian community, enabling them to take full advantage of the digital economy and effectively combat misinformation.
The ASEAN Regional Conference was also attended by the Chairman of the Board of the ASEAN Foundation, representatives from Google.org, representatives from the ASEAN Secretariat, local partners of the ASEAN Digital Literacy Program, ASEAN entities, regional initiators and digital literacy experts. .
The conference concluded with a panel discussion on "Gap to Empowerment: Strategies for Digital Literacy in ASEAN", which discussed strategies for empowering towards a digital literacy environment, especially among the community. Shortages in the ASEAN region.
Taipei claims 32 Chinese warplanes operate near Taiwan
BEIJING, March 21 (Xinhua) - Thirty-two Chinese warplanes were spotted near the island of Taiwan in the last 24 hours, the second such incident in the past 24 hours, according to the Ministry of Defense. The discovery of such a large number of Chinese fighter jets in 2024. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency.
In the last 24 hours of late January and early February, the Taiwan Defense Ministry also confirmed the discovery of 33 Chinese warplanes near Taiwan, the highest number in the world. This year.
White House says Ukraine can not say when new military aid package will be approved
Kiev: A senior US official said on Wednesday that Washington could not predict when a new $ 60 billion military aid package for Ukraine would be passed by the US Congress. Both agreed as President Zelensky insisted on more Western air defense systems after a Russian missile strike killed five people. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
On Tuesday, Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmytro Kuleba said he was "shocked" that the aid package had not been approved, and on Wednesday stressed that the West had a system in place. Defend the airspace that could save the lives of the Ukrainian people if handed over to his country.
Australia has decided to join the International Drone Coalition to help Ukraine (Video inside) (Canberra) In the war with Russia in cooperation with other Western allies such as Britain and Latvia. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
Ukraine has been relying heavily on using drones to make up for the shortage of artillery to fight the Russian army. During the two years of war, hundreds of thousands of drones have been used on the battlefield in missions ranging from targeting targets hundreds of kilometers away, reconnaissance and attacking enemy forces.
Ukrainian President Recep Tayyip Erdogan has vowed to produce 1 million drones this year. Ukrainian officials told AFP that their armed forces needed between 100,000 and 120,000 drones a month, meaning Kiev needed more external assistance.
Australia has announced its decision to join the International Drone Coalition as Canberra welcomes British Defense Secretary Grant Shapps. In February, Britain and Latvia agreed to lead a joint drone group aimed at supplying thousands of additional drones to Ukraine.
