Ministry of Labor and GIZ Sign Memorandum of Understanding on ASEAN-Switzerland Technical and Vocational Training Initiative
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on Tuesday, March 19, 2024, signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the German Cooperation Agency (GIZ) on the implementation of the ASEAN-Switzerland Technical and Vocational Training Initiative.
The MoU, signed at the Ministry of Labor, will complement the capacity of the Cambodian workforce with low skills or little education to have clear technical skills as a stepping stone to access decent employment opportunities, which is a key factor for development. National society.
Speaking at the bilateral meeting before the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding, the Minister emphasized that this Memorandum of Understanding will complement what the Ministry has trained in the past, focusing on a wide range of target groups and levels of training.
The Minister emphasized that the effort to train the people is a preparation for Cambodia to leave the low-income country to the high middle-income country by 2030 and the high-income country in 2050.
