Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth chairs the 11th National Social Protection Council meeting to review and discuss the draft "Roadmap for Global Health Coverage in Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Council for Social Protection, on March 20, 2024, chaired the 11th meeting of the National Council for Social Protection. From His Excellency Lok Chumteav, Vice Chairman and Member of the National Council for Social Protection and related working groups.
The purpose of the meeting was to review and discuss the draft "Roadmap to Global Health Coverage in Cambodia" before requesting the high review and decision of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In essence, "Global Health Coverage (IOC)" is a commitment of the member countries of the World Health Organization, including the Kingdom of Cambodia, to providing quality health care services. Equitable to target citizens without worrying about financial challenges.
In this regard, to accelerate this work, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly has designated "the expansion of health care services towards global health coverage in Cambodia" as the first of the six priority policy programs. Also.
This "Draft Roadmap" sets out the priority policy options for the reform of the social health care system and the health system in a multi-sectoral, multidimensional, and comprehensive manner, outlining the direction and milestones of the strategic level for which the relevant ministries and institutions are responsible. Develop a detailed plan for implementation.
As a result, the meeting reviewed and revised the "Draft Roadmap to the CWC", setting out a step-by-step strategic action and priority goals to gradually expand the scope of citizen coverage. Coverage of essential health services, and financial risk prevention and health financing.
