Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Issues Press Release in Case of Building Dispute Dispute, but Chinese Tenants Strictly Refuse to Mediate
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration on March 20, 2024 issued a press release in the case of a dispute over the lease of a building owned by a Chinese national and a Cambodian who owns the site, but under the coordination of the provincial administration. The tenants took a firm stand and refused to compromise, only to finally the court decide to implement a temporary ruling.
On December 2, 2022, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court issued a decision at the request of the landowners, then QIU RUIXIAN appealed to the Preah Sihanouk Court of Appeal on the decision of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, but as a result On 15 May 2023, the Preah Sihanouk Court of Appeal upheld the decision of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court.
On October 31, 2023, the Sihanoukville Investment Promotion Team, together with the Ministry of Economy and Finance, invited the two sides to reconcile to find a win-win solution for both parties. Still can not find common ground.
Please be informed that on the morning of March 20, 2024, the Bailiff of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court led the implementation of the Provisional Judgment of December 2, 2022 of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court on the above dispute site. . Three Japanese companies interested in investing in Cambodia after meeting with the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association organized a four-day business visit to Japan under the leadership of Mr. Pech Bolen, President of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association.
During the business visit, the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association met with three potential Japanese companies, three of which have expressed interest in investing in Cambodia.
Attending this General Assembly to celebrate the achievements of a group of young Japanese entrepreneurs, expanding the network, promoting cooperation and business opportunities between Cambodia and Japan, as well as entrepreneurs from ASEAN countries who came to celebrate this event.
The conference is a valuable opportunity for association members to connect with young entrepreneurs from across Asia and potentially promote new ventures and new partnerships.
Mr. Oknha Pech Bolen and the delegation of the Association paid a courtesy call on Mr. Tuy Ry, Ambassador of Cambodia to Japan. The meeting discussed the facilitation of an exchange of views regarding the current investment climate and potential opportunities in both Cambodia and Japan.
On March 18, 2024, the leaders of the Young Entrepreneurs Association of Cambodia paid a visit to three potential Japanese companies in Tokyo, where they expressed their interest in expanding their business to invest in Cambodia and ASEAN region as well.
The overall purpose of this business visit is to look at the overall management of the company, the production process, the management of the technology and the entry and exit of each company's products. In addition, the three companies also shared their interest in investing in Cambodia, seeing the potential of using Cambodia as a production base to distribute to a wider ASEAN market.
This interest is due to their view that Cambodia has a favorable investment law and attractive policies and is an important strategic location in the region.
Expansion of the Association's priority business market to support small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) in Cambodia in order to expand business partnerships and investment, both locally, regionally and internationally.
The Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association has promoted collaboration and initiatives among entrepreneurial members to promote the provision of business-to-business (B2B) services, including the promotion of business innovation and interest in business ventures.
Over the past 10 years, Japan-Cambodia trade has grown significantly, with the two economies benefiting from business opportunities and international trade cooperation between the two countries.
The Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association was established in September 2009 by a group of young entrepreneurs from different sectors of business in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Srey Isanvarman Museum of Economics and Monetary Affairs of the National Bank of Cambodia (USA) and the Banking Association of Cambodia (ABC) have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to promote understanding of economic and monetary history. Of Cambodia and the educational experience of Cambodian youth through the combination of cultural expression with knowledge.
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was officially signed on March 20, 2024 with the participation of Dr. Chea Serey, Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
This Memorandum of Understanding marks a new era of cooperation aimed at benefiting students in public educational institutions.
This pioneering initiative leads to the promotion of understanding of the economic and monetary history of Cambodia and the educational experience of young Cambodians by combining cultural expression with practical knowledge.
The Memorandum of Understanding underscores the Cambodian banking sector's commitment to corporate and social responsibility, especially the creation of a sustainable and environmentally sound financial environment through education.
Through this Memorandum of Understanding, several key initiatives were highlighted: 1. Joint Fund for Study Tours: The Banking Association of Cambodia will call on its members to provide funding to support visits to the United States Museum. By providing additional study opportunities to students at public educational institutions across the country.
2: Twice a year visit: The agreement includes the arrangement and financing by the Banking Association of Cambodia directly for a double visit to the US Museum for students in public education institutions in 2024, provided A unique opportunity for hands-on learning about Cambodia's monetary history and financial principles.
3. Promoting corporate social responsibility in the banking sector of Cambodia: This partnership will also focus on promoting corporate social responsibility efforts in the banking sector of Cambodia, especially the role of the banking sector in promoting Financial knowledge.
Through this initiative, we coordinate our efforts in line with the Cambodian Sustainable Financial Principles of the Banking Association of Cambodia, highlighting the role of the banking sector in capacity building and raising awareness for a sustainable and inclusive future.
Dr. Chea Serey stated that an understanding of general history, especially economic and monetary history, is essential for the younger generation to understand the past and to provide a basis for decision-making for the present that will determine the future of the country. We. In this sense, it is important that everyone should gain knowledge through education and culture, both inside and outside the school.
Raymond Sia, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that education enhances knowledge and this collaboration is a direct investment in the future stability, robustness and financial resilience of the banking sector as well as the well-being of the Cambodian people.
"This significant collaboration will provide an opportunity for public institutions to bring thousands of students to the U.S. Museum in the coming year," said Bless Gillion, co-director of the U.S. Museum. I would like to thank the support of the Banking Association of Cambodia and its members for their commitment to promoting financial education, which is a key factor for sustainable economic growth in Cambodia. ” .
This Memorandum of Understanding is effective immediately and will be valid until December 31, 2024, subject to renewal.
