Samdech Hun Sen Presides Over 13 Recommendations to the Ministry of Rural Development to Promote Environmental Rural Development and Improve Livelihoods in Rural Areas (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia 13 points to the Ministry of Rural Development to promote sustainable rural development and improve living standards and reduce poverty in rural areas.
These recommendations were made on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Rural Development on the afternoon of March 20, 2024.
He said that in order to promote sustainable and sustainable rural development in terms of economy, society and culture, he would like to make the following recommendations:
First. The Ministry of Rural Development must prepare a policy on rural development 2025-2035 and a policy on rural roads as soon as possible to be used as a legal document on professional work and promotion of rural development.
Second. I would like to encourage the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to pay attention to strengthening the quality of rural roads through efforts to study, research and develop, build, repair, upgrade and improve rural roads through new technologies, especially to pay attention to construction. Upgrading and improving rural roads to withstand climate change and other disasters to ensure long-term quality of use.
Third. The Ministry of Rural Development must cooperate with the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the budget for the maintenance and repair of high quality rural roads and ensure the use of all seasons, especially rural roads that have been paved with two layers of rubber, to meet the principle Of the Royal Government is to improve the quality of 70% and expand connectivity by 30%.
Fifth. Relevant ministries and institutions and local authorities at all levels must participate in preventing all overweight transport activities of all types of vehicles on rural roads and must cooperate in educating and disseminating to people living on both sides of rural roads to stop deleting Drainage canals on both sides of the road, which affects the quality of the road.
Sixth. I encourage the Ministry of Rural Development to cooperate with the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and relevant ministries to review their jurisdiction to avoid overlapping jurisdictions that hinder or delay supply. Water for people in rural areas.
7th. The Ministry of Rural Development must continue to improve and improve the living conditions of the people in rural areas by strengthening the implementation of existing mechanisms to achieve the goals of the political program of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly for the construction and Homeland Security 2023-2028, set by 2030 to achieve 100% water and sanitation coverage throughout the country.
8th. The Ministry of Rural Development must continue to promote and expand rural economic diversification activities to improve livelihoods and reduce poverty in rural areas by promoting employment, entrepreneurship and economic activities, and vocational training for job creation and income generation through Model village development as well as development and conservation of indigenous communities.
10th. The Ministry of Rural Development must continue to expand and strengthen good cooperation with stakeholders, such as development partners, local and foreign NGOs, the private sector and friendly countries, to mobilize financial and technical resources to support development. Rural development.
11th The Ministry of Rural Development shall study, collect and manage statistical data on the economic, social and cultural situation in the rural areas of the Kingdom of Cambodia, including mountainous areas, highlands and lowlands.
12th. I would like to recommend the Ministry of Rural Development to focus on short, medium and long term plans on rural development to improve the economic, social and cultural situation of the general rural population, including ethnic minorities in the Kingdom of Cambodia. Gradually, poverty and differences between rural and urban areas.
