* Samdech Maniphat Hun Manet stated that rural areas of Cambodia have been changing and changing from day to day and are moving towards development and civilization in all fields.
* Samdech Maniphat Hun Manet stated that the coverage rate of clean water and toilets has increased by about 85%, which confirms the comfortable living of the people in rural areas, including occupations and economic activities to increase income, raise Raise living standards and contribute to poverty reduction.
* Samdech Thep Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, has been leading the country on the right path, continuing the historical legacy from the Royal Government of the 6th legislature, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen who led Cambodia to achieve complete peace and development in all areas throughout the country.
* Samdech Thep Hun Manet stated that the new Royal Government is committed to maintaining peace and implementing major reform programs in order to serve the national interest as well as respond to the requests and needs of the people, despite An environment in which the world is changing and uncertain.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the new Royal Government has set out a number of policies to develop in rural areas to reduce the living gap between people in rural and urban areas.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that by 2023, the Ministry of Rural Development will build more than 50,000 kilometers of rural roads, covering more than 70 percent of the country.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the new Royal Government will continue to develop more rural areas to improve the lives of people in rural areas.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government aims to build a rural town, which is a project to better organize rural villages.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that the policies set by the Royal Government are for the people. This confirmation responds to the opinion of a citizen that the Royal Government does not do what the people want.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet said that this year, Samdech attended the closing of the conference in almost all ministries because it was the first year of national leadership to show up and thank civil servants. From next year will be represented by the Deputy Prime Minister.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to pay attention to the construction of roads that have not yet been built, to strengthen the quality of existing roads, and to continue to pay attention to the construction of clean water networks and toilets for people in rural areas.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet encourages the Ministry of Rural Development to continue to pay attention to strengthening the quality of rural roads through efforts to study, research and develop, build, repair, upgrade and improve rural roads through new technologies, especially attention To build, upgrade and improve rural roads resistant to climate change and other disasters to ensure the quality of long-term use.
Samdech Hun Manet said that the Ministry of Rural Development must cooperate with the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the budget for the maintenance and repair of rural roads to be of higher quality and ensure the use of all seasons, especially rural roads with double asphalt. Then, in response to the Royal Government's policy is to strengthen the quality of 70% and expand connectivity by 30%.
* Samdech Hun Manet said that the relevant ministries and institutions and local authorities at all levels must participate in preventing all overweight transport activities of all types of vehicles on rural roads and must cooperate in educating and disseminating to people living in Both sides of the rural road to stop the removal of drainage canals on both sides of the road, which affects the quality of the road.
* Samdech Hun Manet encourages the Ministry of Rural Development to cooperate with the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and relevant ministries and institutions to review their jurisdiction to avoid overlapping or slowing down each other's competencies. To supply water to people in rural areas.
