Banning water spray, powder, gambling and explosives in the pagoda during the upcoming Khmer New Year
(Phnom Penh): All pagodas across the country will not be allowed to play dangerous games such as spraying water, throwing powder, mart powder, gambling and explosives on the occasion of the upcoming Khmer New Year. . This is according to the instruction of the Ministry of Cults and Religions on March 20, 2024.
Therefore, the Ministry of Cults and Religions has taken strict measures to avoid any bad incidents in the pagoda, which is a peaceful place, by instructing all pagodas not to have all of the above activities. In addition, the Ministry has instructed all pagodas to pay attention to inspiring caution in burning candles, incense burners, stoves and other fire extinguishers to ensure the safety and security of all monks and all citizens.
All pagodas, centers of the Vipassana Center, Buddhist hermitages must hold the relics of Samdech Akka Moha Sangkha, President of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Dr. Tep Vong, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and celebrate the birth and dedication of the body of Samdech Preah Moha Sang Sang Reach Tep Vong.
However, the Ministry of Cults' directive is aimed only at pagodas, while last year, as in the past, water spraying was observed in some public places, especially in Provinces with a lot of tourists.
