If you do not visit the Kokotuhai Commune Museum, you will not know that the commune, which now exhibits the beauty of modern Chinese-style modernization where humanity and nature coexisted peacefully more than 70 years ago, is a quiet "sea of minerals". The unfavorable living environment, almost all construction work depends on human strength, however, it has supported China's first star to rise in space.
Under difficult conditions, a large number of rare earth metals were extracted, providing valuable raw materials for the development of China's new technical and scientific industries. In the 1960s and 1970s, China researched and developed the first satellites, the first hydrogen bomb, the first nuclear-powered submarine, all of which were inseparable from the mine's contribution.
At that time, the number of trucks and sacks loaded with ore was still limited, and most of the transportation work depended on manpower. Thus, handmade cowhide baskets became an important means of transportation. Cowhide baskets of different shapes and sizes, the smallest can hold more than 10 kg of ore, the largest can hold more than 100 kg. In winter, you can drag on the snow, in summer you can carry it on your back.
Raw cow hides are very hard, miners have to carry heavy weights and walk about 800 meters to reach the storage station. The backpack left a lot of bruises on their backs and shoulders. In the icy mines, people are busy carrying endless ore because they know that they have sacrificed more sweat, directly cutting off external pressure for the motherland.
The country has developed because there are patriotic fighters of all nationalities in all fields. Chinese President Xi Jinping has repeatedly stated that solidarity is the spirit of the Chinese people, as well as the Chinese Communist Party, the great family heritage of China.
