(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, has expressed his heartfelt congratulations to Vladimir Putin, who has received popular support for his re-election as President of Russia.
In a congratulatory message to Putin, the president described the victory as a strong testament and recognition of the work that Putin has brought to the Russian nation.
In this message, the President also highlighted that since the beginning of the relationship 70 years ago, Cambodia and Russia have enjoyed the traditional relationship of warm and genuine friendship, bound by strong emotions of political trust, respect and respect. Understand each other based on common values and common interests.
He expressed confidence that through joint efforts, Cambodia and Russia will be able to use the potential of cooperation and partnership between the two countries in the existing field and in the future.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen announced his readiness to work closely with Putin and the Russian government to mark a new era of improved Cambodia-Russia relations for the benefit of the two peoples and to bring new fruits. Further achieve peace, harmony and prosperity for the region and the world.
Putin has been given the opportunity to lead Russia for another six years after receiving nearly 90 percent of the vote in the recent three-day presidential election.
With this victory, Putin will be able to stay in power until at least 2030. With another term in office, the 71-year-old Putin becomes Russia's longest-serving leader in more than 200 years. This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet closed the meeting of the Ministry of Rural Development
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Wednesday, March 20, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, will preside over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting. Work direction 2024 of the Ministry of Rural Development.
The Ministry also has the role of managing, leading and responsible for the implementation of multi-family rural development programs at the village, commune level, including rural roads, rural water supply, primary health care, community development and rural economic development, in collaboration with relevant institutions and promote the organization and strengthening. Rural development structures at all levels, especially rural development committees at the local level.
In order to achieve the ambition of the Royal Government on rural development and improve the living standards of the people, the leadership of the civil servants of the Ministry of Development, which is the staff, has made great efforts to pay attention to their roles and responsibilities and has achieved beneficial results. For the nation and the people continuously from one mandate to another and from one year to another.
According to the report presented at the job review meeting, in 2023, the Ministry of Rural Development has achieved a lot of work on rural development work as follows:
In particular, in 2023, the Ministry built 2,016 water wells, 316 community ponds, 105 rainwater catchment tanks, 2 community drinking water production stations, and community water distribution system. 127 places, built 28,641 household toilets, 78 public toilets and 2,399 public hand washing facilities, and educated 313 people on sanitation with 15,978 participants.
These achievements have increased the coverage of rural water and sanitation to about 85% in 7,397 villages, 654 communes, 59 districts and 7 capitals / provinces (Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang, Kep). And Phnom Penh) have completed the completion of open defecation.
Fourth, Institutional Strengthening: The Ministry pays attention to and supports the implementation of the Royal Government's in-depth reform programs and strengthens the capacity of civil servants at both the national and sub-national levels to serve the people in rural areas more effectively, honestly and effectively. High responsibility.
The Ministry has completed the preparation of the Rural Development Strategic Plan 2024-2028, the draft Rural Development Policy 2025-2035, established the IT and Digital Working Group to participate in the implementation of the digital government policy of Cambodia 2022-2035 and support the Royal Government's Pentagon strategy. In order to serve rural development in accordance with digital policy.
At the same time, the Ministry is also active in analyzing the functions of the Ministry and its subordinate institutions to participate in the implementation of public administration reform and public financial reform.
