Interior Ministry Spokesman: 76 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on March 19
(Phnom Penh): At least 76 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on March 19, 2024 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on March 20, 2024.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 76 suspects, 67 were arrested in 22 drug cases and nine were arrested in 10 criminal cases.
Phnom Penh Capital Hall Organizes Workshop on Reducing Plastic Waste on "Today I Do Not Use Plastic Bags"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Huot Hay, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, on behalf of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, on March 19, 2024, presided over a workshop on reducing plastic waste under the theme "Today I do not use bags. "No plastic." The workshop was held at Phnom Penh Capital Hall with the participation of Mr. Keat Rainsy, Director of Phnom Penh Department of Environment and more than 500 teachers from public and private schools.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Huot Hay said that today the use of plastic bags has increased significantly since the import of plastic to Cambodia more than 25 years ago. In this sense, to prevent the use of plastic bags, people should participate in the implementation of four methods, including: 1: Refuse to use plastic bags or do not accept plastic bags, Second: Reduce the use of plastic bags, Third: Reuse And 4: recycling.
In addition, he urged stakeholders to educate and disseminate knowledge on reducing the use of plastic waste through the "Today I do not use plastic bags" campaign in public and private educational institutions.
At the same time, Mr. Keat Rainsy, Director of the Department of Environment of Phnom Penh, said that from the opening day of the campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags until March 18, 2024, the Department of Environment has launched this campaign in all 249 public educational institutions. From kindergarten to high school, 53 out of 509 private institutions in Phnom Penh and 29 factories, with a total of more than 2 million participants.
Ministry of Water Resources announces weather condition in Cambodia for March 20, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for March 20, 2024.
The Ministry states that low pressure will continue to cover the Kingdom of Cambodia, Thailand, the Gulf of Thailand, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea. This situation will make: From March 20 to 22, 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 26 ° C and maximum temperature 37 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest have an average speed of 2 m / s. In the northwestern lowlands of Battambang, Pursat, Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap, about 20% of the area is likely to receive rain.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 38 ° C. Winds from the east and southeast have an average speed of 2 m / s. In the northwestern highlands, Pailin and Oddar Meanchey provinces may receive about 15% of rainfall.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many: Good leadership requires a clear vision, skills and a gentle and thorough attitude.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the training workshop on "Leadership and Innovation 6th Generation" at the Royal School of Administration this morning, March 20, 2024, Mr. HUN Many, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Function The public and the chairman of the Royal School of Administration have stated that leadership needs to have three factors: a vision, skills and a gentle but thorough attitude.
Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many added that this training workshop was organized to provide knowledge support and skills development in human resource management, detailed management leadership, organizational change, co-operative and highly productive workplace. By providing the necessary resources to meet the needs of senior civil servants in ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels.
He added that the sixth generation course, like the previous generation course, is a six-week course online from today and one week directly at the Royal School of Administration.
