Foreign Minister: Despite global instability and complexity, Mekong-Lanchang cooperation continues to grow
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, expressed his strong belief in Mekong-Lanchang cooperation, saying that despite the global instability and complexity, "Mekong-Lanchang operations continue to grow steadily."
The head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps said this in a message congratulating the "Week of Mekong-Lan Chang Cooperation 2024" from March 18 to 24, 2024.
Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation was established in Sanya in 2016 with the participation of China and five ASEAN countries, including Cambodia, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and Thailand, with the aim of promoting peace, stability and development in all areas. Sector as well as building a community with a common future of peace and prosperity for the people of the region and the world.
