(Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has said that about $ 150 million in Japanese aid will be used to build regional hospitals in Kampong Cham and Siem Reap to provide better services to the people. While the two regional hospitals will appear in the next two or three years.
This statement by Samdech President Hun Manet was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Health on Tuesday afternoon, the 10th day of the month of Phalkun, the year of Panchasak . 2567 is on March 19, 2024.
Samdech Hun Manet added that the efforts to strengthen regional hospitals are to alleviate the difficulties and overcrowding of national hospitals, especially to alleviate the difficulties of people who are sick so that they do not have to travel far to receive treatment. Until Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet said that in the future, the Royal Government will establish regional hospitals in other places for the health of the people must dare to invest. So in the future, if there are serious patients such as heart surgery, cancer who live in the provinces can also treat their disease in the provinces where they live.
According to Samdech Manet Hun Manet, the efforts to develop hospitals at the regional and provincial levels will also reduce the gap in medical standards for the people. As for the work to improve the health sector in Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working since the previous mandate and will continue to do so in order to improve the well-being of the Cambodian people.
Samdech Hun Manet claims that the construction of regional hospitals in Kampong Cham and Siem Reap is worth $ 141 million, so it is expected that in the next two or three years, some patients will be able to treat their patients in the hospital. These two regional doctors do not have to travel long distances to the National Hospital in Phnom Penh.
Samdech Mani Hun Manet continued that the strengthening of the health sector in Cambodia from one mandate to another mandate to have the ability to treat people and decentralize responsibilities and the ability of doctors to the local step by step. This is what the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party wants.
According to Hun Manet, for the further development of the national society, the Royal Government of Cambodia has paid attention to two areas in all areas, including further expansion of positive achievements and reduction of negative points. That existed in the past. In particular, for the health sector to increase positive achievements is to increase the capacity to provide health services to be more quality and comfort to people everywhere.
"In the work to increase the positive achievements in the health sector, we focus on strengthening this capacity should follow two approaches," he said. "The bottom-up approach and the top-down approach."
In this regard, the Prime Minister of Cambodia explained that the bottom-up approach is to strengthen the capacity to provide basic services by strengthening the health units from the grassroots level. The direction of the first rule to strengthen the health center to the district referral doctor is a necessary task, including the quantity and quality of doctors, as well as the quality of medicine and medical equipment.
Samdech Hun Sen said that the top-down approach must be implemented step by step to strengthen the top-down approach to modernize and diversify the medical treatment capacity of doctors at the national, regional and provincial levels. While the Royal Government of Cambodia has been continuing to build infrastructure to serve this sector as well.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also claimed that in the future, the Royal Government will establish regional hospitals in other places, because for the health of the people, the state must dare to invest.
