(Banteay Meanchey): For the upcoming Khmer New Year, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration has imposed a strict ban on those who play patrol, spraying water and throwing dangerous water on public roads and some other inappropriate activities that affect That person's rights will be dealt with in accordance with the law.
In the morning meeting on March 19, 2024, Mr. Oum Ratrey, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, strictly forbade young men and women from throwing water on public roads, pouring drums and drinking alcohol. Lola in public.
He stressed that the three armed forces and the Unity Command of the districts must guard all lanes day and night to strengthen security during the three-day Khmer New Year in Banteay Meanchey province traditionally.
He also warned young women who like to dress sexy and come out to visit during the Khmer New Year, spraying water or watering powder or playing other games to dress appropriately and respect the traditional Khmer law. Key Remarks by Samdech Hun Sen Manet on the Occasion of Closing the Meeting of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, the 10th day of the month of Phalkun, the year of Thao Panchasak, B.C. 2567 On March 19, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Health.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet on the occasion of closing the meeting of the Ministry of Health:
* President Hun Manet stated that the crisis of Kovid 19 has severely affected our health sector, which requires strengthening the resilience of the health system in response to any possible public health threats or emergencies. Will happen eventually in the future.
* President Hun Manet stated that the 19 epidemic of Kovid has demonstrated the ability of Cambodia's doctors and health sector to save lives.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Kovid 19 outbreak also showed some shortcomings in Cambodia's health sector.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that strengthening the health sector is based on two approaches: bottom up and top down.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that strengthening from the bottom up is strengthening the basic services, primary services, referral services, strengthening the quality of medicines and medical equipment.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that strengthening from top to bottom is the modernization of medical equipment and diversification of medical capacity at the national, regional and provincial levels.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Japanese grant of about $ 150 million will build regional hospitals in Kampong Cham and Siem Reap to provide better services to the people.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that in the future, the Royal Government will establish regional hospitals in other places. He said that for the health of the people, they must dare to invest.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that training human resources in health is a necessary task.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet said that some doctors are not good, but many doctors are good professionals.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Health, on the basis of a clear functional analysis, must continue to review, adjust its role and restructure the Ministry and the health unit in line with the new turning point of the public administration reform process.
Samdech Hun Manet said that the Ministry of Health must continue to evolve the health vocational training system and program, as well as teaching methods for basic training and follow-up training in a realistic approach that focuses on building knowledge, skills and multidisciplinary skills. Sure, as well as cultivating a culture of good ethical practice.
Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Health Professions Committee has a very important role to play in strengthening the capacity of the health care system in the public and private sectors and to support the Ministry of Health's efforts to build and develop health human resources. With high knowledge, real skills and good ethics now and for the future.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Health must continue to promote the transformation of digital health to become a people-centered health care service through the adoption of adaptive and inclusive use of digital technology. And effectively in collaboration with the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications to develop a digital health ecosystem that operates efficiently and effectively.
