Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Confirms Implementation of Law on Protection of State Land in Kulen District and Applies Only to Violent and Armed Authorities
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, said that the implementation of the recently registered state land protection law in Kulen district is the authority of the authorities to implement only those who have committed violence and armed. On the authorities only.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that Seila Damix registered 6371 hectares of state land in 2017 on a total of 9,000 hectares and cut 2,440 hectares in 2012 to 770 families through the tiger skin formula and land reserve. 182 hectares of social land concessions for the poor.
He said that during the operation from March 6, 2024, 33 people were arrested, six of whom were educated to return home, while those who responded with the police using various means such as knives, axes and forks. Rubber and gas bottles thrown at the authorities, etc. are carried out in accordance with the law.
He said that the implementation of the law by the authorities, we did not use violence against the people by the accusation, the authorities use the right to defend themselves by throwing smoke bombs to disperse those anarchists.
Regarding the death of a woman due to a family dispute to the point of drinking herbicide, Mr. Kim Rithy said that there was no involvement in the case of law enforcement by the coalition forces and his family did not flee to live in the forest He escaped from the pursuit, and as for his family's livelihood, he had a big house and land to enjoy like ordinary people.
He also called on residents who were reportedly fleeing the forest to return to their villages so that children could have the right to go to school and not to take children and women hostage. Project to improve solid waste and plastic waste management in Cambodia has been officially launched.
(Phnom Penh): "Project to improve the management of solid waste and plastic waste in Cambodia" was officially launched this morning, March 19, 2024 at Sokha Hotel Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Mr. Santibandit Mao Chandara, Permanent Secretary of State, represented the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, Abhisit Bandit Sar Sokha.
Speaking at the ceremony, Dr. Mao Chandara stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 6th legislature of the National Assembly, has introduced a policy on urban solid waste management (2020-2030) to ensure that from 2030, solid waste All types of towns will be segregated, packaged, cleaned, collected, transported, used and processed, as well as treated with hygienic and environmentally safe technology.
He added that for the seventh legislature, the Royal Government has set out a pentagonal strategy, the first phase, by continuing to consider improving the quality and efficiency of services to the people as a priority to be achieved. The fourth pentagon focuses on sustainable and environmental development, in which ensuring environmental sustainability and preparing for climate change and promoting a green economy is a priority for the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In parallel, the National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development Phase II (2021-2030) defines urban solid waste management as sub-national administration as a mandatory performance. In the fifth component, focusing on the promotion of public services and local economic development.
