Ministry of Rural Development Holds a Meeting to Summarize 2023 Work Results and 2024 Work Directions
According to the Minister, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, who continued the historical legacy from the Royal Government of the 6th legislature under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has launched a political program for construction and Defend the motherland 2023-2028 to continue the historic mission and to continue to build a peaceful, independent and developed Cambodia.
With this, the Royal Government has identified five key priority areas, including people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology, with the goal of transforming Cambodia into a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2030. 2050.
In line with the strategy of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Rural Development has been actively involved in improving the quality and value of life of people in rural areas with a comprehensive economic, social and cultural environment to achieve development and live in harmony. And civilization, outlining four key strategies:
First. Develop physical infrastructure and rural communication so that all villages have access roads and become integrated rural areas, especially areas with high economic potential.
Second. Improve the living conditions of rural communities by educating the mindset so that rural people can change their behavior and live in good hygiene and comfort.
Third. Diversification of rural economic activities through training of basic skills, life skills to create jobs and occupations, to increase income in addition to agriculture and to reduce poverty and live in prosperity. In addition, the Ministry has focused on establishing model villages based on economic and tourism potential and favorable conditions in rural communities and especially indigenous communities.
Fourth. Strengthen institutions at both the national and sub-national levels, especially the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration policies, as well as strengthen the capacity of civil servants in order to serve the people in rural areas with high integrity and responsibility.
The Minister praised the efforts of all officials of the Ministry and highlighted the merits of the previous generation of leaders as well as other leaders who have achieved in many achievements and leadership experience, which is a good example. For the next turn.
