(Kandal): The AG Footwear Cambodia AC shoe factory, which employs more than 2,000 workers in Andong village, Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, was severely attacked by fire at 4:30 pm. On March 18, 2024, the authorities at all levels were shocked to see the rescue intervention led by Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management in cooperation with the Provincial Unity Command.
Speaking to Fresh News, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chhoeun Socheat said on March 19, 2024 that the location of the shoe factory that caught fire was 45-year-old Pol Ramisiphon, who lives in Village 10, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
The General Commissioner claimed that after receiving the news of the fire, the Provincial Administration, District Administration, Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the National Commission for Disaster Management, immediately intervened to rescue.
From the time of the incident until 4:50 a.m. on March 19, 2024, the police were in full control. The reason why the police are difficult to rescue and shoot because of the dark night and the location is difficult to enter. In this case, there is no danger to the life of the worker.
(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment and Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Government Working Group, on the morning of March 19, 2024, on behalf of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inaugurated the Grand Palace and other achievements. In Wat Chrey Bit Meas in Sangkat Suong, Suong Municipality, Tbong Khmum Province.
On that occasion, Dr. Eang Sophalleth said that the most recent achievements in Cambodia today are the efforts of the Royal Government, authorities at all levels and people across the country in general and in particular for Buddhists. Wat Chrey Bit Meas, as well as the philanthropists who came to contribute to the charity ceremony in Wat Chrey Bit Meas and give the pagoda the opportunity to build a good achievement for worship.
Please be informed that Wat Chrey Bit Meas covers an area of about 3 hectares and 20 acres. This pagoda was built by devotees in 1550 until now for about 474 years and under the leadership of 10 chief priests. The construction of this pagoda is to be a place of worship and worship of Buddhists who believe in Buddhism, easy to perform other rituals, and also to be a legacy for future generations to worship.
Before 1975, the entire pagoda had a temple, a Pali school, four schools, two huts, and one chan school, run by Chief Inspector Ma Khieu and sponsored by Mr. Seng Youhat, Member of Parliament for Kandol Chrum District, who helped build the pagoda.
From 1975 to 1979, when the flames of war entered the pagoda, it was almost completely destroyed by the Democratic Kampuchea regime (Pol Pot). It is used to raise chickens, ducks, pigs, horses, cattle and many other animals.
A lieutenant general, deputy director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Police Department, has been remanded in custody in connection with a case of money laundering of more than $ 50,000.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy Chief of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and an Investigating Judge in the case, on the morning of March 19, 2024, decided to detain Major General Eng Savoeun, Deputy Director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Police Department in connection with the fraud case. More than $ 50,000 has been jailed pending further sentencing.
It should be noted that Major General Eng Savoeun, who works in the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Police Department, was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police this morning, March 18, 2024, according to the arrest warrant issued by the investigating judge in connection with the fraud case. More than 50,000 dollars to run to join the National Police.
Speaking to Fresh News, Colonel Sam Vicheka, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, said that the arrested police chief was Major General Eng Savoeun, the deputy director of the National Police Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department. .
The spokesman claimed that the arrest was made in accordance with the arrest warrant issued by Investigating Judge Horm Mengse of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and with the permission of Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Police Commissioner. Phnom Penh, which is operated by the Bureau of Minor Offenses.
After the arrest of Major General Eng Savoeun, the case was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings.
