(Phnom Penh): The tourism sector of the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) is estimated to have a recovery rate of 60.5% in 2023 compared to 2019. The assessment was made at a special meeting of the Greater Mekong Subregion Tourism Working Group on March 19, 2023 in Bangkok, Thailand.
Mr. Chuob Ratana, Director of the Department of Tourism Development Planning of the Ministry of Tourism, said that member countries praised and appreciated Cambodia for restoring the yellowest tourism sector at the rate of 82.4%. After Cambodia are Laos at 71.3%, Thailand at 70.5%, Vietnam at 70% and Myanmar at 30%. On the Chinese side, especially in Yunnan and Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, the recovery rate is still around 3-5%.
"The above documents will be consulted at the regional level to get a consistent input before submitting to the leaders of the GMS countries, decided through the GMS Senior Officials Meeting during August-October 2024. Coming ”according to Mr. Chuob Ratana.
