(Prey Veng): On behalf of the Ministry of Interior and on behalf of the head of the Royal Government's working group in Prey Veng province, Mr. Abhisandith Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, shared his grief with the people affected by the fire in In Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, at 7:20 pm on March 17, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha pointed out that the location of the fire was a flat of two flats with a store selling machinery and engine oil. At that time, the house was locked by the owner on two floors, the front lock on the porch and the key to the house. Seeing the complicated situation and the serious risk of fire, Major General Chhoeun Bunchorn, Commissioner of Prey Veng Provincial Police, ordered other municipal and district inspectorates to release additional fire trucks.
Based on the report of the Major General of Prey Veng Provincial Commissioner, the decision to focus on the target was on fire, which made some people unhappy at that time because the experts clearly concluded that if not put out the fire in two flats in time, the walls on both sides. Will be cracked, causing the fire to continue to spread to the next house. The nearby house also has wooden furniture, medical equipment and a money changer.
In this regard, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha would like to express his gratitude and appreciation to the Prey Veng Provincial Administration, the Provincial Police Commission, the authorities and the Joint Forces, especially the fire brigade, for their professional and dedicated firefighting and rescue operations. "Do not die, do not drown, do not sink the boat in the middle of the river, do not let the house fire" We also understand the feelings of the people.
Death news! Brigadier General Hong Sarin dies at 65 of disease
(Phnom Penh): Brigadier General Hong Sarin, working at the Development Office of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, passed away on Monday, March 18, 2024 at 10:25 am at the age of 75.
The body is kept for a traditional and Buddhist ceremony at Mrs. Neou Narin's address in Yeay Mao Pichnil village, Yeay Mao Pichnil commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province.
This information is considered as an invitation to relatives, friends and the public who know Brigadier General Hong Sarin to attend the funeral for everyone. Lao Airlines resumes flights between Phnom Penh-Vientiane, Cambodia first leg welcomes 116 passengers
(Phnom Penh): Lao Airlines has resumed connecting flights between Phnom Penh and Vientiane from March 19, 2024 onwards to provide convenience to passengers between Phnom Penh and Vientiane with this first leg. Cambodia welcomed more than 100 passengers from Laos. This is according to Mr. Sin Chansery Vutha, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for Civil Aviation.
Speaking to Fresh News on March 19, 2024, Mr. Sin Chanseryvutha emphasized that this first flight was warmly welcomed by Mr. Hul Seila, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, together with the Phnom Penh International Airport. A bouquet of flowers and a bouquet of jasmine for all tourists.
According to Sin Chanserivutha, 116 passengers from Vientiane on the first flight arrived at Phnom Penh International Airport and 86 passengers from Phnom Penh to Vientiane.
The senior civil aviation official said that the re-launch of Lao Airlines flights is a big positive sign for the travel of tourists, business people, businessmen, investors and enhancing relations between the people of the two countries. Such as increasing the attractiveness of more tourists to visit Cambodia.
The announcement of the direct flight connection was made after a working meeting between Samdech Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit, President of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, on the occasion of participating in the "Belt and Road Forum". The third time "in Beijing, the People's Republic of China on the morning of October 19, 2023.
Please be informed that as of the announcement of the Ministry of Health on March 19, 2024, Cambodia found 19 cases of Kovid disease: a total of 139,097 people, a total of 136,040 people were cured, a total of 3,056 people died. . This afternoon, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet closed the meeting to review the work of the old year and raise the work direction of the new year of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, the 10th day of the month of Phalkun, the year of Thao Panchasak, B.C. 2567 On March 19, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Health.
The health sector is a priority that the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party has paid the highest attention since Samdech Techo Hun Sen led the country and continued until Samdech Hun Sen. Improving the well-being of the people, providing better health services to patients is one of the priority policies of the new government led by Samdech Thipadei.
Expanding health care services towards global health coverage is the first of the six priority policies set by President Hun Manet. Through this policy, Samdech President Hun Manet aims to ensure that about 9 million people have access to better health services when they are sick.
In order to achieve the policy of providing better health services to the people, the Ministry of Health is an important agency of the Royal Government in managing and implementing this work.
The Ministry of Health, led by Mr. Mam Bunheng in the old legislature and continued by Mr. Chheang Ra in the new legislature, has actively worked to achieve the ambition to improve the well-being of the people and the quality of health services, which is the desire of the Prime Minister.
At the opening ceremony of the convention on March 18, 2024, the Ministry of Health presented many achievements that the Ministry has achieved in 2023 and laid out more work to continue activities for 2024.
The following are the achievements in 2023 and the work to be carried out for 2024:
+ Expanding coverage of health services
About 2.4 million new outpatient cases were referred from lower-level public health facilities to higher-level health facilities, of which only 4 percent had referrals. As of December 31, 2023, there were 616 ambulances operating nationwide, of which 117 were national.
+ Promoting reproductive health, maternal, infant, child and adolescent / adolescent health and nutrition
Use of reproductive health services, maternal, infant and child health and nutrition is higher than in 2022. Between 2014-2022, infant and child mortality under five years of age achieved the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals ahead of the 8-year deadline. During the same period, the maternal mortality rate continued to decline to 154 (per 100,000 live births), but was still higher than the 2020 Transitional Goal of the Cambodia Sustainable Development Goal 2030.
The rate of use of any modern contraceptive in public health facilities tends to decrease from 21 percent to 14 percent between 2019-2023. Modern contraceptives in use are mostly 51% pills, followed by injections 30%, and condoms around 3%. Cases of abortion and miscarriage tend to decrease between 2020 and 2022, but have increased by about 19% in 2023.
The rate of mother and infant care after the first, second, third and fourth births has increased compared to 2022. There were 2,087 births and deaths, of which 492 were born within 24 hours and 2,025 were stillborn. There were 95 suspected maternal deaths reported from public health facilities.
+ Prevention and management of major infectious diseases
+ Prevention and management of non-communicable / chronic diseases
* The use of outpatient and inpatient services for major non-communicable diseases such as diabetes, hypertension, cardiovascular disease and cancer patients has increased significantly. Between 2022 and 2023, new cases of diabetes examined at public health facilities and hospitalized patients increased by 42%.
Outpatient cases of hypertension in public health facilities increased by 12% and inpatients increased by 32%.
In 2023, the number of mental health examinations will increase by 5% compared to 2022 and the number of hospitalized patients will increase by 24%.
+ Improving the quality of health services * In September-October 2023, the Ministry used the first level 2 quality assessment equipment at 1,281 health centers, 60 first level referral hospitals, 38 second level referral hospitals and third level referral hospitals. 21 points of this evaluation will be used as a starting point for monitoring the progress of quality improvement at the next evaluation.
* 10 health centers were selected as the winners of the 2023 Model Public Service Provider Competition.
+ Development of social health protection system
* The risk burden on health expenditures tends to decrease, with the proportion of people falling into poverty due to health expenditures falling from 3.93% in 2019 to 3.54% in the same period. This data seems to be high compared to other countries in the region.
+ Strengthening the capacity of the health security system
Institutional mechanisms and systems for monitoring and responding to communicable diseases and public health emergencies continue to be proactive and interactive, continuing to control and prevent the spread of new infectious diseases.
* The system for monitoring and responding to diseases and public health issues is regularly strengthened through the 115 hotline system, the zero reporting system, the health event tracking system and the flu surveillance system.
* The quality of laboratory services has been strengthened, the quality management system, external quality assessment program and the process towards obtaining quality certification.
In 2023, total blood donations will increase by 25 percent, and the supply of blood and blood products to public and private hospitals will increase by 30 percent compared to 2022.
* Chattalysak rules at border gates are regularly applied, Chattalisak officials also inspect vehicles and inspect transport facilities.
* Prevention and control of animal-to-human transmission and research and response to food poisoning, monitoring and evaluation of food hygiene and safety have been strengthened.
* Monitor immunity to viruses and antiviral drugs through a network of 9 microbiological laboratories.
For the work direction in 2024, the Ministry of Health has set out as follows:
+ Expansion of health services
Strengthen the role of health centers and referral hospitals at all levels in providing primary health care services.
* Expand non-communicable diseases, emergency services and surgery and other essential services
* Strengthen the referral system for patients or victims in both the public and private health systems.
* Increase educational activities to promote health and manage diseases or health risks
* Promote community participation, relevant sectors, local administration, civil society organizations
* Strengthen human resource capacity, supply of medicines, equipment, medical equipment, budget, improve physical infrastructure and use basic information / digital technology to improve the provision of primary health care services.
+ Improving the quality of health services
* Manage patients according to technical standards at health centers and referral hospitals
* Prevent and reduce avoidable dangers in the process of providing care, treatment and improve the implementation of infection prevention and control measures in all health facilities
* Strengthen the implementation of treatment approaches, care, ongoing treatment and coordination within and between health facilities.
* Continue to strengthen the evaluation and quality improvement mechanisms in health centers and referral hospitals at all levels
* Update standards, technical principles / clinical protocols and monitor implementation
* Strengthen the mechanism for receiving information or feedback from patients / families and reporting incidents that occur in treatment, care and timely resolution.
+ Expanding the coverage of the social health protection system
* Strengthen the implementation and monitor the implementation of the ESS Fund program. And social assistance programs
* Increase awareness of the operation of social health care programs and benefits
* Implement a roadmap towards global health coverage
* Update and calculate the medical expenses of the Equity Fund Program
* Develop a method of paying for health care services that ensures cost-effectiveness and the provision of quality health care in sufficient quantities.
+ Strengthen the capacity of the health security system and essential services * Continue to strengthen the leadership and coordination capacity in response to the emergence / recurrence of infectious diseases or public health emergencies
* Improving the implementation of precautionary measures, prevention, timely and quick response, surveillance systems, network services, laboratories, communication networks, risk communication, etc.
* Prepare medicines, equipment, medical equipment, doctors, staff, appropriate health infrastructure
* Increase education, promotion and monitoring of food safety and monitoring of immunity with antiviral drugs, animal-to-human transmission, prevention and management of disasters and health risks related to climate change.
* Promote the study, research and search for or development of new medical and non-medical rules, as well as regional and global cooperation in the prevention / control of health security threats.
+ Strengthening resilience and modernization of the health system
Review and adjust the structure and role of the Ministry of Health and the central health unit in accordance with the progress of public administration reform and decentralization.
* Develop / update laws, regulations, policies, strategies, plans and technical tools, continue to provide leadership training and innovation to management and management officers, strengthen the implementation of public and private health service regulatory mechanisms.
* Build / develop public-private partnerships and strengthen cooperation with ministries, institutions, national and international development partners and non-governmental organizations
* Strengthen the implementation of mechanisms to monitor and evaluate the achievements of the health system, implement laws / policies / plans, and promote health research / digital health.
* Implement appropriate mechanisms to improve recruitment, allocation and retention of staff, giving priority to health centers / health posts and district referral hospitals.
* Improve the quality of basic and continuing training by focusing on curricula based on knowledge, skills and attitudes and high quality of teaching methods.
* Increase the capacity of the budget unit to analyze and analyze the budget and budget preparation and improve the efficiency of financial management and expenditure and procurement work.
* Strengthen the supply and improve the efficiency of the use of medicines, vaccines, reactors, equipment and medical equipment to health centers / health posts and referral hospitals in accordance with the standard.
* Construction, expansion and improvement of health posts, health centers and district referral hospitals
* Build and develop electronic medical recording systems and integrate information technology systems with a focus on standards and interoperability, system functions, and digital health capacity building and training for health workers.
* Develop institutional structure and capacity for leadership, governance, facilitation and support for the development of digital health ecosystems.
* Strengthen the implementation of health data / information reporting mechanisms from private health care providers in accordance with the procedures in force in the health information management system of the Ministry of Health.
* Support the development of civil registration system and civil statistics
Ministry of Public Works Holds a Meeting of the Working Group to Amend the Road Traffic Law of the National Road Safety Committee
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Mon Manvy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, chaired a meeting to review the new draft law on road traffic with the participation of the Ministry, representatives of the Office of the Council of Ministers, representatives of the Ministry of Interior and relevant officials. Under the guidance of the Ministry.
The meeting was held at the Ministry's office on the afternoon of March 18, 2024, with the meeting approving the old draft, which had already passed the NCDD and was sent back from the office. The Council of Ministers at the end of the sixth term of the Royal Government to review the points that need to be adjusted in accordance with the development of society and economy, maintain good security, order, national traffic safety.
Following this meeting, the working group to study and amend the new draft law on road traffic will submit it to the leadership of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to request the decision of the NCDD to continue the procedure for final approval. As soon as possible to prevent and reduce traffic accidents with high efficiency. Islamic League organizes international conference on bridge between Islamic sects in Saudi Arabia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Member of the Supreme Council of the Islamic League (MWL), Leads a Cambodian Delegation to Lead an International Conference on the Building of a Bridging Bridge between Islamic Sects in Makkah Saudi Arabia from March 17-18, 2024.
The Islamic World Alliance is a large organization founded in 1962 by Faisal al-Saud, a member of the United Nations (UN) Observatory, a member of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC). Headquartered in Makkah, Saudi Arabia, it has offices in 95 countries and partners with major international organizations.
Twelve families sue Battambang deputy commissioner for encroaching on state land given to them in flooded forest area in Maung Russey district
(Battambang): Twelve out of nearly 80 families living in Talas and Chrey communes, Maung Russey district, have filed a complaint with the Land Survey Working Group on the systematic registration of land in two areas in Chrey commune to help find The solution came after a deputy commissioner from Battambang province took professional officers to measure and encroach on about 64 hectares of their land in order to make a solid plan to take ownership of it.
According to Mr. Than Sean, Chrey Commune Chief, this case really happened because on the morning of March 18, 2024, the people and the representative of the Deputy Commissioner came to meet with the Deputy Commissioner. They demanded 60 percent for 40 percent of the people, but the people refused.
The commune chief said that the disagreement was due to the fact that when they cleared all the land since 2008 and enjoyed the actual benefits until the Royal Government announced to the people to recognize, the above person did not come out. However, when the land survey team came to cut the land and make a plan for the people, suddenly the deputy commissioner pointed out to the land survey team to become the owner of the land, and this case is not over yet.
Pursuant to the instructions of the Battambang Provincial Administration in December 2021, all signatures, certificates of recognition of the transfer of rights, purchase, lease, mortgage, land tenure or application for land use, purchase and sale by Self-contact between individual seller and individual buyer and confirmation of location on flooded state land, area 3 in Battambang province.
For the announcement of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction in Chapter 2, Article 4, the registration of plots of land is given to the people as well as the communities who are actually enjoying it, which means that there is no recognition of trade. From the past.
Regarding the land in Zone 2 and Zone 3, the Royal Government of the sixth mandate under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, announced the confiscation of all the flooded forest land and ordered the working group to clear the land for the people to enjoy. Due to this problem, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature is working hard to register systematically.
