Tens of thousands of young people support the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party and the National Strategy for Informal Economic Development 2023-2028
(Phnom Penh): The Youth Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Phnom Penh, especially the activists of the Informal Economic Plan, is committed to implementing the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) and is committed to expanding its membership. More to be a force to help drive the informal economy in Cambodia and to support the CPP as a whole.
This commitment was made in a meeting with about 4,000 informal youth activists of the Phnom Penh CPP Youth Working Group, chaired by Mr. Hem Vandy, Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation at the Koh Pich Theater on the 17th. March 2024.
Mr. Ley Sopheap, Chairman of the Informal Economic Plan of the Phnom Penh Municipal Party Youth Working Group, read out the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party, which includes nine major points, especially the promotion of economic growth in 2024 and the vision of Cambodia. A high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Mr. Ley Sopheap, together with members of the Informal Economic Activists of the Phnom Penh Municipal Party Youth Working Group, pledged to abide by the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) and to work to expand the number of party members. As a force to boost the informal economy in Cambodia and as a voice to support the CPP to grow.
Mr. Nuon Pharath, Vice Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh, expressed his intention to disseminate the contents of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as inform the informal economists about the political program as well as the focus. The attention of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature to those who are looking to eat in the informal economy.
Mr. Nuon Pharath advised to work hard to build more active members of the informal economic plan to be a force to promote the informal economy in Cambodia to be stronger and to support the CPP to grow. In addition, it must join the policy of the Socialist Party. Equity cards and training policies for young people from 1.5 million poor families.
Mr. Hem Vandy expressed his pleasure to meet with the activists in the Informal Economic Plan of the Youth Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh and informed them about one of the six priority policy programs that focus on entrepreneurs. In the field of informal economy through the implementation of the National Strategy on Informal Economic Development 2023-2028.
Mr. Hem Vandy informed that the Royal Government has now established the Informal Economic Development Coordination Committee and is preparing an action plan and data collection mechanism with stakeholders to identify and evaluate a database related to the informal economy before reaching development. Upcoming registration system to set clear goals for receiving practical assistance from the Royal Government.
He said that the activists of the Informal Economic Plan expressed their welcome, understanding of the work of promoting and promoting the Informal Economy of the Royal Government and expressed strong support for the above policy program through the Pay close attention to both the party and the national policy.
Dr. Ley Sopheap also thanked Mr. Suon Rindy, Member of Parliament for Phnom Penh, who always pays attention to the work of building economic youth, supporting, supporting and giving good recommendations to the youth working group of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh.
