The Pakistani airstrikes came just two days after a suicide bomber drove an explosive-laden truck into a military base in northwestern Pakistan, killing seven soldiers.
Both the Pakistani army, the defense minister and the president have vowed to retaliate for the attack.
"It is clear that the recent wave of terrorism in Pakistan has the full support and assistance of Afghanistan," the Pakistani military said in a statement shared on social media X.
"Terrorist incidents in Pakistan have increased with the help of the Afghan Taliban and the supply of modern weapons," the report said.
However, the Pakistani military has not commented directly or confirmed that it has carried out retaliatory airstrikes in Afghanistan, although it has accused the Afghan government of providing safe havens and participating in attacks in Pakistan. .
