Phe Thongthan Sinawattra, President of the Pheu Thai Party, the youngest daughter of Thaksin Shinawatra, who has close ties to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has been visiting Cambodia at the invitation of CPP President Samdech Techo Hun Sen. . The visiting young Thai politician met with Samdech Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Cheam Yeap, Acting President of the National Assembly.
On the afternoon of March 18, 2024, she also paid a courtesy call and discussed work with Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The family-politician meeting discussed much about the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand.
Ms. Phethong Thansinavattra thanked the President for taking the time to allow her and the delegation to pay a courtesy call and congratulated the President-elect on the election of the Prime Minister of the National Assembly. Kingdom of Cambodia, 7th legislature in August 2023.
She also congratulated the success of the Senate election in Cambodia on February 25, 2024. She praised the good relations and cooperation between the two countries, which have brought mutual benefits to the people and the two countries.
She also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and President of the Cambodian People's Party, for inviting her to visit Cambodia. She expressed strong hope that the relationship and cooperation between the two countries would be further strengthened and expanded in other important areas, including the promotion of the role of women.
Samdech Hun Sen President warmly welcomed the visit to Cambodia by Ms. Phe Thong Than Sinavattra and the delegation. The President also congratulated her on her appointment as President of the Pheu Thai Party and sent a message to Thaksin Shinawatra.
He also praised the relations and cooperation between the two countries and informed them of the fruitful results of his official visit to Thailand in February, which contributed to strengthening and expanding relations between the two countries. Both in many areas, including the economy, trade, tourism, employment and so on.
The Prime Minister wished Ms. Phe Thongthan Sinawattra and her delegation success in their visit and enjoyed their stay in Cambodia and safe repatriation. Minister Sok Soken: Cambodia is expected to attract more Indian and Chinese tourists to Cambodia
(Siem Reap): Cambodia expects to be able to attract more quality tourists to Cambodia, while the Chinese and Indian markets are Cambodia's priority tourism markets. This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism.
Mr. Sok Soken also stated that in order to attract more Indian tourists to Cambodia, the government will launch direct flights from Cambodia to New Delhi on June 16.
However, the Minister should not forget in the readiness of Cambodia, with the government, the Ministry of Tourism and all relevant service providers ready to receive tourists, which can ensure that visitors to the country. Cambodia and will return to visit Cambodia again.
The Minister of Tourism's statement was made in response to a question from a group of journalists in front of the Angkor Wat temple, leading the Club of Cambodian Journalists, chaired by Puy Kea, in the "Information Mission to Promote Large-Scale Tourism Potential." Siem Reap province. Minister Sok Soken launches five development strategies to boost Cambodia's tourism sector
(Siem Reap): Minister Sok Soken has set out five strategies and three developments to promote Cambodia's tourism sector towards a new future based on the basic principles of "tourism connects land and nature." This new strategy aims to make Cambodia a leading global tourist destination, rich in opportunities and warmth to contribute to enhancing Cambodia's prestige and resilience.
This strategic plan is in line with the political program of the Royal Government, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly for building and defending the motherland 2023-2028, the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, the main policies and strategic plans related to tourism.
To achieve this vision, three strategic goals have been identified: 1, tourism competitiveness 2, sustainable tourism and 3, tourism environment, and these 3 strategic goals have five strategic pillars called 5-BUILD and There are three priority support activities called Development 3-3Ds.
