Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Ordered Forces to Take Measures on All Types of Vehicles Equipped with Non-Standard Speakers
(Kampong Cham): Pursuant to the order of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the guidance of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, on March 18, 2024, Major General Heng Vuthy, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham In principle, take drastic action on all types of vehicles, especially on trucks equipped with loud-sounding trumpets.
Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy claimed that in recent days, the specialized force of the Land Traffic Police Office of Kampong Cham Provincial Police in cooperation with the specialized forces of the district / municipal police inspectorates has taken measures to stop trucks with the wrong loudspeakers. The technology causes loud noises, disrupts people's lives and affects public order.
According to the commissioner, the specialized force stopped seven vehicles and called the drivers for education and instruction, and required the removal of the wrong technology and did not allow the installation of such systems.
At the same time, the General Commissioner appealed to the people who own all kinds of vehicles not to change the technical standards that lead to traffic accidents and to respect all laws to reduce traffic accidents. Another 260 vehicles were inspected and fined on March 18, 2024
According to the spokesperson, for March 18, 2024, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 6,801 vehicles, including 5,229 motorcycles and 1,572 vehicles.
It should be noted that for March 18, 2024, there were 8 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 3 people were killed and 14 people were injured (8 people were seriously injured). In 18 days, there were 155 traffic accidents, resulting in 91 deaths, 193 injuries (115 serious injuries).
(Phnom Penh): After receiving the Prime Minister's order on the car with the wrong horn, Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, held an emergency meeting to control and prevent anarchy on public roads caused by the processing of all kinds of vehicles, especially Equip these wrong horns.
The meeting was held on the afternoon of March 18, 2024 with the participation of 14 district governors, relevant departments and the Armed Forces under the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
In this meeting, the Governor of Phnom Penh set out three principles:
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the misuse of trumpets and trumpets was a serious disturbance to public order on the streets, which authorities must strictly enforce.
On that occasion, the Governor also issued a circular prohibiting all vendors from stopping the sale of processed cement pipes and trumpets, and if not followed, legal action will be taken by collecting the wrong technical items. That will save and can lead to the closure of the business.
In addition, during the meeting, Mr. Khuong Sreng also urged the 14 district authorities as well as the relevant authorities to review the business of entertainment clubs as well as beer gardens, which cause noise to the people. In particular, all kinds of gambling must also be cracked down on like rain in its base.
At the same time, Samdech President stated that the police in some provinces have taken action by instructing the drivers of trucks to remove the wrong horns and replace the original horns and to stop this activity. .
In order for the implementation of this measure to be more effective and comprehensive, Samdech Thipadei instructed the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the General Commission of the National Police, the Capital-Provincial Authority and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission to cooperate, inspect and provide guidance related to the technical characteristics of car horns. To prevent anarchy on public streets.
In particular, Samdech Thipadei would like to entrust the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Administrative Unity Command to instruct and take strict measures to prevent anarchic activities that affect public order and may endanger the lives of the people. The Office of the Prime Minister presents the results of the meeting between Samdech Hun Sen and Mrs. Phethong Thansinavattra
