Minister of Public Works Highlights 12 Tips for Public Financial Management Reform Working Group to Implement Effectively
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this afternoon, March 18, 2024, presided over the opening ceremony of a seminar on public financial management reform for leaders and civil servants. Ministry with the participation of ministry leaders, representatives of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as many participants.
The organization of this workshop is an important basis for the mainstay of knowledge related to the Public Financial Management Reform Program, such as the leadership structure, the mechanism of implementation of the detailed action plan, which is defined as Work direction and key indicators (KPIs) of this reform program.
In addition, the Permanent Secretary of State briefed on the major achievements of the Ministry's Public Financial Management Reform Working Group and demonstrated the commitment of the Ministry's Public Financial Management Reform Working Group. Continuing to implement the reform program to successfully achieve the reform goals in this fourth phase as an operator.
On that occasion, Mr. Peng Porna stated that the Public Financial Management Reform Program has the vision to transform the Cambodian public financial management system from an input-centric and centralized system to a system that focuses on results or achievements and characteristics. Decentralization in accordance with international standards and practices.
The Minister took this opportunity to highlight 12 key priorities for the Ministry's Public Financial Management Reform Working Group to review, organize and promote implementation, including:
12. Strengthen the monitoring, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of the budget, the achievements of the budget unit under the Ministry.
The Minister also expressed optimism that through today's outreach workshops will be an important part of providing the will, the spirit of reform and a deeper understanding to the leadership and civil servants of the Ministry. Focal officers are responsible for achieving the goal of reforming public financial management.
The Minister urged the leaders in charge of the working group and all relevant key officials to continue further efforts to achieve the Ministry of Public Financial Management Reform work successfully in accordance with the action plan. Work in the fourth phase as planned and achieved results for the Ministry as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia.
