(Phnom Penh): This morning, March 18, 2024, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, gave a speech on the reform of the Gendarmerie to the trainees of the Judicial Police Training. 26th generation at the Royal Gendarmerie Institute.
Also present were the Deputy Commander, Deputy Chief of Staff, Deputy Commissioner, Deputy Chief of Staff, Deputy Director of the Office, Deputy Director of the Institute, Director of the Department, as well as many trainees of the 26th generation of judicial police officers.
General Sao Sokha said that the reform of the Gendarmerie is:
* First: Goal: Maintain the culture, achievements and achievements of the Royal Gendarmerie to be stable, long-term and provide opportunities for successors * Second: Objective: To provide knowledge to give each soldier a correct view and a strong position. Participate and support the reform process * Third: Request: Ensure national unity and the rule of law.
The Commander-in-Chief claimed that, in the words of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Armed Forces participated in the modernization of the structure, modernization of training and modernization of equipment.
General Sao Sokha emphasized that the structure of the Gendarmerie is divided into three parts: operations (roles and responsibilities), support and legislation and control. For the Royal Gendarmerie, there are Headquarters (Commission) and District, Municipal and Khan Units, while the Units are Mobile Gendarmerie, Security Information Unit, Judicial Police Unit, Special Forces Unit, Warehouse, Hospital, and Administrative Command.
