Life in a poor family, working as a laborer, an indigenous young woman overcomes difficulties, seeks to learn makeup skills because she wants a better future
(Rattanakiri): The eldest of four siblings living in a poor family, working as a laborer to earn a living, a young indigenous woman living in Veng Sai district, Ratanakkiri province, decided to drop out of school. 9th grade to become a rubber plantation worker, take money to support their families and help young people to get an education, even if they dream of getting a higher education.
However, Veasna did not harm people, with the support and encouragement of Plan International, including the Ratanakkiri Vocational Training Center (PTC), she was able to pursue a career as a beautician. In the future, through this skill will be able to help her have a clear skill can earn income to support the family without having to be a laborer.
She told Fresh News recently that while she was learning this makeup skill, Srey Mon said that under the encouragement of Plan International, including the Ratanakkiri Vocational Training Center, she was able to enter. Learn a specific skill in makeup, while this skill is also her dream that she had dreamed of learning since childhood.
In this makeup, she has to learn makeup, hair, hair, nails and other make-up, and after more than a month, she knows how to do nails and hair. She is also determined to master the art of make-up in order to open a small self-employed stall to earn a living for the family and to help the three of them get an education.
According to Srey Mon, before entering this profession, due to her family's poor living conditions, she decided to drop out of school in the ninth grade to help her parents farm and work as a rubber plantation worker to earn money to support her family. . After learning this skill, she expects that this skill will really help her to have a decent job and not be as difficult as working as a rubber tapper.
