(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has signed new concessional loan agreements with development partners totaling 1.81 billion US dollars in 2023. This is according to the Cambodian Public Debt Statistics Bulletin issued by the Ministry of Economy and Finance, obtained by Fresh News on March 18, 2024.
In addition, according to the Ministry of Economy, in the fourth quarter of 2023, the Royal Government signed new concessional loan agreements with development partners totaling 779.62 million US dollars, equivalent to 578.15 million SDA.
According to the Ministry of Economy, the above data compared to the same period last year, the signing of new concessional loan agreements in 2023 decreased by about 16%.
The Ministry of Economy emphasizes that "these loans are all high-concessional loans, with an average of 45% of donations."
The Ministry of Economy added that the purpose of these new credit agreements is to meet the financing needs of the Royal Government's priority areas to contribute to sustaining long-term growth and increasing economic productivity or productivity.
Cambodia's current public debt situation is still assessed as manageable, remaining "sustainable" and "low risk" despite the impact of the Cambodian economy on the spread of the Kovid-19 crisis and From other external factors.
