(Prey Veng): A car parts store in Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province was attacked by fire, causing damage to the owner, claiming that about 1 million dollars. This incident happened on the night of March 17, 2024.
According to a report from the Prey Veng Provincial Police, immediately after receiving information about the fire, Prey Veng Provincial Governor Suon Malin led the police force and relevant officials to intervene and extinguish the fire. The house that caught fire was 18 meters by 22 meters and was owned by Khan Phearun and his wife Sorn Sopheap.
During this operation, the police used 15 water trucks, using 52 water trucks and a total force of about 200 people to jointly spray water to put out the fire.
The report claimed that the rescue operation took about five hours to take full control, but also caused four police officers to suffer serious and minor injuries.
Cambodia allows Chinese companies to study Phnom Penh subway project and light rail connecting Phnom Penh and Techo International Airport (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Two Chinese railway companies have received the green light from the Royal Government of Cambodia. Study on the project of subway in Phnom Penh and light train connecting Phnom Penh and Techo International Airport.
After receiving the green light from the Royal Government of Cambodia to study the above important projects, the management of China Metro and Guangzhou Metro arrived in Cambodia to meet with relevant institutions to study the project.
At the beginning of the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol welcomed the delegation of the two Chinese companies with great pleasure. Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that improving the transportation system in Phnom Penh is an important task and is highly valued by the old government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and in the new legislature. By Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that Cambodia has allowed many studies related to this transport, including the construction of air trains studied by Japanese Jaika. However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet are more interested in building subways.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that the subway line in Phnom Penh and the light rail connection between Phnom Penh and Techo International Airport are very important to facilitate travel while traffic in Phnom Penh is more congested. He added that the construction of a subway line in Phnom Penh and a light rail link between Phnom Penh and Techo International Airport has helped the Cambodian economy and the environment.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol instructed the two Chinese companies to work directly with Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, to expedite the study to submit to the Royal Government for review.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also advised the relevant authorities to facilitate the two Chinese companies to study quickly.
China Metro and Guangzhou Metra are companies with many years of experience in railway construction. The company has not only participated in the development of railways in China, but also built railways in many countries.
Representatives of the company expressed their pleasure at the opportunity to study the project to improve the transportation system in Phnom Penh, as well as the connection of the transportation system with Techo International Airport. The company representative announced that with the company's many years of experience, the company will do its best to be responsible and collect good academic results on the above project to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
This morning's meeting was also attended by many representatives from relevant ministries and authorities. In that, the Governor of Kandal Province and the Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh announced that they are ready to cooperate with the company at any time to achieve results quickly.
Ministry of Economy considers building and developing the capacity of civil servants on public financial management skills necessary
He said this on the occasion of the Academy on March 18, 2024, presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2023 course and the opening ceremony of the 2024 course of the "Technical Training Program for Certification of Positions" at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The event was also attended by Undersecretaries of State, leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, representatives of development partners, as well as a group of lecturers and 2023 winners and 2024 target trainees, a total of about 500 people to ministries, institutions, public institutions, administration, Department of Economy and Finance and Capital-25 provincial administrations.
Speaking at the ceremony, the professor emphasized that the training and capacity building of skills related to public financial management has become an obligation for civil servants in public finance to perform their duties in the budget units of ministries-institutions and specialized units. Involved both at the national level and at the sub-national administration.
He continued that in accordance with the spirit of the Law on Public Financial System 2023 in Article 14 stipulates that public finance officials of ministries, institutions, public entities, similar to sub-national administrations and public institutions that have the duty to perform financial work must have Professional qualifications by type of job position.
Vocational qualifications by type of position shall be determined by sub-decree at the request of the Minister of Economy and Finance and the regulations in force. Accordingly, the Sub-Decree on Professional Qualifications in Public Finance was officially signed by His Majesty the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia Hun Manet on March 11, 2024.
Dr. So Sok Bunthoeun, Senior Public Sector Specialist of the World Bank and Representative of Development Partners in the Kingdom of Cambodia, expressed his support for the building and capacity building of public finance professionals for the implementation of the Financial Management Reform Program. Public objects of the Royal Government to achieve effectively.
