Dr. Chea Serey said, "Sending children to school is not only an obligation for every parent, but also as a way to save money for their children and effectively save their lives from poverty, as the saying goes. "Education is a bridge to the future. I want to have tomorrow until I prepare today."
Dr. Chea Serey made this remark on the occasion of her meeting with teachers and students of Snor-Khlay Primary School in Kampong Thmor Commune and Banteay Yom Reach Primary School in Prasat Commune, Santuk District, Kampong Chhnang Province on Sunday, March 17. 2024.
Dr. Chea Serey brought a message from Dr. Chea Chanto, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Member of the National Assembly of the 7th Legislature, and Ms. Khieu Sina to Mr. and Mrs. Teachers and nephews. All as well as the local team and the National Bank team.
