Ms. Bandith stated that in addition, sending children to school is also a contribution to building and developing the society for a long time, because the children are studying now will be a strong pillar of quality in various fields. And you can also become a leader in the future, so you need to continue to send your children to school and help encourage your children and create conditions for them to continue their education, both sons and daughters equally.
She strongly encourages sending girls to school to receive a full education, as women play a very important role in the development of Cambodian society as well as raising Cambodia's profile on the international stage. In fact, in the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, women have been given more important positions and responsibilities in both the public and private sectors, in which Cambodia has a female National Assembly President and Minister.
