(Phnom Penh): March 18, 54 years ago, was a day when a group of politicians, including Prince Sisowath Sirimat, Lon Nol, In Tam and Cheng Heng ... committed conspiracy. The coup overthrew Samdech Norodom Sihanouk from the post of Sangkum Reastr Niyum head of state. Starting from that illegal coup d'etat, it led to Cambodia experiencing the greatest tragedy because of the flames of war.
Dr. Ros Chantraboth, a Cambodian historian, highlighted that there were two factors that led to the coup. Both of those factors include external and internal factors of Cambodia.
Cambodian historian Dr. Ros Chantraboth emphasized that despite Samdech Norodom Sihanouk's efforts to declare Cambodia's neutrality, the United States and its allies tried to put significant pressure on Norodom Sihanouk's regime. Until a serious economic crisis.
As for the internal factors, Dr. Ros Chantraboth reminded that during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, there were many Khmer groups that acted against the leadership, such as the Khmer Rouge movement, the Viet Minh movement, and the Khmer Serei movement. All the movements of the Sangkum Reast regime have resulted in armed clashes, unrest, insecurity and instability.
The Doctor staged a coup d'état to overthrow Samdech Norodom Sihanouk by Prince Sisowath Sirimatak, General Lon Nol In Tam and Cheng Heng, because of the thirst for power and the hunger for dollars of this group of politicians, forgetting the hardships of the nation and the people. People. According to Ros Chantreabot, the Khmer Republic regime of General Lon Nol was one of the most corrupt.
On the day of the bitter history of Cambodia, Dr. reminded the Cambodian people today to monitor the development of the situation in the region and the world of the superpowers. In addition, be balanced and considerate, do not do anything according to the instigation of politicians.
With the commemoration of the day that led to the flames of war in Cambodia, Dr. also mentioned the achievements and advantages of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who issued a mission and political philosophy to end the war, bring peace and Strong national development.
The Cambodian historian, who went through many Cambodian journeys, called on the Cambodian people, especially the youth, to unite the vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to ensure peace and progress. . 54th Anniversary of the Coup: Additional Mystery Behind the March 18, 1970 Overthrow of Norodom Sihanouk
(Phnom Penh): March 18, 2024, this is the 54th anniversary of the coup d'etat (March 18, 1970) to oust Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk as the head of state and as a cause to bring Cambodia into the eyes. The flames of civil war spread throughout the country, leading to the killing field regime.
On the occasion of the 54th anniversary of the coup d'état overthrowing Prince Norodom Sihanouk on March 18, 1970, Fresh News would like to share a deeper story with readers Behind the coup.
The visit of the Dulles in 1955 was seen as the starting point for the implementation of political pressure on the Kingdom of Cambodia to turn the island of peace into a liberal bloc against the communists. From then on, coercion and pressure on Cambodia continued to flow for about 15 years until their success on March 18, 1970.
In the face of the Cold War context, in order to avoid Cambodia from the flames of war and to maintain a balance between the liberal ideological bloc and the communists, as well as in order to reduce political pressure from the United States and Seattle, Prince Norodom Sihanouk decided to opt for a neutral political line. Coalition. He actively increased diplomatic activities with countries with similar policies to Cambodia.
The first meeting with the Chinese Prime Minister in Bandung was seen as a starting point for pursuing a neutral policy by balancing the two ideological blocs, and was the first day that would move Cambodia to the brink of collapse. War, too.
China, on the other hand, seems to consider Cambodia as a strategically important country, and Cambodia's neutral foreign policy is even more important for communist China, which can help China escape its own stock. Surround another level.
Washington seems to see Thai and South Vietnamese pressure along the border with Cambodia as an effective weapon that could be used to force Prince Norodom Sihanouk to return, but it is a misconception.
Faced with the above state of emergency, Prince Norodom Sihanouk asked the United States to use its influence to persuade Ngo Dinh Yeam to withdraw its troops from Cambodia. But US Ambassador to Cambodia Carl Strom replied, "The United States can not intervene in the conflict between its two friendly neighbors."
Reacting to this frustration, Prince Norodom Sihanouk has openly stated that "not allowing Cambodia to use auxiliary weapons to confront the enemy means that the United States is sinking Cambodia and pushing the country into the hands of the social bloc." "Definitely popular."
Another project was an armed uprising to seize Siem Reap and Kampong Thom provinces, as well as plans to establish separatist territories under the leadership of Soeng Ngoc Thanh, Sam Sary and Dap Chhuon. In the actual operation, Ngoc Thanh mobilized Khmer Serei forces along the Cambodian-Thai border, accompanied by two Thai officials and more than $ 1 million in cash (currently more than $ 9 million) provided by the CIA.
Authorities also found documents and arrested two South Vietnamese officers, as well as radios, which could be used as evidence of Washington, Bangkok and Prey Nokor interference in their internal affairs. Cambodia, but the US government refuses to accept the truth for fear of embarrassment in front of the international community.
While some traitors were arrested, Dap Chuon was shot by the authorities in Sre Noi (now Sre Noi commune, Varin district, Siem Reap province) and brought to trial in Phnom Penh. The traitor was shot dead and his body was dragged slowly by car throughout Phnom Penh with loud loudspeakers saying, "This is the result of a traitor."
Finally, while Prince Norodom Sihanouk was on a royal visit to Moscow, Russia, the planned meeting was hastily implemented, with the March 18, 1970 coup overthrowing Prince Norodom. Sihanouk, from the position of head of state to the Sangkum Reastr Niyum, also came into being in an instant.
After the coup plan was completed, the plan to establish the Khmer Republic was immediately implemented. The United States was the first country to recognize this new government.
