Preah Vihear provincial authorities claim that a citizen who took his own medicine after committing a family crisis was not involved in the joint law enforcement case
(Preah Vihear): Preah Vihear provincial authorities have confirmed that a villager who committed suicide by drinking herbicides in Kdak village, Sroyong commune, Kulen district, on March 15, 2024, started from a family crisis not related to the implementation of measures. The law of the coalition forces.
The revelations came after foreign media outlets, including some on social media, reported that a woman ran into the forest and drank herbicide after authorities cracked down on Sela Damex.
According to the authorities, the woman who drank the herbicide named Hem Ley lives in Kdak village, Sroyong commune, Kulen district. According to the information from the husband, Nuon Heng, son-in-law, Sokha Yap Piban, and the village chief, Nuon Yun, confirmed that the victim really died from drinking weed.
Authorities confirmed that he had a family crisis on the day of the March 9 incident, with his wife arguing and arguing. The son-in-law stopped him and took his father-in-law home in the village. After the son-in-law returned to the farm hut, he saw his mother-in-law was unwell and sent him to the provincial hospital for treatment.
