(Phnom Penh): A fire engulfed a house of a villager, completely damaging one house and spreading to two houses, causing damage to a hotel and some broken glass and upstairs.
This incident caused a surprise to the people and the authorities called the fire truck to intervene and spray water at 10:00 pm on March 17, 2024 at house 42, street 19, village 9. Sangkat Chey Chumnak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh.
In the above operation, the competent force used 15 fire trucks, including 11 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Office, used 11 water trucks, and 1 auxiliary vehicle from the Cambodian Beer Company used water. One car and three OCIC cars in Koh Pich did not use water. The fire was extinguished at 10:30 pm the same day.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that the fire was caused by an electric shock that caused the fire. In it, no one was injured and the lives of the people were not affected.
