MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia on Sunday ordered an increase in naval forces and training to counter the threat of drones and Ukrainian air strikes following a series of attacks on ships. Its warriors. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on March 17, 2024.
Russian Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu said in a statement during a visit to the Black Sea Fleet in southern Russia that "there should be regular staff training. "Training on how to counter air strikes and drones."
The statement added that Shoigu "ordered the deployment of additional weapons to the navy, especially large-scale machine gun systems, to defeat enemy drones."
The Black Sea has been a major battleground in the conflict for the past two years, with Ukraine claiming to have destroyed dozens of Russian ships.
Ukrainian officials have achieved military success in the Black Sea as their ground forces are often forced to withdraw or defend themselves in eastern Ukraine.
