Phnom Penh Municipal Court Detains 3 Chinese and 1 Malaysian for 6kg of Drugs and Money Laundering
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has issued arrest warrants for 3 Chinese nationals and 1 Malaysian national in a drug case weighing about 6 kg and money laundering offenses. This is according to the press release of the spokesperson of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
According to the press release, there are five defendants, including:
Criminal offenses punishable under the provisions of Article 40, Article 42, Article 44 and Article 71 of the Law on Drug Control and Article 38 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing.
