The first business forum of 2024 of the Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships Cambodia helps to build a relationship between participants for business owners and operators
The Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association of Cambodia is a former association of participants of the Southeast Asian Youth Ship and Japan Program, a large regional youth exchange program established in 1974 and with about 12 young people from ASEAN and Japan. 000. Cambodia fully participated in the program in 2000, after which the Cambodian Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships was established in 2004.
The theme of the forum is "Business Sustainability for Small and Medium Enterprises: Solving Financial and Other Challenges." In a highly uncertain global environment, after the effects of the 19-year Kovid disease and the ongoing war in the world, small and medium enterprises are increasingly focused on ensuring business sustainability.
The key to building a business that is more resilient, sustainable and profitable is valuable knowledge and experience in responding and assisting enterprises in this critical time. In this forum, some topics were presented and debated with the coordination of Mr. Seang Sopanha, Director General of Cam-ASEAN International Institute and former President of this association. Those topics include:
The outcome of this discussion is expected to be knowledge and experience, which is an important input for business owners and operators to implement in their enterprises.
