The Governor of Sangkum Thmey District underlined: “Apart from Wat Techak Rainsy called Wat Boeung, which we are meeting now, there is also continuous progress, as we inaugurated a beautiful gate in the presence of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province last year. And now we have a joint flower festival to collect money to build a temple in the town to grow even more.
The Governor of Sangkum Thmey District presented the monks and informed the civil servants, the people must join in solidarity to develop the Rainsy Temple called Wat Boeung to be developed as a shrine for monks and Buddhists near and far. On behalf of the Sangkum Thmey District Administration, he also contributed 51,000 Riels to the Solidarity Flower.
Russia's presidential election enters final day as Moscow accuses Ukraine of trying to disrupt its election process
Russia on Sunday kicked off the last day of the presidential election as Moscow accused Ukraine of using airstrikes in an attempt to disrupt its elections. This was released by Reuters on Sunday, March 17, 2024.
Putin has also vowed to retaliate against Ukraine. According to Russian officials on Sunday, Ukrainian forces appear to be continuing their offensive on Russian areas near the Ukrainian border. Kiev considers the election to be held in its Russian-controlled territory illegal and invalid.
A total of more than 114 million Russians are on the voter list, and as of Saturday evening, more than 63 million of them have already cast their ballots, according to the Central Election Commission.
