The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, with the invitation and participation of government officials, monks, people near and far.
Achievements in Wat Chan Rainsy Nimit, also known as Wat Chhnoun, which has been under construction since May 11, 2019, include: Plans at a cost of 185 million riels, the roof of the temple at a cost of 40,000 dollars, bathroom 5 costs 17 million riels, pouring land in the pagoda costs 15 million riels, pouring concrete roads costs 2,615 dollars.
On this occasion, Mr. Hor Bun Hour brought greetings from Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Mr. Ouk Kimsan, Chairman of the Provincial Working Group to Rovieng District to provide monks and people present here as well. People all over Rovieng district.
The Governor of Rovieng District congratulated the monks and the people on the achievements in Chan Rainsy Nimit, also known as Wat Chhnoun, which was held today. He considers these achievements as collective achievements made by the participation of monks, local authorities, people near and far.
Mr. Hor Bun Hour presented the monks and informed the people about the value of peace, which gave us the opportunity to get together, have the opportunity to build common achievements, especially for the development of the whole country in all fields.
He also called on the people to continue to work together to maintain lasting peace under the wise leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to support the Royal Government's political programs, especially the policy of safe villages and communes. All 7 points.
