Speaking on this occasion, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun said that the solidarity and good cooperation between the party working group and members of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Party Committee at all levels serve the people responsibly in accordance with the policies and good deeds of party officials. It is an important factor in gaining the trust of the people and a major factor in the victory of the Cambodian People's Party in the past.
He encouraged all members to continue this wonderful tradition and work together to serve the people to the best of their ability. The victory that the CPP has won in every election is not just a victory on the ballot, but a victory for the Cambodian people across the country.
On that occasion, Mr. Chiang Am commended all the working group and members of the Cambodian People's Party in Ratanakkiri Province for their hard work, dedication, and budget for the cause of the people and to continue to work closely with the Party Committee. Provinces, municipalities, districts and communes, branches, villages to continue to serve the people in Ratanakkiri better in accordance with the spirit of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party.
In order to work more effectively, the team leader has prepared a plan for the team for further implementation, including:
1: Continuing the work of assigning grassroots working groups in cities, districts, communes, sangkats and adjusting the composition of the working groups to visit local municipalities, districts, communes and sangkats.
2: To continue to disseminate the political program of the party launched through the first phase of the Pentagon Strategic Political Program and to implement the main tasks, including:
The Pentagon Strategy, the first phase of the seventh legislature of the National Assembly, focuses on the five priorities "people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology." The army is not neutral to the Royal Government, neutral to political parties. "
Phnom Penh Municipal Court Holds Trial in Case of Fraud on Japanese Investor in Land Purchase in Kampong Speu Province
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court heard the case of fraudulent Japanese investors in the land purchase and sale of land in Kampong Speu province's Thpong district last week and will announce the verdict at the end of March.
According to the explanation from the victim and the Japanese plaintiff, Ms. Thong Sok Kheng and the above party, including other stakeholders, have obstructed and disturbed all forms of his investment project in the past.
In fact, his border post was completely destroyed by 2020. Not only that, during the survey to find the border post again, the representative of the landowner was sued by the above group, alleging that his group had entered to destroy their property.
Even more shocking is the fact that 16 chicken farms worth more than half a million dollars, which were already disrupted, were completely burnt down by unknown people in the middle of the afternoon. On February 28, 2024, just before the trial in the case of Ms. Thong Sok Kheng, only about a week.
Currently, a Japanese investor (Khmer nationality) has been unjustly accused of swindling 328 hectares of land from Ms. Thong Sok Kheng and a party member in a case of violent encroachment on 117 hectares of land by a group of people. .
Separately, one of his representatives, a Cambodian national, was the victim of a criminal case No. 1371 dated November 26, 2020 at the Kampong Speu Provincial Court from a group of abusers.
In addition, the victims as investors have lost a lot of time, capital and investment opportunities in the agro-industry, services, education and lost opportunities to attract other Japanese investors to invest in business in Cambodia.
Japanese investors and his representatives would like to respect the institutions of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Provincial Court of Kampong Speu, especially Samdech Hun Sen, please provide justice to him and his colleagues so that he has the opportunity to contribute to development with The Royal Government of Cambodia through the private sector. "How should people be careful not to suffer from being attracted to investment" Please wait to watch the Fresh Talk at 6 pm.
