(Phnom Penh): The spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on March 16, 2024 issued a press release rejecting and completely rejecting the broadcast that the arrest of the interim deputy chairman of the National Forces Party of Kampong Cham is politically motivated.
In a press release, it was stated that the spokesperson of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police was honored to inform the public about the arrest of Mi Seng Hor (aka Kea Visal), a 59-year-old Cambodian man, currently the Interim Vice Chairman of the National Forces Party. Kampong Cham Province as follows:
On March 12, 2024, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police received a complaint from Mai Hong Sieng against Kea Visal, the owner of the Facebook account named Mi Seng Hor (aka Visal), male, occupation, Interim Vice Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial National Forces Party. Current address: Concrete Road, Koh Pen Village, Koh Mit Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province.
After receiving the complaint from the victim, the competent authorities researched, collected evidence, specific information on incitement to cause discrimination and public insult, and reported to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
With the permission of Mr. Seng Heang, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued an arrest warrant No. 175 AYON dated 15 March 2024 in connection with the case of incitement to discrimination. And publicly insulted and arrested Mi Seng Hor (aka Kea Visal), a Cambodian male, in Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province.
Currently, the suspects are being processed by the competent authorities and sent to the court for processing. The arrest was made by law enforcement authorities without any other reason related to intimidation or intimidation of any political party activist.
The spokesperson of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission, please completely reject and reject the baseless and baseless allegations of the National Forces Party, published on March 15, 2024. Cambodia, China Hold Meeting on Cambodia-China Railway Cooperation Mechanism
