The working group mentioned in this law points to four types of violence: 1: Physical violence (any act that affects the body, such as punching, pushing, using weapons, knives, guns, can affect life. Life), 2nd: Psychological violence (refers to any harassment, emotional abuse, insulting words, 3rd: sexual violence and 4th: economic violence.
The settlement of violence involves a mechanism by way of going to court, in the event that the act is serious, causing serious injuries, loss of life, can be sued in court. In particular, out-of-court settlement involving psychological and economic violence is not a serious crime, it is a criminal offense, family members can rely on the village chief, commune chief, authorities.
