In order to achieve the above solution, Mr. Chea Somethy provided 9 recommendations for stakeholders to participate in the implementation. The nine recommendations include:
1. Co-study, prepare and revise legal documents, including: Take appropriate action against ministries, institutions and legal entities that do not fulfill their obligations, recruit people with disabilities to work and provide allowances, policies, food and travel expenses. People with disabilities come to receive services at the capital-provincial rehabilitation centers in accordance with the actual economic situation of the country.
2: Improve the quality and modernization of artificial prostheses, satellites and physical support equipment with standard quality to meet the needs of the rehabilitation center in the country and have a basis to compete in the free market and export to export. .
3. Strengthen and expand rehabilitation services for people with disabilities with quality and timely, as well as increase the provision of rehabilitation services in the community to make it easier for people with disabilities to access services.
4: Examine and improve the location of the physical infrastructure of the Capital-Provincial Rehabilitation Center in accordance with the development of the country.
5. Continuing good cooperation with relevant partner organizations that support the field of rehabilitation.
6: Increase the construction of houses for people with disabilities in the community more than in previous years.
7. Strengthen good cooperation with partner organizations, stakeholders and the private sector to study and promote various investment projects through legal business to mobilize financial resources to support the disability sector.
8: Strengthen the management and increase the donation box of the Fund for the Disabled in the capital-provincial branches to mobilize financial resources to support various projects that help people with disabilities and ensure the sustainability of rehabilitation work. People with disabilities get better.
9. Study, research and evaluate people with disabilities in the community to promote the implementation of funding projects or loans, provide vocational training and create suitable jobs for people with disabilities to improve their lives.
