Invest in China! Global Media Dialogue on "China in the Spring" Held in Chicago, USA
BEIJING, March 13 (Xinhua) - The "Spring China" dialogue between the world's media was held at the University of Chicago in Chicago on March 13, 2013, hosted by the National Radio and Television. Central China and coordinated by the Chicago branch of the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in the United States.
Last year, China's economy grew by 5.2 percent, accounting for a third of global economic growth. A global referendum conducted by the Central Radio and Television of China (CGTN) found that 93.1% of global respondents noted that the Chinese economy was strong, with great potential for recovery. "China's opportunity" can not be missed, China is still China!
National and international speakers agreed that the high-quality development of China's economy has a bright future, expects Sino-US economic and trade cooperation and China-US people-to-people exchanges will become more frequent. .
