He added that pastor leaders not only fulfill the role of disciple-making for Jesus, but also for the ministry in all respects, because the pastor is close to the people, so there must be good cooperation with local authorities to help restore common sense. And fill the gaps as much as possible, such as humanitarian work, charity, etc. Contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia to reduce poverty in the community.
Please be reminded that the consultation meeting was held at the office of the Cambodian Christian Association (EFC) with a total of 120 participants from 25 provinces, capitals of Cambodia.
