(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has found that in recent times, logging, encroachment, burning or clearing of forest land in protected areas is in violation of the provisions of the law in force and is using the land that is under Proceedings of the judiciary.
In this regard, in order to continue to strengthen the management of state land and forest resources in protected areas, the Ministry of Environment would like to introduce the following measures:
First, the relevant authorities to manage the protected area must continue to enforce the law 100% without any exceptions and end the culture of contracting and releasing the perpetrators.
Second, the relevant authorities shall immediately dissolve and stop the signing of the letter or document requesting the use of the land, the purchase and sale letter, the transfer letter of the occupation or the confirmation of the map showing the location of the land within the protected area.
Third, individuals who commit acts of clearing or encroaching or clearing, burning or clearing forest land for ownership are natural resource offenses that will be punished in accordance with the provisions of the law in force.
Fourth, the person who committed the act as stated in the third point above must return the land he has occupied to the competent Ministry of Environment voluntarily and unconditionally.
The Ministry of Environment has been cooperating with the relevant ministries, institutions, relevant authorities and sub-national administrations to take the strictest measures to prevent, eliminate and suppress all illegal activities in protected areas in accordance with the laws and regulations. Effective.
