(Phnom Penh): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia on March 14, 2024 issued an official press release on the results of the two-day Central Committee meeting.
The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) has convened its Central Committee meeting under the chairmanship of HUN Many, President of the Youth Union of Cambodia. Also present were His Excellency Lok Chumteav, Vice President and members of the Standing Committee, as well as members of the Central Committee and distinguished guests from 13 to 14 March 2024 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The purpose of this meeting is to monitor the progress of the work on the decisions of the General Assembly, strategic plans and other programs that the CPPCC Achieved in the past, as well as to set priorities and direction the activities to continue and find additional inputs to link the work plan in line with the actual development of society.
The Closing Ceremony of the Central Committee Meeting of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia took place this morning, March 14, 2024, under the high presidency of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
Addressing the members of the Central Committee and the ceremony, the Prime Minister praised and appreciated the work activities of the Central Committee and the CPPCC. At all levels in the past, which has contributed to raising the image of the country and join the Royal Government in serving the nation, motherland and people.
