Mr. Om Mak Thearith, Director General of the General Department of Public-Private Partnership, Ministry of Economy and Finance, explained that BOT is a type of project specified in the Public-Private Partnership (PPP). In a BOT project, a private partner is authorized to design, build and operate project assets. For example, a power station, road, or bridge that requires a fee to be collected from a fixed period of use.
The private partner is responsible for financing the project and is authorized to collect utility fees from users of the infrastructure or users of the project for the period specified in the PPP contract. At the end of the contract, the private partner must transfer the rights and project assets back to the relevant institution (government).
In general, BOT projects are a specific type of project under the PPP framework, while PPP contracts can take many different forms depending on the agreement between the relevant institution and the relevant private partners. Stung Treng Governor Instructs Officials to Increase Control on Illegal Gambling and Crimes
(Stung Treng): Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Provincial Governor and Chairman of Stung Treng Provincial Administrative Unity Command, on March 14, 2024, instructed officials to pay more attention to management, monitoring and action. It is necessary in accordance with the law in time for the lucky adventure game in Stung Treng province.
According to the provincial governor, currently the types of lucky games that are allowed to run in Cambodia include: scratch card, lottery and lottery, which is a game with a long history and a game based on luck. Purely.
"Regarding gambling and lottery, I would like to recommend that you take action to control and manage all licensed gambling companies and lotteries, and especially not to create new ones," he said. In particular, companies whose licenses have expired must end and cease to operate.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang said that the drug problem must also be strengthened, controlled and prevented by starting drug testing from civil servants of the provincial administration as well as the armed forces, and in case of drugs found in the body. Legal measures must be taken and evicted from the framework. He also recommended intensifying the investigation of drug traffickers to bring them to justice.
