Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet: Youth play a central role in maintaining old achievements and continuing to build new achievements
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovarit Hun Manet, considers the youth to be the key players in safeguarding the hard-won national achievements of the previous national leaders. Not only keep the old achievements, the youth are also the key players in building more new achievements for the motherland.
The Prime Minister made this remark while closing the meeting of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) this morning, Thursday, March 14, 2024.
The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia is the largest public service youth organization in Cambodia that has contributed to the mission and duties of social, humanitarian and for the cause of the motherland through volunteering, regardless of political affiliation, class or religion.
In front of the leadership of the members of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, who are also civil servants in the national leadership, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet reminded the deepest gratitude to the former Cambodian youth who volunteered to sacrifice their lives. Fresh blood, starting the national liberation movement to save Cambodia from the abyss of death and has continued to protect, restore and develop the country until today.
The Prime Minister also highlighted that the youth have been playing a central role and participating in the national cause of the motherland to develop the country in all fields by continuing to maintain the achievements of the previous generation, leaving more positive achievements and organizing A solid foundation for the next generation.
The Prime Minister also praised the efforts of the leadership of the CPPCC. All levels, as well as all members from the central level to the grassroots level, who have fully participated in the effective implementation of the "Youth Strategic Plan for the Motherland 2023-2028".
