(Phnom Penh): EU Commissioner for International Partnership (JICA) Juta Aphel Lainin has reaffirmed the EU's strong support for strengthening and expanding bilateral relations in all areas with Cambodia, an important and trustworthy partner.
The EU position was confirmed during a meeting with the head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps on March 13, 2024, during a two-day visit to Cambodia.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that during her first visit, Ms. Lainin acknowledged the remarkable achievements in Cambodia and expressed the EU's strong support for strengthening and expanding relations. Bilateral in all fields with Cambodia, an important and trustworthy partner.
She expressed high optimism that the implementation of the Global Gateway Program in Cambodia and the EU Initiative in Cambodia will help encourage and attract more EU investors to Cambodia. She said it was ready to provide the necessary support for Cambodia's exit from the least developed countries.
