BANGKOK: Thai Prime Minister Setha Thavisin said this week that Thailand expects to conclude free trade agreement negotiations with the European Union by 2025 as the government seeks to attract trade and investment to boost the economy. .
Reuters quoted Thai Prime Minister Setha as saying in a press release after meeting with French President Emmanuel Macron during a visit to France that the talks The free trade agreement between Thailand and the EU should be completed within a year.
The free trade talks resumed last year after a stalemate for nearly a decade, according to Reuters. The European Union suspended talks in 2014 after a military coup overthrew a civilian government in the Southeast Asian country.
