(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out in a house of a villager, causing complete damage to two houses and to the surprise of the people and the authorities, calling the fire truck to intervene and spray water. This incident happened at 1:20 AM on March 13, 2024 at the intersection of Tumnup Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that in accordance with the order of Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy National Police Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. Instructed the specialized force of the Office of Fire Prevention, Rescue and Rescue to pay close attention to the rescue operation in a timely manner.
Upon receiving the order, Colonel Prohm Yorn, Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, directed the fire brigade stationed at all targets to intervene in a timely manner. The fire continued to reach nearby houses.
In the above operation, the competent force used 19 fire trucks, including 15 fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Office, using 15 water trucks, and 1 auxiliary vehicle from the Cambodian Beer Company, using all the water. 1 car and 3 OCIC cars use 3 trucks of water. The fire was extinguished at 2:30 a.m. the same day.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that the fire was caused by burning garbage, causing a fire. In it, no one was injured and the lives of the people were not affected.
At the same time, Colonel Prohm Yorn called on all citizens to be extremely careful. Due to the hot weather for a while, people before leaving home to the recreation area and to work to turn off the electricity properly before leaving home.
