A new concrete bridge in Srayong commune, Kulen district, which was built by the great solidarity between the monks and the people, is scheduled to be completed soon.
(Preah Vihear): A new concrete bridge built by the great solidarity between the monks and the people at the reservation point in Romchek village, Srayong commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province, is scheduled to be completed and officially inaugurated at the same time. Coming soon.
Venerable Kim Raksmey, a resident of Khnong Koul pagoda in the upper commune village, who is the founder of this concrete bridge, said on March 13, 2024 that the construction of this concrete bridge will start on February 15, 2021. Construction will be completed before the end of March 2024 and the inauguration ceremony will be held soon.
Venerable Kim Raksmey also confirmed that the new concrete bridge is 5 meters wide and 21 meters long, and the bridge is built to replace the old wooden bridge across the stream, which is in poor condition, making it difficult for people to travel during the rainy season. As well as transporting various agricultural products.
Venerable Kim Raksmey had a priest show the difficulties from the construction of the first bridge until the completion of the bridge. However, he also thanked the local authorities, Buddhists near and far, both inside and outside the country, who participated in the construction of this bridge to complete the total cost of $ 55,000, but so far. He still lacks another 8 million riel to cover the cost of construction materials.
