6 months: Ministry of Labor provides physical examination services to nearly 300,000 Cambodian workers
(Phnom Penh): From September 2023 to February 2024, for six months, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training provided public services to 286,254 Cambodian workers through screening and certification. There are 197,577 female employees.
In addition, the Department of Labor Medicine of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training provided training on occupational health and safety to 1,428 delegates, including 829 women. In addition, the Department of Occupational Medicine also provided training on occupational safety and health to workers, delegates, staff and unions in additional factories.
At the same time, Mr. Kata On, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that through these achievements, the work activities in the Department of Labor were well implemented in accordance with the duties and responsibilities. Defined by the Prakas of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, as well as efforts to increase capacity through practical work, participation in workshops and training courses.
Mr. Kata On added that at the same time, the Ministry of Labor has launched the action plan for 2024 to improve occupational safety and health for workers, and it is in line with the Royal Government's Pentagon-Phase 1 strategy and the strategic plan for employment development and Vocational training 2024-2028.
In addition, Mr. Kata On emphasized that these activities include: * First, the legal framework and policies on occupational safety and health are in line with international standards and effective implementation.
* Second, the establishment of the infrastructure of occupational safety and health management system, which operates at the national, sub-national and enterprise levels through cooperation and capacity development.
* Third: the implementation of compliance with the law and the inspection of occupational safety and health at work with qualifications and efficiency.
* Fourth: Increasing cooperation between employers and workers on occupational safety and health in the system sector, especially in high-risk areas, to improve the work environment and increase productivity.
* Fifth: Promoting a safe and healthy working environment in small and medium enterprises, the informal economy and in rural areas, as well as raising awareness of occupational safety and health.
* Sixth: Elimination of child labor and forced labor, cooperation in the prevention of HIV / AIDS, drug use, infectious diseases and non-communicable diseases in the workplace. Vice President of the Khmer Will Party in Chbar Morn City asks Samdech Techo Hun Sen to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party (Video inside)
