Preah Vihear Provincial Administration Holds Annual Reflection Workshop on Social Accountability 2023 and 2024
(Preah Vihear): The Preah Vihear Provincial Administration has organized an annual reflection workshop on the implementation of social accountability in 2023 and the direction for implementation in 2024.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Min Sitha, Deputy Provincial Governor, on behalf of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, with the participation of Deputy Governors, Municipalities, Departments, Relevant Units, Partner Organizations and Commune / Sangkat Chiefs on March 12, 2024. .
On that occasion, Mr. Min Sitha said that today's workshop was held in order to reflect on the implementation of social accountability in 2023 and set the direction for 2024 to ensure the sustainable efficiency of the implementation of social accountability through sharing. Good experience for other communes that have funded social accountability projects.
The Deputy Governor said that for Preah Vihear province, the implementation of social accountability has been implemented in three areas: commune administrative services, health centers and primary schools, which cover the target areas of 51 communes, 216 primary schools and 30 health centers. Implement services to 2 district administrations: Rovieng and Chep districts in 8 districts throughout Preah Vihear province.
It is also implemented in two parts: First: the supply side is the state body, which refers to the service providers in the sub-national administration, second: the demand side is the population group, which refers to the non-state actors And facilitated by civil society organizations as partners and advocates for implementation of the Partnership and Demand for Action, led by the Innovative Project for Social Accountability in Cambodia (ISAC).
In addition, Mr. Min Sitha expressed his hope that the workshop will get better results in line with expectations and get support from partner organizations to the provincial, municipal, district, commune and sangkat administration, especially Support for the need to participate in the implementation of social accountability for the following years, as well as to expand the scope to more target districts of Preah Vihear province.
The National Committee for Disaster Management of Cambodia and the Danish Church signed an MoU to continue the implementation of joint disaster risk reduction and emergency response activities in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDD) and the Danish Church in Cambodia have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to continue closer cooperation between the two sides in implementing activities on disaster risk reduction and Joint emergency response in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Dr. Hang Samoeun praised and appreciated the assistance of the Danish Church in Cambodia, which has worked closely with the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Noting that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, Dr. Hang Samoeun stated that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding between the two sides was carried out in the implementation of activities on disaster risk reduction and emergency response in Cambodia. The Memorandum of Understanding will enter into force for a further three years from the date of signing in March 2024.
On behalf of His Excellency Dr. Kun Kim, Dr. Hang Samoeun noted with satisfaction that the Danish Church Assistance Organization in Cambodia has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Royal Government of Cambodia from 2004 to 2024. Subsequently, the aid organization of the Danish Church in Cambodia, and in particular, also signed a memorandum of understanding with the National Committee for Disaster Management from 2012 to the present.
He further encouraged the Danish Church Aid Organization in Cambodia to strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation more actively and closely with the NEC, chaired by President Hun Manet and Honorary Doctor. Kun Kim is the first vice chairman, such as organizing national and international forums, seminars, training, gender suppression and other activities.
In this regard, the Deputy Prime Minister reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to promote and strengthen a close partnership with the EU in various priority areas in the future.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has organized a vegetable exhibition of Cambodian farmers at the Cambodia-International Digital Government and Digital Technology Exhibition of the 3-Day Digital Government Forum from March 11-13, 2024 at the Center. Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition H-L Building.
Ms. Hong Chanvibol, Deputy Director of the Office of Agricultural Product Quality and Safety of the General Department of Agriculture, who was present at the exhibition, said this morning, March 13, 2024, that the participation in the exhibition of Safe Vegetable Products (CamGAP) for two periods. Today, received a lot of attention from the exhibitors.
She stated that this exhibition is so that those who participate in the exhibition can try to scan the QR Code attached to the vegetables to know the information from those vegetable sources, so that they have confidence in buying safe vegetables to take. Eat.
Visitors also raised the question that if there is a case of forgery of vegetable products, for example, vegetables imported from abroad, but the CamGAP label with the same QR Code, what are the measures? To this question, Ms. Hong Chanvibol stated that the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture has measures to control the market, in case of farm owners, packaging facilities or producers misbehaving, they will be punished according to the law.
