(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, March 13, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the inauguration of the Techo Hospital. Sen Koh Thom ”is located in Koh Thom District, Kandal Province.
Techo Sen Koh Thom Hospital is a hospital that provides advanced medical services and is equipped with modern treatment facilities and equipment. Techo Sen Koh Thom Hospital was originally named Koh Thom District Hospital.
Koh Thom District Hospital started operating after the liberation on January 7, 1979, providing services such as consulting and general treatment, pediatrics, gynecology, gynecology, surgery, tuberculosis and so on. In 1997, the hospital changed its name from Koh Thom District Hospital to Koh Thom Referral Hospital.
Koh Thom Referral Hospital provides Level 2 (CPA2) complementary activities that include services such as outpatient counseling, pediatrics, STIs, AIDS, diabetes, hypertension, and hospitalization. Tuberculosis and treatment of infectious diseases. In fact, in 2021, when there was an outbreak of the 19 communicable disease, the hospital was actively involved in the treatment of 19 communicable diseases.
The new hospital responds to the specific needs of the Royal Government's political program and the vision for national development of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has taken into account the health and well-being of the people.
The construction of this hospital started on January 7, 2022 and was completed on June 20, 2023, with a total construction period of 18 months and 13 days.
The hospital covers an area of more than 14,000 square meters, divided into three buildings, with a total construction cost of more than 10 million US dollars.
The three hospital buildings play a role in providing different health services. The first building in the center is U-shaped and serves as a service point.
The second building serves as a two-story infectious disease service. Downstairs there is an ambulance parking lot, a workshop, a laundry room and a repair room for medical equipment.
The third building is the same size as the second building, which is used as a dormitory to provide accommodation for volunteer doctors who come to help the hospital and downstairs as a canteen.
In addition to these three large buildings to the hospital, there are five other small buildings, including an oxygen plant, a generator room, a control room, a water distribution network, a waste storage facility and an incinerator.
The hospital has a total of 179 beds, of which there are 2 beds for general illness, 163 beds and 5 beds for serious illness and 16 beds after surgery. The hospital is equipped with high-tech medical equipment in accordance with technical standards. The hospital is capable of providing outpatient, diagnostic and therapeutic services, including:
In order to prepare for the smooth operation of the hospital's health care services, the Ministry of Health and the Kandal Provincial Administration discussed and organized the hospital management, including one director and four vice presidents, who are officials from Victory Referral Hospital in Kandal Province. Koh Thom Referral Hospital and from Takeo Provincial Referral Hospital. There are a total of 95 civil servants, including 72 civil servants and 23 contract officers.
All 72 officers are technical staff: 2 specialists, 16 doctors, 2 pharmacists, 2 dentists, 6 laboratory technicians, 2 bachelor of nurses, 17 intermediate nurses, 6 primary care technicians and 6 physiotherapists. 1 bachelor, 1 midwife, 14 midwives, 2 primary midwives and 1 administrative accounting major.
Techo Sen Koh Thom Hospital will play an important role in providing public health services to more than 600,000 people living in Saang district, Koh Thom district, Leuk Dek district of Kandal province and Prey Kabas district of Takeo province.
