Kampong Tralach district has become an attractive potential area for foreign tourists. Almost every day, foreign tourists travel by boat and bus to ride ox carts through the countryside, and especially to visit the ancient paintings and temples of Wat Po Rukkaram, a national heritage site. It is more than 100 years old. This is according to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Tourism.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Sum Mab, Chairman of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, said that Wat Po Rukkaram or Wat Kampong Tralach Leu is one of the ancient pagodas that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has taken care of. Preserved and preserved for a long time until now.
