In a meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet on the afternoon of March 12, 2024, EU Commissioner for International Partnership Jutta Urpilainen highlighted the positive developments in EU-Cambodia relations.
During the meeting, Ms. Jutta Urpilainen thanked His Excellency Hun Manet for taking the time to allow her and the delegation to pay a courtesy call. She also congratulated the President on his election as Prime Minister in August 2023. She also congratulated Cambodia on its glorious success during its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022.
She also reaffirmed the close and lasting good relations and cooperation between the EU and Cambodia with fruitful past. She briefed the President on the progress noted in all areas of Cambodia, enabling Cambodia to move from a least developed country to a lower middle-income country by 2015 and become a middle-income country. High level in 2030.
She also informed the President that the European Union will continue to strengthen and expand cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in key areas such as trade and investment, industry, education and vocational training and health.
Meanwhile, during her current visit to Cambodia, the European Commissioner will witness the signing ceremony of a number of agreements, including: (1) the EU-Cambodia Partnership Program for Technical Education Training 2024-2027, ( 2) Trade and Private Sector Programs, (3) EU Partnership for Sustainable Energy Practices in Industry, and (4) Cambodia's Partnership Program for Sustainable Agriculture and Food Systems.
The President and the European Commissioner also discussed and exchanged views on regional cooperation and a number of regional and global issues of mutual interest between Cambodia and the European Union.
