Liu added that in particular, the "emerging music tourism" will inject economic stimulus, benefiting the travel-related sectors, including aviation, accommodation, retail and food and beverage. Arms imports to Europe almost double in 5 years
Stockholm: International arms imports to Europe have nearly doubled in the last five years, in part due to the war in Ukraine, while arms exports From Russia fell by half. According to the AFP news agency.
Ukraine has become the world's fourth-largest arms importer, while France has replaced Russia as the world's second-largest arms exporter after the United States.
According to the Stockholm International Peace Research Institute (SIPRI), arms imports to Europe increased by 94% in the period 2019-2023 compared to the previous five years. Global armaments have slowed down a bit.
China is usually one of the largest buyers of Russian weapons, but the country has been pushing for the development of its domestic production. China still accounts for 21 percent of Russia's exports, while India is the largest buyer of 34 percent of its weapons from Russia.
As Russia's exports fell, France saw a 47 percent increase in its arms exports, replacing Russia as the world's second-largest arms exporter. According to the AFP news agency.
Mr. Try Dalux was very pleased to be invited to celebrate the 113rd anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution". Mr. Try Dalux also sent greetings and greetings from Duke Dr. Try Pheap, Lok Chumteav Neak Oknha Kien Srey Neang to all participants in the program.
