Speaking of women's rights, Mr. Try Dalux highlighted the current capabilities of women who are strong in family, social and political affairs. Women are also considered by the Royal Government to play an important role in the family and society until the slogan "Women are the backbone of the economy."
Regarding the value of women, Mr. Try Dalux also pointed out that now in the ministries, public and private institutions are always present, especially the number of female civil servants is increasing.
Mr. Dalux also stressed that for Cambodia, the opportunity to promote the rights of women, men's rights as well as the rights of the people in general must necessarily demand peace and social stability. Without peace, the nation will face the flames of war, it will not be able to build and develop, the country will not be able to implement policies to promote women's rights as well as men's rights in general.
