Senior official of the Ministry of Economy: More than 6.6 million people benefit from the Cambodian social protection system as the Royal Government plans to expand
The people who benefit from the Cambodian social protection system are included in the framework of the social assistance system, which includes:
* Cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old with a total of 362,903 beneficiaries.
* Community-based school feeding programs have been implemented in 553 target schools in 10 provinces, with 148,787 beneficiaries and 1,748 chefs.
* Scholarship program for poor primary and secondary students, with a total benefit of 263,751 poor students.
Meanwhile, in response to past crises, including the crisis of Kovid-19 epidemic, the crisis of inflationary pressures and floods, the social protection system has become an effective tool for the government to Provide support to stabilize livelihoods, reduce negative impacts and restore people's livelihoods through the launch of special social assistance programs such as:
* Cash Support Program for Poor and Vulnerable Families During the Fight Against Kovid-19 has 704,280 beneficiaries or 2,771,809 members. Currently, the Royal Government has been implementing the exit strategy from this program (January-March 2024) before implementing the National Social Assistance Program in the family package from April 2024.
* Post-closure cash social assistance program: Introduced in 2021 to alleviate the living conditions of people in the area under the closure measures and who have been infected with Kovid-19 or died of Kovid. 19 with 129,666 families benefiting.
Cash program for vulnerable households during times of inflationary pressure: aims to help absorb the pressure of rising inflation (market prices) in times of crisis, covering a total of more than 500,000 target households. Or about 1.8 million people.
* Cash Social Assistance Program for Flood-Affected Families Affected by Floods: This program is implemented in 16 geographical areas of the target capital-province and has a target population of 99,169 families or equivalent. 372,859 for the three months from December 2022 to February 2023.
Within the framework of the social security system are:
* Social security system for pensions, health care and occupational risk for public officials, ex-civil servants and veterans: The Royal Government fully covers the payment of pensions to retirees. The regime has about 131,129 former civil servants and veterans.
* Social Security, pensions, health care and occupational risk for individuals subject to the provisions of the Labor Law: 1,494,576 mandatory contribution members and 4 active voluntary contribution members 338 people.
* Health Equity Fund for Equitable Citizens and Target Groups: The Royal Government provides free health care through Equity Health Fund to the poor, vulnerable families and other groups, including informal workers. , Cyclo riders, national team players, village-commune councilors, families of victims and individuals working in the informal economy tourism services.
Ms. Pen Sophea added that overall investment (expenditure) in the social protection system will increase from about 1% in 2018 to about 3% of GDP in 2022, with coverage increased from 26.5 % In 2018 to about 42% of the total population in 2022, which reflects the will and efforts of the Royal Government to build and strengthen the social protection system in Cambodia with a better environment.
This does not include other social assistance programs related to emergency response, such as the food supply system, vocational training and assistance programs for suspended workers, employment contracts, post-closure cash support, and support programs. Cash for households is difficult after the closure, which can account for about 5% of GDP.
