(Phnom Penh): During his stay in Phnom Penh to attend the Digital Government Forum on Tuesday morning, March 12, 2024, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, met with Mr. Keut Rith, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Justice.
The two sides discussed the importance of legal cooperation, combating transnational crime and strengthening the rule of law and criminal justice in ASEAN.
The ASEAN Secretary-General thanked Cambodia for its active participation and contribution to the work and efforts of the ASEAN Legal Ministers' Meeting and the Ministerial / Attorney General Meeting of the Central Authority on Legal Aid. On criminal issues in seeking legal cooperation and supporting the ASEAN Community, which is based on the rule of law.
On Tuesday morning, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also met with Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister and First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, to discuss untapped business, economic and investment opportunities in ASEAN.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General reaffirmed to the Deputy Prime Minister the unwavering support of the ASEAN Secretariat in promoting the ASEAN Economic Agenda, including promoting the attractiveness of ASEAN as a global investment destination.
On Tuesday afternoon, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also met with Dr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications to discuss the latest developments in the digital revolution and digital economy in ASEAN.
