Minister of Labor wants to see PSE students become role models for young people interested in professional skills
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Heng Sour, expressed his desire to see the students of PSE become a role model for young people interested in professional skills, so he urged the students of this institute to help Disseminate the Royal Government's plan to need 1.5 million skilled people by 2025.
Heng Sour said this at the graduation ceremony for 905 students of PSE Institute of the Organization for the Smile of Children for the 2018-2020 school year on March 12, 2024.
Among the 905 winning students (1 person with disabilities, 10 pregnant women and 464 women, including:
* 42 Bachelors of Business Administration * 137 Master's Degrees in Technology * 451 Bachelors of Technical and Vocational Training (451) * 57 Bachelor of Technical and Vocational Training * 5 Technical and Vocational Certificates * 5 * Professional Certificates 213 people continue to build bridges.
Mr. Heng Sour considered that the 905 winning students were given additional access to technical human resources to serve the development of the country as well as to solve development-related problems in their families.
Ms. De Palier Leakena, General Manager of the Organization for the Smile of Children, stated that the organization has the following vision:
* Children who are hungry need to be fed * Children who are sick need to be treated * Children who do not go to school need to be educated in both general knowledge and vocational training * Child victims need to be protected And maintenance.
Please be informed that since 1996, PSE has been helping children and youth from poor and uneducated families in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville through six major programs: Food Program Health programs, prevention and accommodation programs, general education programs, vocational and higher education training programs, and family support programs. All of these programs are in line with government policy.
