(Banteay Meanchey): On March 11, 2024, the local police force of Poipet City arrested a suspect named Chhun Sina, 36 years old, living in Phnom Chhnang village, Chob Vary commune, Preah Net Preah district, Banteay Meanchey province, in a case of breach of trust.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Poipet City Military Police Base, said that the plaintiff, who owns a business selling all kinds of construction materials in Poipet City, hired Chhun Sina to work for him as a marketing staff and walked. Distribute construction materials in 4 provinces.
Later, the plaintiff used his son to register all customers, only to find out that Chhun Sina had embezzled his company's money from 2015 until the beginning of 2024 for a total of $ 353,761.
Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro said that after receiving the complaint and obtaining permission from Brigadier General Born Bin, the Commander of the Provincial Armed Forces, the procedure was coordinated by Mr. Keut Vannareth, the Prosecutor of the Court of First Instance. In Banteay Meanchey province, he led a force to bring Chhun Sina to the municipal military police base for questioning.
Colonel Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime investigation and investigation, said that the suspect, Chhun Sina, along with his personal exhibits confiscated by the Provincial Gendarmerie were sent by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau. Provincial Court and on the morning of Tuesday, March 12, 2024 to proceed with the procedure.
The Senate unanimously approved two draft laws in the extraordinary session of the fourth legislature.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the opening of the Extraordinary Session of the 4th Legislature, the Senate reviewed and unanimously approved the entire draft law without amendment by 57 votes out of the total number of senators.
The Extraordinary Session of the 4th Legislature was chaired by Mr. Kittisangha Dr. Tep Ngon, Second Vice President of the Senate. The meeting will be attended by 57 senators on March 12, 2024.
The meeting proceeded with the following 2 agendas:
* Agenda 1: Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of the protocol for the amendment of the Marquez Agreement on the Establishment of the World Trade Organization to include the agreement on fisheries subsidies.
This draft law is designed to contribute to ensuring the sustainability of marine fisheries resources on a global scale by each region and member state by banning or stopping harmful subsidies related to marine fisheries, which are a major factor in the destruction. To the world's marine fisheries stocks.
Through this agreement, Cambodia will receive the following major benefits:
