Cambodian Red Cross Disseminates 161st Anniversary of World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day May 8, 2024 in Prey Veng Province
(Prey Veng): To celebrate the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, 8 May 2024, under the theme "Together with the Cambodian Red Cross for a Healthy and Climate Resilient Community" Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Chairman, appointed Mr. Yulana, Second Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross to lead the working group to disseminate the content of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024.
The event was attended by Mr. Sok Pheng, Permanent Vice President of the Branch, Mr. Chim Sok, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Prey Veng Branch, which was attended by the branch staff, sub-branches, volunteers, CRC youth, departments around the province and philanthropists. In the afternoon of March 11, 2024.
The Second Deputy Secretary General paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen and presented the following objectives: (1) Disseminate to the public the knowledge and understanding of what the Cambodian Red Cross is doing. (2) Demonstrate the achievements and progress of the Cambodian Red Cross; (3) Continue to call on philanthropists from all walks of life to raise funds for continued humanitarian operations, help vulnerable people and participate in solving challenges.
