In addition, Samdech Hun Manet said that for the construction site of the Techo International Airport, before the groundbreaking, there were war remnants, but under the roof of peace is now being turned into a large airport for tourists. For landing and a place where there is a lively life movement and so on.
According to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, according to the Royal Government's infrastructure investment plan for the Third Ring Road, National Road No. 1, National Road No. 2, it is planned to invest in a river-to-sea waterway project near the Techo Airport area, which has a land road. Waterways and airways close together.
As of February 21, 2024, the construction of the first phase of Techo International Airport 4F has reached about 66% and the total construction cost of 961 million US dollars of the total investment of 1.5 billion. US dollars.
