The National Council for Social Protection organized the "Cambodian Social Protection Week 2024" to discuss with stakeholders to further develop the Cambodian social protection system.
(Phnom Penh): The National Council for Social Protection organized a two-day program "Cambodian Social Protection Week 2024" from 12 to 13 March 2024 to discuss and exchange views with stakeholders to collect key inputs. To continue to develop a better Cambodian social protection system.
The program "Cambodian Social Protection Week 2024" was organized under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Chairman of the National Council for Social Protection and with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, employers' representatives, employees, development partners, Civil society organizations, students who participated in person and online.
Ms. Pen Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chair of the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection, stated that "Cambodia Social Protection Week 2024" is a forum for discussion and exchange of perspectives, policies, implementation and knowledge sharing. The experience is particularly relevant to the progress of the Cambodian social protection system and to other countries, both regionally and globally.
She added that the "Cambodian Social Protection Week 2024" is set to "continue to build a social protection system for sustainability and resilience" as a theme for discussions with national and regional speakers and will be held for two years. Full day.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that this is the third celebration of Cambodian Social Protection Week 2024 since the establishment of the National Social Protection Council in 2017. The organization of the last two Cambodian Social Protection Week has yielded proud results and key inputs that have been used in further consideration for the development of the Cambodian Social Protection System.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth added that the organization of the Social Protection Week is part of the strengthening of good governance principles in the social protection system, which creates opportunities for discussion and awareness of the results of the launch. Policies that can be an important input for further planning in order to better move forward.
