A 14-year-old girl named Den Sotheavy died at Samaki 1 Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Sen Chey. The other two seriously injured, 13-year-old Nhem Reaksa, resided in Veal village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey, broken left leg and broken eye. Second, 13-year-old Kim Dina, a resident of Samaki 1 Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasang, suffered a broken left leg and was the son of Samaki 1 Village Chief.
When they arrived at the scene, the car suddenly turned left and crossed the road into the Teng Lay Dry Port Company, causing the motorbike to not escape and crashed into the back of the truck, killing the girl who was the motorcyclist. Immediately on the spot, two other girls, who were passengers, broke their legs and the motorcycle was hit by the rear bumper of the car tuk tuk.
After the incident, the driver of the car escaped. After that, the Samrong Krom Police went to the scene and reported to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Traffic Office to measure and bring cars and motorcycles to be stored for later settlement.
