Discover the fasting month of Ramadan for the upcoming Muslims on March 12
Ramadan is the ninth month in the Islamic lunar calendar and is considered the lord of the other months. Because the lunar calendar year is 11 days shorter than the solar calendar, Ramadan revolves around each season. Example: Ramadan in 2022 corresponds to April, while Ramadan in 2023 corresponds to Thursday, March, and it will continue to decrease every year.
In addition, this fasting is fasting during the forbidden time from dawn to dusk. During the day, one should not eat, drink or have sex, while a woman's menstruation also impairs this fast. However, unintentional or forgetful eating is not considered a break or a break in fasting.
Some questions are asked, who is to fast? The answer is that Muslims (Muslims), in general, men or women (if a man becomes an adult from the time of intercourse, while a woman is menstruating) have the right mindset, not a man. Dementia. Must be a person with the right mindset, have a clear conscience and a willingness to perform the duties of fasting.
On the other hand, this endurance is not only a reduction in the fulfillment of bodily needs from eating and drinking more or less, but it is a commitment between the body and cleansing the spirit from material needs, patience. Have control over lust or hunger, and especially the practice of dharma discipline as an apostle who adheres to the right beliefs.
Not only the veneration of the night, the Muslims and men and women hurry to gather in the mosque, but the divisions do not see each other to perform the salutation (worship) "Taraveh" for a long time. Many Rocks (number of times of worship), in some churches, the average worship until almost dawn, some as little as 9 o'clock, depending on the ability without coercion, the old saying is to celebrate many festivals. A lot.
