Save the Children Organizes 7th Cambodia Hearing Day
(Phnom Penh): Save the Children organized the 7th Cambodia Hearing Day 2024 under the theme "Change your mindset: Let's ear care and hearing become a reality for all" to increase Understand and share hearing information to the public and health care providers.
The 7th Cambodia Hearing Day 2024 was organized with the participation of Prof. Dr. Sok Siphana, Co-Founder of Save the Children and Mr. Chhim Kim Hean and Ms. Kep Chansama, Founder and Deputy Executive Director of Cambodian Hope Organization. On March 10, 2024.
The World Health Organization (WHO) estimates that 80 percent of the world's population needs access to hearing care, which requires a trillion dollars.
Hearing problems are not just a physical problem, but can also cause psychological problems due to inability to receive information and communication barriers. Therefore, the purpose of this year's Hearing Day is to provide specific information to encourage the public as well as society and the Royal Government to focus on providing high quality ear care and hearing services.
In Cambodia itself, Hope Cambodia has been involved in providing hearing care to approximately 25,000 patients since 2020. In addition, Krousar Thmey, which participated in today's program, also helped about 650 children with hearing loss, including 200 at Phnom Penh Thmey Special Education School and children at other schools. Includes schools in Chbar Ampov, Siem Reap, Battambang and Kampong Cham.
However, the needs of hearing care in both educational and health institutions are still met by specific needs for prevention, care and treatment, which should be considered as basic and necessary.
Please note that the Day is always celebrated annually in the world, set for March 3, which can be organized by companies, organizations, associations or government institutions. Receive policy money from the Royal Government
