(Phnom Penh): Addressing the National Reading Day on March 11, 2024 under the theme: "Reading is the foundation for all in life" held at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister Education, Youth and Sports states that reading is also one of the most effective ways to improve academic achievement and understanding of the world.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron added that while technology is advancing every day, there are many reading aids for reading enthusiasts, including: reading books, reading on electronic devices, reading on smartphones and reading on computers. These are all important ways to lead readers to achieve their reading goals. On the other hand, reading using modern technology means less time, easier to read and also helps the environment.
Today, Cambodian students and young people who love to read are also using these means of reading, if you look at developed countries, despite the advanced technology, reading through books is still very strong. In this regard, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has already celebrated the National Reading Day eight times since 2016.
