Speaking on that occasion, Samdech President Hun Manet said that this forum will also have a discussion, so as an additional input to the discussion, Samdech would like to request the forum to focus on five key points. Below:
First, to respond to the rapid development of new digital technologies, especially artificial intelligence (Generative AI) technology, which in turn leads to innovation and increase productivity, and in other words, leads to an increase in the flow of private data, people and Cross-border use of that data raises concerns about commercial exploitation, privacy breaches and cyber security threats.
Third, harmonizing policies, regulations, standards between countries in the region to facilitate trade and digital services, as well as strengthening the sharing of knowledge and experience.
Fourth, identifying the key drivers of digital human capital building and methods to increase the capacity of people to capture and use digital technology.
Samdech Manipur Hun Manet hopes that the first Digital Government Forum can run smoothly and encourages active participation in discussions to achieve fruitful results.
