Key Remarks by Samdech Mani Hun Manet on the Opening Ceremony of the 1st Digital Government Forum
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, March 11, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the opening ceremony of the first digital government forum. The forum is organized by the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Mani Hun Manet on the occasion of the opening of the first Digital Government Forum:
* Samdech Hun Manet was pleased to preside over the opening ceremony of the "Digital Government Forum and the 1st Cambodia-International Digital Government and Digital Technology Exhibition", under the theme "Promoting Sustainability and Development Environment through Practice "Digital Policy" with the participation of ASEAN countries, regional countries, as well as ministries, institutions, the private sector, universities and development partners of Cambodia.
* His Excellency appreciates and highly appreciates the great achievements in the digital sector that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, relevant ministries and institutions and the ASEAN Secretariat have achieved in the past, both within Cambodia and ASEAN.
* President Hun Manet stated that in recent years, digitalization in Cambodia has progressed at a remarkable pace. The Kovid 19 crisis has spurred the use of digital technology more and more than ever before.
* President Hun Manet stated that, in fact, digital payments will reach about 492 billion US dollars by 2023, which is about 16 times the GDP.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the number of registered mobile internet users and mobile subscribers will increase to more than 19 million by 2023.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has been implementing the digital policy agenda with a proactive and open spirit in order to achieve the national digital development goals and regional and global digital development goals as set out in the ASEAN Digital Plan 2025 and the Digital Strategy. 2022-2025 of the United Nations.
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia has been joining ASEAN member countries in advancing the ASEAN Digital Economic Framework Agreement, which is expected to increase the size of the ASEAN digital economy from $ 1 trillion to $ 2 trillion annually. 2030.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet stated that as an additional input to the discussion, Samdech Thipadei requested the forum to pay attention to the following five key points:
First. Responding to the rapid evolution of new digital technologies, especially artificial intelligence (Generative AI) technology, which, in turn, leads to the promotion of innovation and increased productivity, and, in turn, leads to an increase in the flow of private data and the use of data. That crosses the border, which raises concerns about commercial exploitation, human privacy breaches and cyber security threats.
Third. Harmonization of policies, regulations, standards between countries in the region to facilitate trade and digital services, as well as strengthening the sharing of knowledge and experience.
Fourth. Identifying key drivers for building digital human capital and methods to accelerate the capacity of people to capture and use digital technology.
