Comment: China's development of quality new production capacity will provide new impetus to regional and global economic growth
BEIJING, March 5 (Xinhua) - China has set priorities for the 14th National People's Congress (NPC) at the Second National People's Congress (NPC) on March 5. Some important things for 2024, including efforts to modernize industrial systems and develop "quality new production force" at a faster pace.
In Xi Jinping's view, "quality new production force" refers to high productivity, shifting from traditional economic growth model to development model based on high technology, high efficiency and high quality. In order to develop a quality new production force, the Chinese government needs to continue to push for continuous innovation in science and technology, as well as promote the development of the modern technology industry.
As highlighted in the 2024 Government Work Report, China is committed to (1) improving supply chains and industries, (2) actively developing future and industry-focused industries, and (3) promoting Innovative development of the digital economy to ensure China's economic growth, improve people's living standards and achieve China's modernization in all fields.
China's commitment to developing quality new production capacity will have a positive impact on regional and global development by providing countries around the world with access to modern technology and exchanges. Technology includes 5G technology, artificial intelligence, high-tech industry and digital economy.
These benefits will significantly contribute to Cambodia's economic growth, create new job opportunities for its people and increase Cambodia's competitiveness. Overall, in the future, China has great potential and high competition to develop a quality new production force that will not only become a catalyst for China's economic growth, but also create a new impetus for growth. Regional and global economy as well.
The Senate Standing Committee will convene on March 11 to review three agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On March 11, 2024, the 4th Standing Committee of the Senate will meet under the chairmanship of Dr. Simka, Acting President of the Senate of Cambodia, with the following agenda:
