The King Appoints Her Royal Highness Princess Norodom Arunrasmey and Prince Sisowath Thomico as Senators for the 5th Term
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing His Royal Highness Princess Norodom Arunrasmey and Prince Sisowath Thomico as senators for the fifth term.
The Senate for the fifth term has 62 members, two of whom are nominated by the King, two are elected by the National Assembly by a majority vote, and 58 are elected by universal suffrage. Commune / Sangkat Councilors and National Assembly members in office.
According to the results of the election of senators for the fifth term, there are four political parties competing, in which the CPP won 55 seats and the Khmer Will Party won 3 seats. Separately, FUNCINPEC and the National Forces Party, which also contested, did not win seats.
