Cambodian, Thai authorities vow to strengthen solidarity, friendship and good cooperation along the border between Oddar Meanchey and Borei Rom provinces
(Oddar Meanchey): The authorities of Oddar Meanchey and Borei Rum provinces of Thailand have jointly committed to strengthen the friendship, solidarity and good cooperation along the border to serve the common interests of the people of the two countries.
The joint commitment of the provincial authorities of the two countries was made on the occasion of Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, allowing Mr. Charoen Venphet, Deputy Governor of Borei Ram Province and his accompanying delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss some matters at the meeting hall. Oddar Meanchey Provincial Hall on March 8, 2024.
During the meeting, the provincial authorities of the two countries pledged to strengthen the friendship, solidarity and good cooperation between the people and the people and between the provinces and provinces bordering each other, and to build solidarity between the people of Cambodia and Thailand. As well as a joint commitment to crack down on all types of cross-border crime effectively.
Mr. Pen Kosal requested the Thai side of Borei Rom province to help speed up the Saitaku border crossing to become an international border crossing like the Chob Koki border crossing in Cambodia. In response, the Thai side accepted Cambodia's request and confirmed that it was pushing and speeding up the procedure.
