Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Has Several Meetings in Laos Ahead of the 30th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting
(Lao): At the invitation of Mr. Malaithong Kommasith, Minister of Industry and Commerce of the Lao People's Democratic Republic and Chairman of the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting 2024, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, led a delegation of the ASEAN Secretariat to attend the meeting. The 30th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting was held in Luang Prabang, Lao People's Democratic Republic.
On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on the economic achievements that are expected to be achieved under the ASEAN Chairmanship of Laos in 2024, as well as the development of a strategic plan for the ASEAN Economic Community, which is an important part of ASEAN Community Vision 2045.
On that occasion, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn thanked the ASEAN BAC for its active role in establishing a dynamic partnership between the business community and the governments of ASEAN member countries, which is an important vehicle for achieving the ASEAN vision of integration. The regional economy is environmentally friendly and looking forward.
On the evening of March 8, 2024, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, met with Mr. Liew Chin Tong, Deputy Minister of Investment, Trade and Industry of Malaysia to discuss preparations for the ASEAN Chairmanship. Malaysia in 2025, as well as the establishment of the ASEAN Community Vision 2045 in progress.
On that occasion, the Secretary-General of ASEAN stressed that 2025 is an important year in the process of building the ASEAN Community and reaffirmed the readiness of the ASEAN Secretariat to support Malaysia to ensure its success. ASEAN chairmanship next year.
Pursat Governor Warns Against Taking Action Against Offenders for Destroying Natural Resources
(Pursat): Although the nine working groups of the Sub-Committee on Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes in Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh Districts have cracked down on and confiscated nearly 20,000 hectares of land that the perpetrators encroached on. However, encroachment on state-owned forest land continues in the old and new locations, especially during the dry season.
In fact, on March 08, 2024, Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Joint Working Group, inspected some hot spots in Veal Veng district and warned to take legal action. Serious to the perpetrators and those involved without exception.
Khoy Rida once said in an emergency meeting with the provincial commission and the nine sub-committees on the afternoon of March 5, 2024 that he would insult any official who conspired with the perpetrators. Destroy natural resources within its jurisdiction by requesting the head of the Royal Government to implement the fifth approach, which is direct surgery.
He also pointed out that Veal Veng district is a high-risk district and a hotspot for natural resource disasters through deforestation and forest burn, land ownership by the perpetrators and some pumpkin officials Are conspiring systematically.
As the provincial governor and chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, he will use his time off on holidays to go directly to all the targets to take action against the perpetrators and stakeholders without exception.
At the same time, he also requested the 9 sub-committees to continue to inspect the old locations that were confiscated and stored in the past, as well as to map and make specific reports to examine the new cases of logging by targeting research and arrest. The perpetrators come to be punished, no matter what the order. In addition, stand and prepare seedlings for replanting.
