This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Vuthy presiding over the meeting on building cooperation and exchange of views between Shandong Province and Cambodia on the development of "Industrial Corridor" and "Fish and Rice Corridor". In the afternoon of March 08, 2024.
In addition, the Secretary General of the Cambodian Investment Committee stated that in the first two months of 2024, Chinese investment flows were about 545 million US dollars, equivalent to about 39% of total investment.
According to Mr. Chea Vuthy, the total investment flow in Cambodia will increase by about 4.9 billion US dollars in 2023, an increase of about 22% compared to 2020. By 2023, China's total investment inflows will reach more than 3 billion US dollars, accounting for more than half (66%) of total investment inflows.
Mr. Chea Vuthy also pointed out that the flow of Chinese investment always ranks first, second or third every year, mostly concentrated in industry, infrastructure, and agro-industry.
He added that the volume of trade between Cambodia and China is also a positive sign, reaching more than 12 billion US dollars in 2023, an increase of nearly 5% compared to 2022. During the same period, exports from Cambodia to the Chinese market increased by about 19% from more than 1.2 to about 1.5 billion US dollars.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Vuthy expressed his pleasure and warm welcome to the presence of the government delegation and investors of Shandong Province in the study tour to explore the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia and highlighted the importance of cooperation. Investment and other cooperation between Cambodia and China.
He also highlighted that the two countries' cooperation framework has been upgraded to "diamond cooperation", which will enable further political, economic and security cooperation towards building a common destiny community in the era. New.
The Secretary-General encouraged Chinese investors to study, learn more and invest in Cambodia, as well as bring knowledge, skills and technology in industry, agriculture and agro-industry, especially agriculture, aquaculture, processing and industry. The sea is going to add value and modernize these sectors in Cambodia, as well as to meet the huge demand of the Chinese and international markets.
In addition, he also informed that the leaders of the Ministry of Commerce of the People's Republic of China will visit Cambodia in the near future to discuss the establishment of industrial parks to promote the processing of local raw materials and Semi-finished products for supply to car tire factory in Cambodia.
In addition, a potential company will set up a semi-finished processing and production center to supply the Cambodian rubber tire industry. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Chea Wutty.
He emphasized that the meeting was organized in collaboration with the Council for the Development of Cambodia with the Foreign Office of Shandong Province, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, and the Cambodian-Chinese Association in Cambodia in order to strengthen and expand awareness of investment opportunities in Cambodia. .
Acting President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce: Cambodia is a great destination for foreign investors looking to expand the market
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Lim Heng, Acting President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said on March 8, 2024 that Cambodia is a great destination for foreign investors who wish to explore a wide range of markets, favorable policies and potential growth.
This statement was made on the occasion of Duke Lim Heng attending a conference and business meeting between Cambodia and China (Shandong Province) on the construction of the Industrial Development Corridor and the Fish and Rice Corridor on the afternoon of the 8th. March 2024.
According to Duke Lim Heng, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce has been actively involved in promoting business relations between Cambodia and China and cooperating closely with the Chinese business community, having successfully organized more than 100 business and investment promotion events in the past. With Chinese partners, of which the China Overseas Trade Promotion Council is a major partner.
At the same time, Duke Lim Heng emphasized that the conference is also part of the joint efforts of the two countries' business communities to promote trade and investment, while China and Cambodia have a long-standing friendship and relationship.
The duke stated that the leaders of the two countries were committed to building a future Cambodian-Chinese community together in the new era and set out to establish a diamond cooperation framework that focuses on six priority areas, including cooperation. Politics, quality and production capacity, agriculture, energy, security and people-to-people exchanges.
In addition, Duke Lim Heng said that China is one of Cambodia's largest trade and investment partners. In recent years, the trade volume between Cambodia and China has steadily increased, exceeding the target set by the governments of the two countries.
As for direct investment, China has invested in key sectors such as garments, construction, mining, energy, agriculture and tourism. Cambodia regards China as a reliable friend and partner in joint economic development. This is an additional emphasis of Duke Lim Heng
Duke Lim Heng also invites Chinese businessmen and investors to explore Cambodia's boundless opportunities and experience first-hand the growth of a better business environment and a wider range of investments. Together, seize this unique opportunity and participate in the evolution of the Cambodian economy.
Duke Lim Heng pointed out that Cambodia is geographically located in the middle of Southeast Asia with a wide market and high purchasing power. Chinese investors can set up factories in Cambodia and export products with preferential tariffs to many countries under the framework of free, multilateral and bilateral free trade, including:
* Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement with 15 countries * Cambodia-China, Cambodia-Korea Bilateral Free Trade Agreement * and Cambodia-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement. At the same time, Cambodian products can also be exported to the United States, the European Union and the United Kingdom.
Duke Lim Heng said that Cambodia is a good destination for foreign investors who want to find a wide market, favorable policies and potential growth. Cambodia has shown resilience to the crisis, adapting to the global epidemic, Kovid-19 and global trade tensions.
In order to promote, protect, care for and encourage investors, the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the previous mandate under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Royal Government of the seventh mandate led by Samdech Thep Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia always pay attention and Lead the Government-Private Sector Forum to address the difficulties and challenges of the private sector, both domestic and foreign, that come to invest in Cambodia.
In addition, a new investment law came into force in 2021, which provides a clear and complete legal framework for investment in Cambodia. The law provides many incentives, guarantees and protections for local and foreign investors. This is the emphasis of Duke Lim Heng.
