Lieutenant Colonel Chim Rina, Police Inspector of Stong District, said that the house above was 4 x 5 meters in size and made of wood and caught fire at 9:52 pm on March 7, 2024 due to electric shock. And damage to property and entire homes.
Please be informed that the owner of the above house received some food and supplies as well as 400,000 Riels, and the district governor promised to help build a new house for the victims and pay for the treatment of injuries. Preah Vihear provincial authorities reveal the results of law enforcement operations against illegal state encroachment groups in Kulen district, nearly 40 people arrested
(Preah Vihear): Preah Vihear Provincial Authority on the morning of March 7, 2024 held a press conference on the implementation of legal measures to protect registered state land and delegate investment rights to Seila Damex Co., Ltd. Located in Sroyong and Phnom Tbeng Pei communes, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province, after a group of people entered and illegally encroached on the land.
The conference was held at the press conference hall of Preah Vihear Provincial Hall in the presence of Mr. Suon Sovann, Deputy Director of Forestry Administration, Mr. Nop Vuthy, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, Mr. Peng Trida, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ms. Hem Sokun Pisey, Director of the Provincial Information Department. Involvement of stakeholders and journalists.
He claimed that on March 6, 2024, the Joint Task Force led by Mr. Ty Sovinthal, Prosecutor of the Provincial Prosecutor's Office, led by Mr. Keo Omalis, the Royal Government of Cambodia delegate in charge of the Forestry Administration and Mr. Kim Rithy, the provincial governor, took legal action against these groups.
During the operation, 36 people were arrested and more than 30 others were still resisting and retaliating with police using knives, axes, rubber sticks and gas canisters. Use the right to self-defense to throw smoke bombs to disperse those anarchists.
Deputy Director of Forestry Administration Suon Sovann also confirmed that the legal action on March 6, 2024 is not new to these groups, he said this is the second time in the same location, but Those groups are still coming in to illegally invade.
He added that the Royal Government granted an economic land concession to Seila Damex Co., Ltd. in 2010 with an area of 9,000 hectares, but seeing that there are people enjoying the land, the Royal Government The land was cleared twice, the first time in 2012 through the old policy, new activities and the second time in 2019 before the land was registered as state land.
