General knowledge: Making the first riel
(Phnom Penh): The modern currency of modern Cambodia is the riel, which was published with the establishment of the National Bank of Cambodia since 1955, immediately after Cambodia claimed independence from France under God. The crusade of King Samdech Preah Boromneath Sihanouk "Preah Borom Ratanakoth", the father of the Khmer nation.
The riel was disbanded during the Democratic Kampuchea era of Pol Pot and cut off the economic system, completely destroying national achievements. It was not until 1979, the year of the liberation of the country and the people of Cambodia, from the genocidal regime that the National Bank of Cambodia was reopened, and in 1980 the riel was re-introduced.
