Analysis: China offers new opportunities to the world through its new developments
BEIJING, March 5 (Xinhua) - The Chinese government's 2024 work report submitted to the National People's Congress (NPC), China's top legislature for discussion, attracted the world's attention on March 5. The whole world. Many international investors have a better understanding of China's economic development goals and roadmap for 2024.
Currently, the momentum of global economic growth is insufficient and the global growth rate estimates of many international institutions are less than 3%. China has set its target for GDP growth this year at about 5 percent, which is in line with last year's target, which is in line with external estimates and has brought positive signals to the world.
Among them, "new quality production force" is a popular word. Many foreign media outlets have noted that this area with strong development potential will be a catalyst for economic growth, which means that China will pay more attention to the "innovative" development formula. .
From easing access to the services industry, such as telecommunications and healthcare, to expanding the incentives for foreign investors to invest, to ensure the implementation of the eight-point operation to support the joint construction of the "Belt and Road". The high-quality, multi-openness measures identified in this report have boosted the confidence of multinational enterprises.
China has been providing new opportunities to the world through its new development, which is a promise of China and certainly a practical implementation of China.
Cambodia-China Friendship Radio: National Assembly President Khuon Sodary: Addressing Gender Inequality Is Not Just for Women, but for a Just, Equitable and Prosperous Society
(Phnom Penh): At the Second Roundtable on Equality and Equality between Women and Men in Politics and the Role of Women on March 7, 2024, National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, stressed that Cambodia is strongly committed to strengthening gender equality and women's participation in politics.
The National Assembly President said that the Pentagon Strategy, the first phase of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, a five-year development plan (2023-2028) emphasized the importance of gender equality and the empowerment of women in key areas. These include economics, education, health, and public leadership.
The National Assembly stressed that the National Assembly is committed to promoting gender equality through its legislative, monitoring and evaluation work and representation. "We have clarified gender-oriented approaches and responding to gender needs in seeking support for policy and policy-making."
"When we can raise the level of gender equality, we can not only mobilize ideas to achieve women's rights, but we can help promote a just, equitable and prosperous society for all," he said. .
The summit has two main roundtables: the first is the theme of equal education, the fight against violence against women and women's health, and the second is the theme of equality and equality between women and men in the field. Politics and affirmations of women's role models.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary addressed the meeting, saying that women's leadership is not just a fairy tale, but a testament to women's resilience and ability. Women exemplify leadership that is characterized by empathy, caring, sharing, and meticulous leadership, both at home and in the profession.
The National Assembly President informed the meeting that they must recognize the nature that is deeply rooted in gender inequality. Women and girls are often exposed to violence, abuse, and inequality at home, at work, and in the community, and lack access to education, income, and leadership. Addressing gender inequality is a global issue that benefits everyone, not just women.
At the same time, the National Assembly President said that the meeting of women parliament speakers on this occasion is very important for women. Women's representatives who have discussed in detail the potential issues between: gender equality, equality and empowerment in politics highlight the important role of role models in society.
(Phnom Penh): In Paris, France, the Summit of Women Parliamentarians officially began on the evening of March 6, 2024, with the participation of 25 women parliamentarians from around the world. Ambassadors of the 25 countries represented in the French Republic, as well as accompanying delegates and partner organizations of the French Parliament.
She said the current meeting of women parliamentarians is to further promote pro-parliamentary diplomacy that takes into account issues of women and girls and promotes women's rights around the world. "In order to change the global context, we need to change our country's perception of gender," she said.
The President of the National Assembly of France called for joint efforts to consider positive measures that support women, give women full rights against all forms of discrimination and violence against women, as well as promote equality between women and men. By proposing and passing laws.
This is the first time that a summit of Speakers of the World Women's Assembly has been hosted by the French National Assembly. During the meeting, there will be two roundtables, the first of which will focus on equitable education, the fight against violence against women and women's health, she said. And the second roundtable on gender equality, equality between women and men in politics, and affirmation of women's role models.
The Delegation of the Presidents of the National Assembly attended the inauguration of an exhibition dedicated to the first political rights of women in the world and women in France, held at the National Assembly of the French Republic before the opening of the Roundtable. Opportunity is given to all women MPs to express their views on the protection of the interests and values of women around the world.
