Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth provided five points of view to contribute to the development of human capital, which is the core force for socio-economic development in the region as well as Cambodia as follows:
* First, continue to rethink and find ways to take appropriate measures to establish and strengthen the momentum of globalization through the establishment of open cooperation mechanisms and multilateral trade systems to promote the necessary global economic growth. In promoting the health and well-being of our people.
* Second, work together to create a conducive environment in our region to facilitate the development of human capital, to promote sustainable economic development, resilience and sustainability, and to address the gender gap in STEAM education and technology. Digital.
* Third, develop social resilience through strengthening the quality of education and skills development to meet the needs of industry and the development of public health systems and social protection in response to emergencies and humanitarian disasters.
* Fourth, to promote digitalization in the economy and society by building digital citizens, increase digital knowledge and capabilities, and minimize the digital divide, and
Fifth, encourage the participation of all stakeholders, especially the private sector and development partners, to mobilize financial and non-financial resources to strengthen human capital development.
He added that people are:
* (1): The ultimate and most important goal means that the Royal Government will do everything to ensure that the people live with dignity, peace, prosperity and harmony and * (2): the most important capital of the society This means that people must acquire the quality of knowledge, skills, good health and morality to enhance their potential and maximize their contribution to the building of society.
He added that, in fact, three pentagons in the first phase of the pentagon strategy, as well as four of the six priority policy programs set by the Royal Government, have direct consequences for the largest population. This confirms the priority and high attention of His Majesty the Prime Minister Hun Manet to the well-being of the people.
Finally, Mr. Vongsey Visoth expressed his deep gratitude to UNDP for organizing this workshop and preparing a timely human development report.
