This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet presided over the celebration of the 26th "National Cultural Day March 3" 2024 on the afternoon of March 7, 2018. 2024.
Hun Manet stated that the need for youth participation in the field of arts and culture for the socio-economic and the prevention of the spread of other cultures can affect the originality of our culture.
Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet said that the word "respect for the national culture" is an easy word to say, but in order to have true respect and love, we must first have a knowledge or a good understanding of the national art, culture and participation in all forms. Protecting and promoting our national culture.
"In this sense, training, mainstreaming, increasing opportunities for participation, making it more attractive to the general public, especially young people, strengthening respect for the culture, both tangible and intangible," said President Hun Manet. Of the nation.
At this point, Samdech President Hun Manet emphasized that all Cambodians have respect and love, but the lack of understanding can easily lead to activities that negatively affect the national arts and culture unknowingly. Therefore, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, as well as the artists, must continue their joint efforts to create literary texts as well as short films that are educational and engaging to young people.
Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet added that the creation of more cultural arts events such as: Angkor Remembrance Event, Angkor Writing, Remembrance Night, Khmer Folding Skirt Party, Traditional Music Concert and other events at historical sites. The original is a form of mainstreaming and creating love for the national culture.
This encouragement was made during the celebration of the 26th National Cultural Day, March 3, on the night of March 7, 2024.
"I would like to encourage the next generation of young professionals to have a greater opportunity to participate in training, research, compilation and dissemination of national culture, especially on art and traditional clothing," he said.
"Currently, the public, especially young people, are very popular and very proud to use traditional clothes, but the understanding of the form and mode of use is still ambiguous, confusing and misuse," he said.
With the many achievements in the field of culture in the past, in order to continue to promote the betterment of the cultural sector, Prince Hun Manet further recommended the following:
First, the production and innovation of art products is still limited with high prices, which makes the product uncompetitive, so the President requested the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to study the necessary incentives to boost production. And creating attractive and competitive art products.
Second, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and relevant institutions must strengthen the work related to intellectual property, copyright and related rights, prevent plagiarism, amend the legal framework in accordance with the actual situation of technology and international cooperation.
On the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 26th "National Cultural Day on March 3" on the evening of March 7, 2024, together with Her Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, President Hun Manet affirmed that the words "respect "Love of national culture" is an easy word to say, but to have true respect requires clear understanding.
"The word 'respect for national culture' is an easy word to say, but in order to have true respect, we must first have the knowledge and understanding of the arts, culture and participation," he said. All forms to protect and promote our national culture.
In this regard, the Prime Minister of Cambodia emphasized that outreach and awareness-raising increase opportunities for participation, creating greater appeal to the general public, especially youth, and strengthening respect for both tangible and intangible cultures. Of the nation.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia added that the arts and culture sector is one of the priorities of the Royal Government, which refers to the protection of national identity and people. He said the need for youth participation in the arts and culture for the socio-economic and prevention of the spread of other cultures could affect the originality of our culture.
Samdech Hun Sen emphasized that all Cambodians have respect and love, but the lack of understanding can easily lead to activities that negatively affect the arts and culture unknowingly. Therefore, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, as well as the artists, must continue their joint efforts to create texts as well as short films that are educational and engaging to young people.
This recommendation was made on the occasion of Samdech Ao during the celebration of the 26th "National Cultural Day March 3" 2024 on the afternoon of March 7, 2024.
Samdech stated that Samdech would like to provide the following additional recommendations to promote the cultural sector:
First, the production and design of art products is limited with high prices, which makes our products uncompetitive. Samdech requested the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to study the necessary incentives to promote the production and innovation of art products to be attractive and highly competitive.
Second, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and relevant institutions must strengthen the work related to intellectual property, copyright and related rights, prevent plagiarism, amend the relevant legal framework in line with the actual situation of technology and international cooperation.
Fifth, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Tourism to promote the national cultural tourism potential more widely in all forms for national and international tourism, focusing on national cultural values, contributing to national economic growth and poverty reduction.
Sixth, Samdech would like to support the cooperation of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and the Ministry of Information, which has made the Cambodian film industry has been growing remarkably by setting a golden time for the broadcast of Khmer films. At the same time, local authorities at all levels must cooperate to facilitate the provision of locations in their territories to facilitate the process of filming and film production.
Seventh, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, inspire all Cambodian embassies and consulates abroad to organize regular Cambodian cultural events every year to promote national culture and strengthen cultural policies. Diplomacy and to inspire the Cambodian community abroad to participate in organizing the National Cultural Day in a solemn and comprehensive manner.
BEIJING: Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi said on Thursday that China and Russia have set a new standard for relations between superpowers that are completely different from the outdated Cold War model. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on March 7, 2024.
Wang told a news conference on the sidelines of the ongoing National Assembly on Thursday that China and Russia are committed to long-term good-neighborly friendship and deepening reconciliation. Comprehensive strategy based on non-alignment, non-confrontation and non-focus on any third party.
He said that Russian natural gas provides electricity to countless Chinese households, and Chinese-made cars drive on Russian roads, which fully demonstrates the resilience and broad expectations of the cooperation provided. Mutual interests between China and Russia.
At the same time, Wang Yi stressed that maintaining and developing Sino-Russian relations is a strategic choice made by both sides based on the fundamental interests of both peoples, and it is also an inevitable choice. It is in line with current world trends.
He stressed that China-Russia relations are in line with the trend of global polarization and democratization of international relations, and are highly valued for maintaining global strategic stability, promoting healthy relations between major powers and strengthening cooperation. Cooperate with emerging powers.
The Chinese foreign minister's remarks come as this year marks the 75th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between China and Russia. Celebrate "National Cultural Day March 3"
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, March 7, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and His Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet presided over the ceremony on March 7, 2024. Celebration of the 26th "National Cultural Day March 3" 2024.
Samdech Techo Hun Manet would like to bring the greetings and greetings from Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council to Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, Teachers. Teachers, brothers and sisters, artists who have been every year, despite the busy schedule, Samdech Techo did not stop to attend the important ceremony of this National Cultural Day.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet said that in fact, arts, culture, traditions, customs, beliefs and religions reflect the beautiful nature of the nation, which is very important to organize the celebration of National Cultural Day every year.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet said that the arts and culture is one of the priorities of the Royal Government, which refers to the protection of national identity and people.
* President Hun Manet said that the need for youth participation in the field of arts and culture for the socio-economic and prevent the spread of the power of other cultures that can affect the originality of our culture.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must increase direct cooperation with the arts, encourage and provide technical assistance to young people who are focusing on researching and creating new works of art, spectacle, music, film, video and works. Other cultures must maintain an identity, ethics, professionalism and be competitive.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the youth should focus on strengthening the quality, luxury, brand, products, avoid plagiarism of all art products, both ancient and innovative products to promote production and strengthen the recognition of trust and Marketing.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet encourages the increase of the next generation of young professionals to have greater opportunities to participate in training, research, compilation and dissemination of national culture, especially on works of art and traditional clothing. Nowadays, people, especially young people, are very popular and proud to use traditional clothes, but the understanding of the form and mode of use is still ambiguous, confusing and misuse.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the production and processing of art products is still limited with high prices, which makes our products not competitive. Request the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to study the necessary incentives to promote the production and processing of art products to be more attractive and competitive.
* The President further stated that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and relevant institutions must strengthen the work related to intellectual property, copyright and related rights to prevent plagiarism, amendments to the relevant legal framework in line with the actual situation of technology and international cooperation.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, relevant ministries and institutions and local authorities at all levels must continue to take care to prevent and crack down on all crimes in a timely manner and effectively at the site of the temple. History of pagodas, historical buildings and structures that are hundreds of years old at the local level throughout the country.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, inspire all Cambodian embassies and consulates abroad to organize regular Khmer cultural events every year to promote national culture with Strengthening politics, culture, diplomacy and inspiring the Cambodian community abroad to participate in organizing the National Cultural Day in a solemn and comprehensive manner.
