According to the traffic accident measurement chart and the report of the road traffic police officer of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, the cause of the accident was due to the driver of a black HONDA C125 motorcycle who did not obey the stop sign.
After questioning and verifying the evidence in the case file, the prosecution decided to charge Art Chhay Ly with driving under the influence of Article 85 of the Road Traffic Law and sent the case file. To the investigating judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with the procedure.
China confident of economic recovery this year despite some setbacks
BEIJING (Reuters) - China's top economic policymaker on Wednesday expressed confidence that the superpower could achieve a strong recovery this year despite continued setbacks. According to the AFP news agency.
Thousands of delegates are gathering this week in Beijing for the "two sessions," the annual meeting of the Chinese National People's Congress and political advisory body, to discuss a formal strategy for next year.
"The trend of economic recovery will be further strengthened," Zheng told a rare news conference attended by five powerful officials from China's economic watchdog. .
This year's meeting for two summits is being closely watched to see more signs of state support to help the world's second-largest economy, which is currently struggling with a number of issues, including the crisis. Prolonged real estate market, weak exports and high youth unemployment.
China's exports, a key driver of historic economic growth, fell last year, the first decline since 2016, reflecting rising tensions with the United States and recovery. The recovery of the stagnant world economy as Beijing struggles to restart its economy.
According to the AFP news agency, Wang said on Wednesday that despite the recovery of Chinese exports in the first two months of this year, March is likely to see a decline. . He added: "But the whole trend is increasing." Hun Sen issued a sub-decree on the organization and functioning of the Digital Security Committee.
