(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, March 7, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and His Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet will preside over the ceremony on March 7, 2024. Celebration of the 26th "National Cultural Day March 3" 2024.
In the circular on the organization of the 26th National Cultural Day on March 3, 2024, Samdech Hun Sen highlighted that the National Cultural Day is an important day of the Cambodian people to commemorate the merits of all generations of Cambodian ancestors who sacrificed their physical strength. The strength, intellect and life to create, preserve and protect the rich and invaluable cultural heritage is passed on to the next generation.
Samdech Hun Sen also highlighted that the organization of the 26th National Cultural Day, March 3, 2024, by maintaining the theme "Youth for National Culture" was held in order to encourage the Cambodian people, both inside and outside the country, especially young people. To participate more actively in national cultural activities such as:
Promote the spirit of national pride, patriotic conscience, ownership of cultural heritage and citizenship in a highly civilized society with morality, equity and environment by inspiring all Cambodians to participate as a driving force in conservation, promotion and Develop the national culture, including the multiculturalism of Cambodia's indigenous communities, in a sustainable and prosperous manner, regardless of political affiliation, religion, color and ethnicity.
* Raise awareness of the enormous value of the rich national cultural heritage as an inexhaustible source for sustainable socio-economic development through the development of new cultural services and products for trade and tourism purposes that contribute to Creating more jobs that increase income and contribute to reducing poverty of our people
* Encourage entrepreneurial spirit and the creation of arts and culture among Cambodian youth to support the development of cultural and creative industries, which are potential sources of key and new economic growth, especially by providing opportunities for young people from Poor families and for the purpose of vulnerable families to receive vocational training, ancestors ensure the transfer of traditional knowledge and skills to the younger generation
Promote creativity and innovation in the development of cultural arts using digital technology as well as new initiatives to increase the attractiveness and ease of participation in cultural activities for the general public, especially children, youth, women, the elderly and People with disabilities under the slogan "Cultural art for all of us"
* Promote cultural cooperation in the spirit of building bridges connecting society from one society to another, from one nation to another and from one country to another in order to promote mutual understanding and respect that brings Unity, friendship, harmony and peace.
Samdech Hun Sen has introduced a number of activities to the ministries and institutions of the state, both nationally and sub-nationally, to organize the 26th National Cultural Day on March 3, 2024 more widely. The instructions are as follows:
1: The time for celebrating the 26th National Cultural Day is set from March 3 until the traditional Khmer New Year. In this regard, ministries, institutions, units and sub-national administrations must organize programs and support activities to celebrate the 26th National Cultural Day, both in person and / or on social media at any convenient time within a specified period. This.
3. The Ministry of Information must introduce all types of public and private media to participate in widely disseminating the content of activities related to the celebration of National Cultural Day.
4. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must cooperate in disseminating the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day to students, as well as inspiring activities to show and practice national traditions, customs and culture in public and private educational institutions.
5. The Ministry of Tourism shall promote the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day to national and international tourists through travel agencies, tour operators, tourist resorts, hotels, guesthouses and restaurants of all kinds, especially in accordance with the program "Visit Siem Reap 2024".
6. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation shall instruct all embassies, consulates, honorary consulates of the Kingdom of Cambodia abroad and the Cambodian community abroad to participate in organizing programs and activities to celebrate National Cultural Day at Live on social media and / or by other means.
7. The Ministry of Cults and Religions must inspire the movement of monks and all believers to organize programs and activities to promote the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day in temples, religious centers, Vipassana centers and other shrines.
8. The Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of National Defense must advise the local units to maintain security and public order on the occasion of celebrating the 26th National Cultural Day effectively and with a high sense of responsibility.
9. Capital and provincial administrations must support the Department of Culture and Fine Arts to be able to organize cultural promotion programs and activities in their territories, focusing on educating the masses, especially the youth, to have a stronger spirit of participation. Preserve, protect, promote and develop the national culture, as well as prepare banners, slogans in public places and post cultural posters at important locations within its administrative capitals and provinces.
10: All Ministries, Institutions, Sub-National Administrative Units, Schools, Factories, Enterprises, Homes and Cambodian Communities Abroad Celebrate and Celebrate National Cultural Day by Various means such as raising flags, flags, banners, slogans, paintings, arts, culture and / or activities. Appropriate at its location as well as on social media.
11. Participants in programs and promotional activities related to the National Cultural Day must dress appropriately in the national tradition.
