Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandith led the delegation back to Cambodia, bringing many beneficial results for the nation and the people
(Phnom Penh): At 11:30 pm on March 6, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and His Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a high-level delegation to return to Cambodia. Safe after about 10 hours on the plane from Melbourne, Australia.
The spirit and desire to bring achievements for the nation and the people urged Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to do his best not to save energy, regardless of time, day or night. Efforts are evident through the President's daily work program, whether in or out of the country.
In fact, during the current visit to Australia, the official program is a special summit between ASEAN and Australia to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the Dialogue Partnership, which lasted only two days. However, not wanting to miss out on the long journey and to seize the opportunity to expand political and economic diplomacy, Samdech Thepdey organized up to six days with a lot of programs with no free time left.
In that, even when traveling both to and from Samdech Hun Sen chose to travel at night, that is, choose the time to fly to Australia in the light and can work at once. On the other hand, the return flight is the same, the work schedule is set until nightfall in Australia, then the flight to Cambodia.
Through the work program as well as the travel time, this is the strong will of the Prime Minister of Cambodia in leading the nation.
In the current program in Australia, in addition to participating in the official program of the ASEAN-Australia Special Summit, the President met with the leaders of friendly countries and the presidents of major Australian companies, a total of more than 20 programs.
Separately, the management of large private companies that Samdech President Hun Manet allowed to meet and discuss the work, including:
Linfox is a leading logistics company in the Asia-Pacific region and has companies in 12 countries with more than 24,000 employees in Australia, New Zealand and Southeast Asia.
The company also has operations and markets around the world, especially in the supply of nutritional products to nearly 50 countries. SunRice Group is interested in Cambodian jasmine rice products, which are already well-known in the international market.
The company also has business operations, development, management and operation of ports and management services, maintenance and transportation of goods. ICTSI has also been expanding its investment opportunities in Cambodia in the port sector.
Finding investment and opening up markets for Cambodian products is an important task in the mission of leading the country of His Majesty Hun Manet. During his overseas missions, the Prime Minister of Cambodia did not miss the Business Forum, a forum to promote investment potential and doing business in Cambodia.
In addition to meeting with the presidents of major Australian companies, the Prime Minister presided over the opening of the Cambodia-Australia Business Forum, which aims to promote business between Cambodia and Australia. Especially attracting Australian investors to invest in Cambodia.
The Cambodia-Australia Business Forum is organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Victorian Chamber of Commerce and Industry with the participation of 350 investors and 350 companies.
In this forum, Samdech Thipdey reminded about the relationship between Cambodia and Australia, which has been around for about 7 decades. He recalled Australia's role in the peace process in Cambodia and its contribution to Cambodia's development since the Paris Peace Agreement on key areas, including infrastructure, education and agriculture.
He also highlighted the potential and opportunities for investment in Cambodia, which led to investors being able to get the best out of their investments through the Royal Government's policy of encouraging and protecting investors, geographical factors and agreements. Trade between Cambodia and other countries, which makes the product market larger.
The Prime Minister called on Australian investors to come to Cambodia to learn about investment opportunities. The President welcomed the Australian investors with pleasure.
In this business forum, there is also a signing ceremony of a memorandum of understanding on documents such as:
Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Victorian Chamber of Commerce and Industry to promote trade, investment and economic cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and Australia.
In this meeting, Samdech President Hun Manet highlighted the policy of the new Royal Government, which is a policy that gives high consideration to the well-being and livelihood of the people.
The people who participated in this talk show expressed their great satisfaction with the will, conscience, patriotism and consideration of the people as a whole of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet.
