Pakistan: At least 36 killed in torrential rain and snow
ISLAMABAD: The Pakistan Disaster Management Authority (NDMA) reported on Tuesday that at least 36 people were killed and 41 others injured in an unexpected downpour of rain and snow. Attacks remote areas of the South Asian country from February 27 to March 3. This is according to a release by the Xinhua news agency.
In addition, a total of 469 houses were completely or partially destroyed, and about 61 animals died due to heavy rains.
