(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Cashew Association has appealed to farmers who are collecting cashew nuts to dry the seeds and wait for the sale when the price improves in July or September, as the price of cashew nuts at the beginning of this season has dropped sharply. Yields this year have declined.
He added that the cashew nuts he collected were sold to traders at a price of more than 4,000 riel per kilogram, down from last year. One kilogram.
He said the drop in yields and prices would hurt farmers as they had to pay for fertilizers, pesticides and maintenance.
However, the cashew export data of the Cambodian Cashew Association confirms that in January 2024, Cambodia exported raw cashew nuts to Vietnam, an increase of 50% compared to the same period in 2023.
Uon Silot confirmed that the increase in cashew exports to Vietnam is not a cashew harvest in 2024. The increase in exports is the remaining by the end of December 2023.
In order to keep the price of cashews stable, the Cambodian Cashew Association has persuaded its members and other farmers to reduce and maintain 500,000 hectares of plantations to supply only local processing. Currently, Cambodia has seven medium-sized cashew processing plants with production capacity. Processing between 7,000 tons and 15,000 tons of raw seeds. However, Cambodia may need 30 more factories.
Cambodia currently has 35 small family-run handicrafts that should be promoted to become medium-sized factories.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior, has issued a new guideline on the management and use of National Police vehicles.
The Ministry of Interior has issued a series of legal documents, especially Prakas No. 3559, dated November 7, 2013 on the registration, issuance of license plates and license plates of vehicles managed by the Ministry of Interior in order to strengthen management efficiency. Use of all types of vehicles registered with the Ministry of Interior.
But recently, a small number of individuals have misused the designation of all types of National Police vehicles or taken them to inappropriate locations, which has damaged the prestige of the National Police Force and the honor of the Ministry of Interior.
In order to eliminate all these wrongdoings, the Ministry of Interior would like to advise the National Police General Commission, the General Secretariat, General Departments and Units under the Ministry of Interior as well as the Capital-Provincial Commissioners as follows:
1. Must be disseminated and implemented effectively in accordance with Prakas No. 3559 Prak dated November 7, 2013 of the Ministry of Interior on the registration, issuance of vehicle identification cards and license plates managed by the Ministry of Interior and other documents related to management And use National Police vehicles.
2. Must regularly manage and update vehicles with National Police license plates in the unit. In case of stoppage of any vehicle, report and hand over the license plate and ID card to the General Commission of National Police (Traffic Police and Public Order Department) for immediate removal from the list.
3. Prohibit the use of the National Police vehicle as follows: * Take the license plate from a properly registered vehicle to equip another vehicle * Use the vehicle with the National Police license plate to carry out other business is not private Yes, for the benefit of the Ministry or the state
* Take the National Police vehicle for another person to use
* Bring a vehicle with a National Police license plate into a casino, entertainment club, karaoke location or other inappropriate destination * Take a vehicle with a National Police license plate to commit other crimes * Use a National Police vehicle that has expired in Vehicle identification card.
4. The General Commission of the National Police shall regularly inspect the streets of casinos, entertainment clubs, karaoke venues or other inappropriate destinations and take strict action against any misuse of the National Police vehicle, as well as compile quarterly reports and reports in If necessary, to the leadership of the Ministry of Interior to request the principles.
