(Takeo): Mr. Khim Finang, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed that the farmers in Kirivong District, Takeo Province, who volunteered to participate in the demonstration (Demo) using only pure seeds. 60 kg per hectare yields up to 7.5 tons per hectare.
This announcement was made during the Smart Rice Day in Adaptation to Climate Change in Tuol Svay Village, Ang Prasat Commune, Kirivong District, Takeo Province, organized by the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Takeo Province on March 6, 2024 under the presidency of Mr. Toch Bun Hour, Secretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
The day was also attended by Mr. Undersecretary of State, Director of General Department of Agriculture, Deputy Governor, Director of Takeo Provincial Department of Agriculture, Local Authority, Chi Binh Dien Company, Kbal Krabei Company, Yitak Group, Kbal Krabei Fertilizer Distributor and 80 farmers. .
Mr. Khim Finang said that "Smart Rice Day" to celebrate the yield of 7.5 tons per hectare of farmers in Kirivong district, Takeo province, who volunteered to participate in a demonstration program (Demo) on a number of areas. 5 hectares with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
He stated that this model rice field (dry rice) was selected to show to the parents and relatives of farmers in Kiri district to see and understand the correct cultivation techniques, using only 60 kg of pure seeds per hectare, as well as Reducing fertilizer use and production costs.
He added that the use of the right technology and cost savings is the foundation and one of the benefits of modern farming communities, which the Ministry hopes that the farmers here will consider forming a community in the future.
As a result, the yield increased to 7.5 tons per hectare, and if combined with the decline in expenditure, the profitability of this model rice increased by about 1.5 million riels per hectare compared to Normal farming according to farmers' practices (300 kg per hectare, 6 tons per hectare and high fertilizer application).
Representatives of the participating companies also expressed their deep gratitude to the government, ministries, institutions, Mr. and Mrs. and the farmers who have worked hard to help in all ways and support close cooperation to help develop the agricultural sector, especially NPK fertilizer. Buffalo sign to contribute to poverty reduction and sustainable development.
