(Phnom Penh): All expenses for the treatment of injuries are borne by the Thai employer in the case of 20 Cambodian workers and 5 children in a traffic accident in Thailand. This is according to the press release of the Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on March 6, 2024.
According to the same press release, the Cambodian Consulate General in Sa Kaeo province received information from the Thai authorities in Nadi district, Prachinburi province that on March 3, 2024, 20 Cambodian workers and 5 children met. Accident while traveling from the accommodation in Klang Mafai village to work in Nadi district, Prachinburi province, Thailand.
The accident injured two Cambodian workers and seriously injured 23 others. After the incident, two Cambodian workers who were seriously injured were taken by ambulance to Kabin Borey District Hospital, Prachinburi Province. Those who suffered minor injuries after receiving first aid were taken back to their homes by their Thai employers.
The Cambodian Consulate General in Sa Kaeo province also confirmed that all expenses for the treatment of injuries were borne by the Thai employer.
