Minister Peng Poena sets out 10 principles to ensure the effectiveness and sustainability of the subordinate official social media
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, March 6, 2024, presided over the opening ceremony of a training course on public relations and transport mechanisms in the presence of Mrs. Chea. Leaders, ladies and gentlemen, heads of units under the Ministry and a total of more than 200 participants.
In 2023, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport posted on its official social media site 177 video content and 1,467 captioned content, or an average of 4 content per day. .
On that occasion, in order for the outreach mechanism in the field of public works and transportation to be implemented smoothly, efficiently and sustainably, Minister Peng Poena set out 10 principles and requested all relevant units Practices include:
2: To ensure that the sharing, dissemination and response of people's opinions on official social media is carried out regularly with a proactive and responsible spirit.
3: Schedule weekly publications in the field of public works and transportation, as well as national and international festivals, greetings, greetings for the year 2024.
4. Prepare the dissemination report for 2023 and the action plan for 2024 and the list of focal points in charge of public relations of the unit to the Ministry no later than March 26, 2024.
5. Encourage the leaders, civil servants and employees of the units under the Ministry to monitor and share the information published on the official media of the Ministry and its units widely.
6: Collaborate with the General Department of Technology and Public Relations to compile the content, disseminate and respond to the public by regularly copying all reports on the progress of public services and project progress, as well as legal documents and send in all forms. Provides up-to-date information and important events such as disasters, road damage, bridges, traffic jams, etc. Provides information and reports as needed.
7. Respond immediately and respond quickly to questions, comments or false information in collaboration with the spokesperson of the Ministry of General Department of Technology and Public Relations and the Quick Reaction Team to respond to journalists and citizens as needed.
8. All units under the supervision of the Quick Reaction Team and the General Department of Technology and Public Relations shall cooperate to respond to the opinions of the people or related activities under their jurisdiction.
9. Propose training to the General Department of Technology and Public Relations as necessary to strengthen the quality of information that is accurate, accurate and fast to increase the attractiveness that can absorb the popularity and trust of the public.
10. All units under the Ministry must pay attention in this training and must follow the mechanism as in the instructions.
