(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sin Chansery Vutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson for Civil Aviation, on March 6, 2024, confirmed that FOCUS Consortium is a multinational company licensed by the Royal Government of Cambodia. To study the investment project of the airport and satellite city in Mondulkiri province, currently working with the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, the detailed study process, both the development project and the amount of capital to be invested.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Sin Chanseryvutha confirmed that "the Secretariat of Civil Aviation has been cooperating with the Fukus Group to develop projects in accordance with the laws and procedures in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia."
He said the company will receive the right to study and invest in the new Mondulkiri Airport project in the form of Construction-Business and Transfer (BOT) and the development of a multi-purpose satellite city and air cargo center in Mondulkiri.
According to Mr. Sin Chanseryvutha, Fukers Group, led by Fukestra Global Ventures Ltd., is a multinational corporation with investment from Malaysia, China and the United Arab Emirates.
He said that reaching out to invest in the new Mondulkiri airport project and the development of a multi-purpose satellite city in Mondulkiri province depends on the study, if the company finds that the good work will lead to investment.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has allowed the Chinese company China Power to study the airport investment project in Mondulkiri. At that time, Mondulkiri Airport was planned to be built on an area of 300 hectares, about 20 kilometers from Sen Monorom, which is estimated to cost more than $ 80 million.
Due to the crisis of Kovid 19 and the global economic situation, China Power was in financial trouble, so the project was stalled. Only now, the Royal Government has found potential new investors to give Fukers the right to study the Mondulkiri Airport investment project.
