(Prey Veng): In early March 2024, Prey Veng Polytechnic Institute announced the recruitment of more than 400 young people from poor families and young people with disabilities in Prey Veng to enroll in the second phase of technical and vocational training. Free.
According to the institute, the provision of technical and vocational training for 420 trainees in the second phase includes skills in electrical installation in buildings, car maintenance and repair services, beauty services, home air conditioning, cooking. Khmer Vegetable and Fruit Processing, etc. Participants can study from Monday to Friday in two shifts, evening and morning.
Young people who can register to study this skill must be 15 years old or older, in which young people from poor and vulnerable families all over the country can study for free and receive a stipend of 280,000 Riels. Months until graduation. Upon completion of this course, participants will receive a Technical and Vocational Certificate from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and have the opportunity to continue their studies at the Institute.
Separately, young people aged 15 years and over with disability ID card, Health Equity Fund card will also be able to study for free, but no stipend, but participants will receive a technical and vocational degree from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational training and the opportunity to continue their studies at the same institute as young people from poor families.
Please note that this second technical and vocational training course will start on May 1, 2024. Since the Vocational and Technical Training Program opened on January 15, 2024, the first training course has been running smoothly across the country, but technical training institutes across the country are still accepting enrollment. Skills, which are the priority policy of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate.
