He said that from 1992 to 2023, under the skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia cleared 3,024 square kilometers of land mines and explosive remnants of war, including areas with cluster munitions. Despite the efforts and contributions of GICHD, Cambodia still has 533 square kilometers of mines and 1,321 square kilometers of explosive remnants of war, including cluster munitions, to be dealt with.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch continued that with the unwavering commitment of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the visionary Prime Minister of Cambodia is the foundation of progress and confidence in achieving the goal of Cambodia Mine Action 2025, as well as Minimize the threat of explosive remnants of war.
