Negotiators from Hamas, Qatar and Egypt, excluding Israel, are in Cairo, Egypt, to discuss finding a way out of a 40-day ceasefire in the war between Israel and Hamas, while Ramadan is the month of fasting. When the day of the Muslims will start early next week.
"Everything now depends on Hamas' decision, while Israel is cooperating ... but if the fighting continues," Biden told reporters on Tuesday. "Continue in Ramadan, it will be extremely dangerous."
A Hamas official, Osama Hamdan, also told reporters in Beirut, Lebanon, that the main condition of Hamas was that Israel must stop military operations, withdraw its troops from Gaza and allow Palestinians fleeing the war. Can return to their homes. According to the Hamas official, no prisoner swap will take place until a ceasefire is reached.
But Israel has also stated that it intends to suspend the war in exchange for the release of hostages, insisting it will not stop the war until Hamas is destroyed.
Minister of Health demonstrates the use of innovation in the provision of health services will make public services more efficient and effective to meet the needs of citizens
(Phnom Penh): Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, on March 5, 2024, continued to lead the training course on "Leadership and Innovation" for civil servants under the Ministry of Health through a video conference system with the participation of a total of 2,501 people to strengthen the institution, which is one of the three strategic priorities set by the Ministry of Health to support the reform of the Royal Government for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
This week's lessons provide practical knowledge and experience with examples of using innovation to improve public services, especially health services.
The Minister outlined the four phases of innovation, which include problem-solving, service design, implementation and follow-up evaluation. The use of innovation in the provision of health services will make public services more efficient and effective in response to the needs of the people, as well as provide them with a better experience after receiving services from public health institutions.
In addition to giving a lecture, the Minister also presented the topics selected for discussion at the forthcoming 43rd Health Conference, which include: (1) prevention and control of non-communicable diseases (2) Promoting maternal and child health and nutrition (3) prevention and control of infectious diseases, (4) providing primary health care services and (5) providing health care services in referral hospitals.
He urged all health officials to raise questions in order to gather input for consideration at the conference or for use in strengthening the health sector today as well as in the future.
ASEAN-Australia Special Summit officially kicks off
(Melbourne, Australia): The ASEAN-Australia Special Summit, held in Melbourne, Australia, officially opened this Wednesday morning, March 6, 2024.
The meeting was attended by leaders of ASEAN member states and the Prime Minister of Australia, as well as the Secretary-General of ASEAN.
The ASEAN-Australia Special Summit was held to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the ASEAN-Australia Dialogue Partnership. The meeting will provide an opportunity for leaders to set common future directions and deepen ties through the full and effective implementation of key priorities of the ASEAN-Australia Comprehensive Strategic Partnership.
Leaders plan to approve the Melbourne Declaration and the ASEAN-Australia Leaders' Vision Statement.
