Senior official of the National Authority for Combating Drugs: Inter-religious Sihanoukville, a priority target group, can send an education message on drugs to the community
(Sihanoukville): Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot, director of the Department of Education and Public Relations of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that inter-religious Sihanoukville is a priority target group to send an educational message on drugs to the community.
This statement was made by Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot at the closing ceremony of the seminar on the promotion of education on the effects of drug use and the law on drug control in Sihanoukville on the evening of the 5th. March 2024.
Mr. Oung Yohan, Chairman of the Council of Cambodian Church Network, thanked for the good cooperation between the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Sihanoukville Provincial Authority and the religious sector to provide opportunities for the religious sector to participate in social work, especially media. True from the drug problem to its followers.
