(Melbourne, Australia): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and Indonesian President Joko Widodo have expressed satisfaction over the good relations between Cambodia and Indonesia and pledged to improve relations and cooperation.
During a working meeting on the afternoon of March 5, 2024 in Melbourne, Australia, President Hun Manet congratulated President Joko Widodo on the success of the 43rd ASEAN Summit 2023 as well as the election. Presidential election on February 14, 2024.
During the meeting, President Hun Manet and the President of Indonesia discussed key areas that are subject to the strengthening and expansion of further cooperation and mutual benefit between Cambodia and Indonesia, including diplomacy, economy and trade, tourism and tourism. Security.
On the occasion of the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, the President and Mr. Joko Widodo expressed their gratitude for the excellent relations between the two countries over the past seven decades, bearing much fruit. High-level communication, economic relations, people-to-people contacts, especially the strengthening of relations in the fields of security and defense.
In this meeting, Samdech Hun Sen and the President of Indonesia agreed to continue to strengthen and expand cooperation in the field, as well as to further enhance cooperation in other fields in order to further strengthen the cooperation between the two countries. He thanked for the invitation to pay an official visit to Indonesia at any convenient time.
