(Banteay Meanchey): On March 4, 2024, Poipet City Gendarmerie arrested a 35-year-old suspect named Chea Chak in Kilometer 4 Village, Sangkat Phsar Kandal in connection with a case of intentional aggravated violence and use. Illegal possession of drugs.
Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Municipal Gendarmerie Base, said that at 20:30 on March 3, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Base received information from residents that at the scene. In the case of cutting with an ax, causing serious injuries, the local police force immediately arrived and arrested the suspect, including removing the ax and stick and brought to the municipal police base for questioning.
Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro confirmed that the suspect, after being detained by the police, had a urine test and found drugs. The suspect confessed that he had used an ax to cut the victim because he and the victim had been angry with each other for the past two months.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro added that the victim, Saroeun Sen, 34, was taken by his family to the Cambodia-Japan Friendship Hospital in Mongkol Borei.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime investigation and crackdown, said that the crackdown was authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie. Method from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits were sent by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Office to the Provincial Court on Tuesday afternoon, March 5, 2024 to follow the procedure.
Pursat Provincial Governor Chairs an Emergency Meeting to Continue Monitoring, Preventing and Suppressing Natural Resource Crimes in Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh Districts
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Joint Steering Committee, on the afternoon of March 5, 2024, chaired an emergency meeting with the Provincial Commission and the nine sub-committees to continue monitoring. Prevent and suppress natural resource crimes in Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh districts of Pursat province.
The meeting was held at the first floor of the Provincial Administration Building with the participation of the chairperson, vice chairperson and members of the nine sub-committees and the secretariat under the provincial commission to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes. In Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh districts.
He requested the 9 sub-groups to inspect the old locations that were confiscated and stored in the past, as well as to map and make specific reports to examine the new cases of logging by targeting and arresting the perpetrators. Absolutely to take action according to the procedure. In addition, be prepared to stand and replant seedlings, which is the work of the Forestry Administration and the Department of Environment.
Senior official of the Ministry of Commerce urges enterprises and companies to strengthen productivity, quality and quantity to maintain export sustainability despite the loss of favor (Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce Producing products for export needs to strengthen production capacity to maintain exports, although Cambodia may lose some of its advantages.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat made the remarks at a press conference on "Official Launch of the Public Telephone System of the Ministry of Commerce" held on March 4, 2024.
Mr. Pen Sovichet said, "Of course we have lost some tax breaks, but Cambodia also has some conditions that need to be prepared." The enterprise must focus on increasing capacity, increasing its capabilities, how to expand and strengthen its production.
He stated that he has always focused on the confidence of enterprises and companies in increasing their capacity and ability to join the Royal Government, so in order for all companies to strengthen themselves, three key points have to be implemented, including:
* Increasing production productivity. For example, if they can produce 10 lots in one hour, Cambodia must produce the same 10 lots in order to be competitive.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat added that while all companies strengthen themselves on these three points and need to increase skills on capacity, sharing knowledge and skills to their employees or workers so that they can increase their capacity.
"We have gone from being a least developed country and having been favored to become a developing country that has lost some of its favors and requires us to increase our production or improve our production techniques," he said. "Responding to market demand is essential."
The Department of Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime Celebrates the 113th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women and Girls in the Digital Revolution"
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday afternoon, March 5, 2024, Lt. Gen. Thou Saroeun, Director of the Department of Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Crime, and she presided over the celebration of the 113th Anniversary of International Women's Day, March 8, 2024 under the theme "Women and girls in the digital revolution."
During the meeting, Lt. Gen. Thou Saroeun emphasized that women have made significant contributions to the current context in order to continue to promote the invaluable value of women in peacekeeping as well as active participation in peacekeeping. Accelerating development in all areas, especially in this digital age.
At the same time, the General Director of the Department also stressed that:
* Women are on an equal footing with men in society * Women can be more capable than men * Women can also participate in all national and international forums * Women are the driving force behind men's success in fulfilling their roles.
Lt. Gen. Thou Saroeun brought a message of greetings from General Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, and thanked all the members for their participation and provided 50,000 Riels per person. Participate in all social activities aimed at promoting morality, women's values, Cambodian family values and better development
(Kampot): Dr. Governor of Kampot Province, Mao Thunin, requested and encouraged all women to continue to participate in all social activities in order to make a significant contribution to the promotion of social morality, women's values, Khmer family values and development as a society. Without the participation of women, society will not be able to function smoothly.
